/* 生物 (Biology) 内置笔记数据：由 index.html 加载。改了这个文件，记得把 index.html 里 bio.js?v= 的版本号也改一下，浏览器才会重新下载。 */
const PPTS_BIO={"bio|T4-1":[["Biology and Its Branches","生物学及其分支",[["Biology is the study of living things (organisms) and their interactions with the environment.","生物学：研究生物及其与环境的相互作用"],["Main fields: Botany (plants), Zoology (animals), Microbiology (bacteria, viruses, fungi), Genetics (inheritance and variation), Ecology (organisms and their environment).","主要领域：植物学、动物学、微生物学、遗传学、生态学"],["More fields: Anatomy (structure of the body), Physiology (functions of body systems), Cell biology (structure and function of cells), Taxonomy (classification), Biochemistry (chemical processes in organisms).","其他：解剖学、生理学、细胞生物学、分类学、生物化学"],["Biotechnology uses living organisms or biological processes to make useful products, e.g. insulin from bacteria, genetically modified crops, biofuel, yoghurt.","生物技术：利用生物或生物过程生产有用产品"],["Biology is linked to other fields: chemistry (biochemistry), physics (biophysics), mathematics (biostatistics), and computing (bioinformatics).","生物学与化学、物理、数学、信息科学相互关联"]],"","Tip: in MCQ, match the field to the thing being studied (e.g. mushrooms → mycology/microbiology; inheritance → genetics)."],["Careers in Biology and Technology","生物学相关职业与科技",[["Careers: doctor, nurse, pharmacist, dietitian, veterinarian, agriculturist, forester, biotechnologist, geneticist, marine biologist, conservationist, forensic scientist, laboratory technician, researcher, science teacher.","职业：医生、护士、药剂师、营养师、兽医、农艺师、林业员、生物技术员、遗传学家、海洋生物学家、法医、实验室技术员、研究员、科学教师"],["Medicine: vaccines, antibiotics, gene therapy, stem cell therapy and medical imaging improve health care.","医学：疫苗、抗生素、基因治疗、干细胞疗法"],["Agriculture and food: hybrid and genetically modified crops, tissue culture, biofertilisers and biopesticides increase food production.","农业与食品：杂交与转基因作物、组织培养、生物肥料与生物农药"],["Environment: bioremediation, waste treatment, conservation of biodiversity and renewable energy such as biofuel.","环境：生物修复、废物处理、保护生物多样性、生物燃料"],["Industrial Revolution 4.0 technologies (artificial intelligence, big data, robotics, genetic engineering, 3D bioprinting) speed up biological research.","工业4.0技术（人工智能、大数据、机器人、基因工程、3D生物打印）加快生物研究"]],"","Tip: when asked for a contribution of biology, give a field + a specific example (e.g. medicine → insulin for diabetics)."],["Laboratory Safety: Equipment and Functions","实验室安全：装备与作用",[["Laboratory coat/apron: protects clothes and skin from chemicals and microorganisms.","实验袍/围裙：保护衣服与皮肤"],["Safety goggles: protect the eyes from splashes of chemicals and flying particles. Gloves: protect hands from chemicals, hot objects and pathogens. Face mask: prevents inhaling fumes, spores or microorganisms.","护目镜护眼；手套护手；口罩防吸入烟雾、孢子、微生物"],["Fire extinguisher and fire blanket: put out small fires. Eye wash station: rinse chemicals out of the eyes. First aid kit: treats minor injuries. Fume cupboard: removes toxic or harmful fumes.","灭火器和防火毯灭火；洗眼器冲洗眼睛；急救箱；通风橱排出有毒气体"],["Closed shoes protect the feet from spills and broken glass. Long hair must be tied back.","穿包鞋；长发要束起"],["Know the location of the emergency exit, fire extinguisher, eye wash and first aid kit before starting work.","进入实验室先熟悉出口、灭火器、洗眼器、急救箱的位置"]],"","Tip: always pair an equipment with its function — 'goggles to protect the eyes from chemical splashes'."],["Hazard Symbols and Laboratory Rules","危险标志与实验室规则",[["Common hazard symbols: biohazard (infectious microorganisms), toxic/poisonous, corrosive (burns skin), flammable, oxidising, irritant/harmful, radioactive.","常见危险标志：生物危害、有毒、腐蚀性、易燃、氧化性、刺激/有害、放射性"],["Rules: do not eat, drink or run in the laboratory; wear protective equipment; read labels before using any chemical; never taste chemicals; smell by wafting.","规则：不饮食、不奔跑；穿戴防护装备；使用前看标签；不尝化学品；用手扇闻气味"],["Do not carry out unauthorised experiments; report any accident or breakage to the teacher immediately; wash hands with soap after the experiment.","不进行未经许可的实验；意外立即报告老师；实验后用肥皂洗手"],["Handle sharp tools (scalpel, razor blade) carefully, cutting away from the body; heat a test tube at an angle, pointing away from people.","小心使用手术刀、刀片；加热试管时倾斜且管口远离人"],["First aid: chemical on the skin → rinse with plenty of running water; chemical in the eyes → rinse at the eye wash station and inform the teacher.","急救：化学品沾皮肤用大量清水冲洗；入眼用洗眼器冲洗并通知老师"]],"","Tip: write the rule AND the reason, e.g. 'Do not eat in the laboratory to prevent swallowing harmful chemicals or microorganisms'."],["Waste Disposal and Hygiene","废物处理与卫生",[["Biological waste (specimens, cultures, used agar plates) is placed in a biohazard bag/container and sterilised (autoclave) or disinfected before disposal.","生物废物放入生物危害袋/容器，经高压灭菌或消毒后处理"],["Sharp objects (needles, blades) go into a puncture-proof sharps container; broken glass into a glass waste bin.","尖锐物放入防刺容器；碎玻璃放入玻璃废物箱"],["Chemical waste is poured into labelled waste bottles. Do not pour chemicals, microorganisms or solid waste into the sink.","化学废液倒入贴标签的废液瓶；不可倒入水槽"],["Disinfect the work surface with a disinfectant (e.g. 70% ethanol) before and after work; wash hands after handling microorganisms.","工作台前后用消毒剂（如70%乙醇）消毒；接触微生物后洗手"],["Dissected animals/plant parts are wrapped and disposed of as instructed — they must not be thrown into the ordinary dustbin.","解剖后的动植物材料要按指示包好处理"]],"","Tip: biological waste → sterilise first; sharps → sharps container; chemicals → labelled waste bottle."],["Communicating in Biology: Units and Magnification","生物学沟通：单位与放大倍数",[["Scientists communicate findings using tables, graphs, drawings, reports, posters, oral presentations, scientific journals and ICT.","科学家用表格、图表、绘图、报告、海报、口头报告、期刊和资讯科技分享发现"],["SI units: length — metre (m), millimetre (mm), micrometre (µm), nanometre (nm); mass — kilogram (kg), gram (g); time — second (s); temperature — °C or K; volume — cm³ or dm³.","国际单位：长度 m、mm、µm、nm；质量 kg、g；时间 s；温度 °C 或 K；体积 cm³、dm³"],["Conversions: 1 mm = 1000 µm; 1 µm = 1000 nm; 1 m = 1000 mm.","换算：1 mm = 1000 µm；1 µm = 1000 nm"],["Magnification = size of image ÷ actual size of specimen. Total magnification of a light microscope = eyepiece lens × objective lens (e.g. ×10 × ×40 = ×400).","放大倍数 = 图像大小 ÷ 实物大小；光学显微镜总放大倍数 = 目镜 × 物镜"],["Convert all measurements to the same unit before dividing. Magnification has no unit.","计算前先统一单位；放大倍数没有单位"]],"","Tip: write 'Magnification = image size ÷ actual size' first, then substitute with units converted."],["Biological Drawings, Tables and Graphs","生物绘图、表格与图表",[["Biological drawing: use a sharp pencil; clear, continuous single lines; no shading or colouring; draw large and in proportion; give a title and the magnification.","生物绘图：削尖铅笔；清晰连续单线；不涂影不着色；画得大且成比例；写标题与放大倍数"],["Label lines are straight, drawn with a ruler, do not cross one another and touch the structure; labels are written outside the drawing.","指示线用尺画直、不交叉、碰到结构；标注写在图外"],["Table: title; column headings with units; manipulated variable in the first column; consistent decimal places.","表格：有标题；列标题含单位；操纵变量放第一列；小数位一致"],["Graph: manipulated variable on the x-axis, responding variable on the y-axis; uniform scale; label both axes with units; plot points accurately; draw a smooth curve or best-fit line.","图表：操纵变量在x轴，反应变量在y轴；刻度均匀；标明单位；准确描点；画平滑曲线/最佳拟合线"],["Use a line graph for continuous data, a bar chart for categories, a pie chart for proportions, and a histogram for frequency of continuous data.","折线图用于连续数据，柱状图用于类别，饼图用于比例，直方图用于频率"]],"","Tip: most marks are lost for missing units, wrong axes, missing titles or labelling lines that cross."],["Scientific Investigation: Steps and Variables","科学探究：步骤与变量",[["Steps: identify the problem → make a hypothesis → identify variables → plan the experiment → carry out and collect data → analyse and interpret → make a conclusion → write a report.","步骤：提出问题→假设→确定变量→设计实验→进行并收集数据→分析→结论→报告"],["Hypothesis: a testable statement about the relationship between two variables, e.g. 'The higher the temperature, the higher the rate of enzyme activity.'","假设：说明两变量关系且可检验的陈述"],["Manipulated variable: what you change. Responding variable: what you measure. Fixed (constant) variables: what you keep the same to make it a fair test.","操纵变量：你改变的；反应变量：你测量的；固定变量：保持不变以确保公平"],["Operational definition: how the variable is measured, e.g. 'Rate of photosynthesis is measured by the number of bubbles released per minute.'","操作性定义：说明如何测量变量"],["Reliability: repeat the experiment at least 3 times and calculate the mean; use at least 5 values of the manipulated variable; the conclusion states whether the hypothesis is accepted or rejected.","可靠性：重复至少3次取平均；操纵变量至少5个数值；结论说明假设是否被接受"]],"","Tip: the problem statement is a question ('How does…affect…?'); the hypothesis is a statement."],["Worked Example: Planning an Investigation","例题：设计探究",[["Problem statement: How does light intensity affect the rate of photosynthesis in Hydrilla?","问题：光强度如何影响黑藻光合速率？"],["Hypothesis: The higher the light intensity, the higher the rate of photosynthesis (more bubbles released).","假设：光强越高，光合速率越高（气泡越多）"],["Variables — manipulated: distance of the lamp from Hydrilla (light intensity); responding: number of bubbles per minute; fixed: temperature, volume of water, concentration of sodium hydrogencarbonate, size of the Hydrilla.","变量：操纵＝灯与黑藻距离；反应＝每分钟气泡数；固定＝温度、水量、碳酸氢钠浓度、黑藻大小"],["Materials and apparatus: Hydrilla, beaker/boiling tube, funnel, lamp, ruler, stopwatch, sodium hydrogencarbonate solution, thermometer.","材料与仪器：黑藻、烧杯/试管、漏斗、灯、尺、秒表、碳酸氢钠溶液、温度计"],["Procedure: place the lamp 10 cm away, wait 2 minutes, count bubbles for 3 minutes; repeat at 20, 30, 40, 50 cm; repeat each distance 3 times; tabulate the results and plot a graph.","步骤：灯距 10 cm，等2分钟，数3分钟气泡；再测20、30、40、50 cm；每距离重复3次；列表绘图"]],"","Tip: always state how the manipulated variable is changed and how the responding variable is measured."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Hypothesis (Hipotesis); Variable (Pemboleh ubah); Manipulated variable (Pemboleh ubah dimanipulasi)","假设；变量；操纵变量"],["Responding variable (Pemboleh ubah bergerak balas); Fixed variable (Pemboleh ubah dimalarkan)","反应变量；固定变量"],["Magnification (Pembesaran); Biohazard (Bahaya biologi); Disinfectant (Pembasmi kuman)","放大倍数；生物危害；消毒剂"],["Fume cupboard (Kebuk wasap); Eye wash (Pencuci mata); Laboratory rules (Peraturan makmal)","通风橱；洗眼器；实验室规则"]],"","Tip: SPM questions can be answered in English or Bahasa Melayu — know both."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Confusing the manipulated variable (changed) with the responding variable (measured).","混淆操纵变量与反应变量"],["Writing the hypothesis as a question or without a relationship between the variables.","假设写成问句或没有关系"],["Drawings with shading, arrows instead of label lines, no title or magnification.","绘图涂影、用箭头、缺标题或放大倍数"],["Table headings without units; responding variable plotted on the x-axis; axes not labelled.","表格标题无单位；反应变量画在x轴；坐标轴无标注"],["Forgetting to say 'repeat and calculate the mean' and 'keep fixed variables constant' in a planning question.","设计题忘记写“重复取平均”和“控制固定变量”"]],"","Tip: use the sequence Problem → Hypothesis → Variables → Apparatus → Procedure → Table → Conclusion."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: State the function of safety goggles. J: To protect the eyes from chemical splashes and flying particles.","问：护目镜作用？答：保护眼睛免受化学品溅射和飞溅物伤害"],["S: A drawing of a cell is 6 cm long. The actual cell is 60 µm. Find the magnification. J: 6 cm = 60 000 µm; magnification = 60 000 ÷ 60 = ×1000.","问：图长6 cm，实物60 µm，放大倍数？答：6 cm＝60000 µm，÷60＝×1000"],["S: What is the manipulated variable in an experiment on temperature and enzyme activity? J: Temperature.","问：温度与酶活性实验的操纵变量？答：温度"],["S: Why must an experiment be repeated? J: To increase reliability by calculating the mean and reducing errors.","问：为何要重复实验？答：取平均、减少误差、提高可靠性"],["S: How should used agar plates be disposed of? J: Place in a biohazard container and sterilise (autoclave) before disposal.","问：用过的琼脂平板如何处理？答：放入生物危害容器并高压灭菌后处理"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-2":[["Cell Theory and Microscopes","细胞学说与显微镜",[["Cell theory: (1) all living things are made of one or more cells; (2) the cell is the basic unit of structure and function; (3) all cells arise from pre-existing cells.","细胞学说：生物由细胞构成；细胞是结构与功能基本单位；细胞来自已有细胞"],["Robert Hooke first observed and named 'cells' in cork (1665). Schleiden, Schwann and Virchow developed the cell theory.","胡克1665年观察软木并命名“细胞”；施莱登、施旺、菲尔肖建立细胞学说"],["Light microscope: uses visible light and glass lenses; can observe living cells; magnification up to about ×1500; resolution about 0.2 µm.","光学显微镜：用可见光；可观察活细胞；放大约至×1500"],["Electron microscope: uses a beam of electrons; much higher magnification and resolution (reveals organelle details); specimens are dead and in a vacuum. TEM shows internal structure; SEM shows surface 3D.","电子显微镜：用电子束；放大与分辨率极高；标本是死的；TEM看内部，SEM看表面立体"],["Total magnification = eyepiece × objective. Resolution is the ability to distinguish two close points as separate.","总放大倍数＝目镜×物镜；分辨率＝区分两个靠近点的能力"]],"","Tip: light microscope → living, low resolution; electron microscope → dead, high resolution."],["Animal Cell: Organelles and Functions (1)","动物细胞：细胞器与功能（1）",[["Plasma membrane: selectively permeable; controls the movement of substances in and out of the cell.","质膜：选择透性；控制物质进出"],["Nucleus: contains DNA (chromatin); controls cell activities and heredity. Nucleolus: makes ribosomal RNA and ribosomes. Nuclear envelope has nuclear pores.","细胞核：含DNA，控制细胞活动与遗传；核仁合成rRNA与核糖体；核膜有核孔"],["Cytoplasm: jelly-like fluid where metabolic reactions occur and organelles are suspended.","细胞质：代谢反应场所，悬浮细胞器"],["Mitochondrion: double membrane; site of aerobic respiration to release energy (ATP). Cells needing much energy (muscle, sperm) have many mitochondria.","线粒体：双层膜；有氧呼吸场所，释放能量(ATP)；耗能多的细胞含量多"],["Ribosome: no membrane; made of rRNA and protein; site of protein synthesis. Free ribosomes make proteins for use in the cell; ribosomes on the rough ER make proteins for export.","核糖体：无膜；合成蛋白质；游离核糖体供细胞用，粗面内质网上的供输出"]],"","Tip: say mitochondria 'release energy' or 'produce ATP' — they do not 'create' energy."],["Animal Cell: Organelles and Functions (2)","动物细胞：细胞器与功能（2）",[["Rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER): ribosomes on its surface; transports proteins synthesised by the ribosomes. Abundant in cells that secrete proteins (e.g. enzyme-secreting pancreatic cells).","粗面内质网：有核糖体；运输合成的蛋白质；分泌蛋白细胞中丰富"],["Smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER): no ribosomes; synthesises lipids, steroids and detoxifies drugs/poisons (abundant in liver cells).","滑面内质网：无核糖体；合成脂质、类固醇，解毒（肝细胞多）"],["Golgi apparatus: modifies, sorts, packages proteins into vesicles for secretion; forms lysosomes.","高尔基体：修饰、分类、包装蛋白质成囊泡；形成溶酶体"],["Lysosome: contains hydrolytic enzymes that digest worn-out organelles, bacteria and food particles.","溶酶体：含水解酶，消化衰老细胞器、细菌、食物颗粒"],["Centrioles: form the spindle fibres during cell division (in animal cells).","中心粒：细胞分裂时形成纺锤丝（动物细胞）"]],"","Tip: RER → proteins for export; SER → lipids/steroids/detoxification."],["Plant Cell and Comparison with Animal Cell","植物细胞及与动物细胞比较",[["Cell wall: made of cellulose; gives support and protection and maintains the shape; fully permeable.","细胞壁：纤维素；支持与保护；全透性"],["Chloroplast: double membrane; contains chlorophyll; site of photosynthesis. Large central vacuole: contains cell sap; maintains turgidity and stores substances.","叶绿体：双膜，含叶绿素，光合作用场所；大中央液泡含细胞液，维持膨压、储存物质"],["Plant cell: fixed regular shape; cell wall, chloroplast and large permanent vacuole present; stores starch; centrioles absent (in higher plants).","植物细胞：形状固定；有细胞壁、叶绿体、大液泡；储存淀粉；高等植物无中心粒"],["Animal cell: irregular shape; no cell wall or chloroplast; small temporary vacuoles; stores glycogen; centrioles present.","动物细胞：形状不规则；无细胞壁与叶绿体；小而暂时的液泡；储存糖原；有中心粒"],["Both have: plasma membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, mitochondria, ribosomes, ER and Golgi apparatus.","共有：质膜、细胞核、细胞质、线粒体、核糖体、内质网、高尔基体"]],"","Tip: the cell wall is fully permeable; the plasma membrane is selectively permeable."],["Organelles Working Together: Secretory Protein","细胞器协作：分泌蛋白",[["1. The nucleus holds the DNA; a gene is transcribed into messenger RNA (mRNA), which leaves through a nuclear pore.","1. 细胞核中基因转录成mRNA，经核孔离开"],["2. Ribosomes on the RER translate the mRNA and synthesise the protein (e.g. an enzyme).","2. 粗面内质网上的核糖体翻译mRNA合成蛋白质"],["3. The protein enters the RER and is transported in a transport vesicle to the Golgi apparatus.","3. 蛋白质进入内质网，以运输囊泡送至高尔基体"],["4. The Golgi apparatus modifies and packages the protein into a secretory vesicle.","4. 高尔基体修饰并包装成分泌囊泡"],["5. The secretory vesicle fuses with the plasma membrane and releases the protein out of the cell (exocytosis). Mitochondria supply ATP for the process.","5. 分泌囊泡与质膜融合，胞吐排出；线粒体提供ATP"]],"","Tip: sequence for SPM: nucleus → ribosome/RER → transport vesicle → Golgi → secretory vesicle → plasma membrane."],["Unicellular Organisms: Amoeba and Paramecium","单细胞生物：变形虫与草履虫",[["Unicellular organisms carry out all life processes within one cell: nutrition, respiration, excretion, movement, response, reproduction.","单细胞生物在一个细胞内完成所有生命过程"],["Amoeba sp.: moves by pseudopodia; feeds by phagocytosis (engulfs food into a food vacuole); contractile vacuole removes excess water; reproduces by binary fission.","变形虫：伪足移动；吞噬作用摄食，形成食物泡；伸缩泡排出多余水；二分裂"],["Paramecium sp.: moves by cilia; food swept into the oral groove → food vacuole; contractile vacuoles expel excess water; reproduces by binary fission (and conjugation).","草履虫：纤毛移动；食物经口沟形成食物泡；伸缩泡排水；二分裂（亦有接合生殖）"],["Gaseous exchange: oxygen and carbon dioxide diffuse across the plasma membrane because the surface area to volume ratio is large.","气体交换：O₂、CO₂经质膜扩散，因表面积/体积比大"],["Freshwater protozoa live in hypotonic surroundings; water enters by osmosis and is pumped out by the contractile vacuole.","淡水原生生物处于低渗环境，水渗入后由伸缩泡排出"]],"","Tip: contractile vacuole = osmoregulation, not excretion of waste."],["Unicellular Organisms: Euglena and Yeast","单细胞生物：眼虫与酵母",[["Euglena sp.: has chloroplasts → photosynthesises in light (autotrophic) but can feed on organic matter in the dark; moves with a flagellum; the eyespot detects light.","眼虫：有叶绿体可光合；暗处可异养；鞭毛移动；眼点感光"],["Chlamydomonas sp.: green unicellular alga; two flagella; chloroplast with pyrenoid; reproduces asexually by mitosis/zoospores and sexually.","衣藻：绿色单细胞藻；2条鞭毛；叶绿体含蛋白核"],["Yeast (Saccharomyces) is a unicellular fungus; reproduces asexually by budding; carries out fermentation when oxygen is limited.","酵母：单细胞真菌；出芽生殖；缺氧时发酵"],["Adaptations: large surface area to volume ratio for quick diffusion; contractile vacuoles; locomotor structures (cilia, flagella, pseudopodia); eyespot in Euglena.","适应：高表面积/体积比；伸缩泡；运动结构；眼点"],["Benefit of being unicellular: short diffusion distance, so no transport system is needed.","单细胞好处：扩散距离短，不需要运输系统"]],"","Tip: Euglena is both photosynthetic and able to move — a favourite exam example."],["Multicellular Organisms: Cell Differentiation","多细胞生物：细胞分化",[["Cell differentiation: unspecialised cells become specialised in structure for specific functions. Specialised cells group into tissues, organs and systems.","细胞分化：未特化细胞形成特定结构以执行特定功能"],["Stem cells are unspecialised cells that can divide continuously and differentiate into other cell types. Sources: embryo, bone marrow, umbilical cord blood; also induced pluripotent stem cells.","干细胞：未特化、可持续分裂并分化；来源：胚胎、骨髓、脐带血"],["Uses of stem cells: treating leukaemia, repairing damaged tissues, burns, spinal cord injury research. Ethical issue: use of human embryos.","干细胞用途：治疗白血病、修复组织、烧伤；伦理争议：使用胚胎"],["Differentiation is controlled by which genes are switched on or off; all body cells contain the same genes.","分化由基因开启/关闭决定；所有体细胞含相同基因"],["Advantage of multicellularity: division of labour; organisms can grow larger and become more complex.","多细胞优点：分工合作，可长得更大更复杂"]],"","Tip: all specialised cells in an organism have the same genes but express different ones."],["Specialised Animal Cells","特化动物细胞",[["Red blood cell: biconcave disc → large surface area; no nucleus → more space for haemoglobin that carries oxygen.","红细胞：双凹圆盘增大表面积；无核容纳更多血红蛋白运氧"],["White blood cell: can change shape and engulf pathogens (phagocytosis) or produce antibodies.","白细胞：可变形吞噬病原体或产生抗体"],["Neurone: long axon transmits impulses over long distances; dendrites receive impulses; myelin sheath speeds transmission.","神经元：长轴突传导冲动；树突接收；髓鞘加速传导"],["Sperm cell: flagellum for swimming; acrosome with enzymes to penetrate the egg; many mitochondria supply energy. Egg cell: large with food reserve and a jelly coat.","精子：鞭毛游动；顶体酶穿入卵；大量线粒体；卵细胞：大、含养料、有胶质层"],["Muscle cell: elongated with many mitochondria; contractile proteins (actin and myosin) cause contraction.","肌细胞：细长，多线粒体，肌动蛋白与肌球蛋白收缩"]],"","Tip: give structure + how it helps the function (e.g. 'biconcave shape increases surface area for oxygen diffusion')."],["Specialised Plant Cells","特化植物细胞",[["Root hair cell: long projection increases the surface area for absorbing water and mineral salts; thin wall; large vacuole with a high solute concentration.","根毛细胞：突起增大吸收面积；壁薄；大液泡溶质浓度高"],["Palisade mesophyll cell: many chloroplasts; elongated and closely packed at the top of the leaf to absorb maximum light.","栅栏细胞：叶绿体多；排列紧密，充分吸光"],["Guard cell: kidney-shaped with chloroplasts; changes turgidity to open or close the stoma, controlling gas exchange and water loss.","保卫细胞：肾形含叶绿体；膨压变化开关气孔"],["Xylem vessel: dead, hollow cells with lignified walls; transports water and gives support. Phloem sieve tube: living cells with sieve plates; transport food, with companion cells.","导管：死细胞，空心，木质素加厚；运水并支持；筛管：活细胞，有筛板，伴细胞协助"]],"","Tip: xylem is dead and hollow; phloem sieve tubes are living."],["Levels of Organisation","组织层次",[["Sequence: cell → tissue → organ → system → organism.","顺序：细胞→组织→器官→系统→生物体"],["Animal tissues: epithelial, connective, muscular, nervous. Plant tissues: epidermal, ground (mesophyll), vascular (xylem, phloem).","动物组织：上皮、结缔、肌肉、神经；植物组织：表皮、基本、维管"],["Example (human): cardiac muscle cell → cardiac muscle tissue → heart → circulatory system → human.","例（人）：心肌细胞→心肌组织→心脏→循环系统→人"],["Example (plant): palisade mesophyll cell → palisade tissue → leaf → shoot system → plant.","例（植物）：栅栏细胞→栅栏组织→叶→茎叶系统→植物"],["An organ is made of different tissues working together (the stomach has epithelial, muscular, connective and nervous tissue).","器官由不同组织合作构成（如胃）；系统由多个器官构成"]],"","Tip: write the levels in order and give one example in each level."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Organelle (Organel); Cytoplasm (Sitoplasma); Nucleus (Nukleus); Mitochondrion (Mitokondrion)","细胞器；细胞质；细胞核；线粒体"],["Chloroplast (Kloroplas); Vacuole (Vakuol); Cell wall (Dinding sel); Plasma membrane (Membran plasma)","叶绿体；液泡；细胞壁；质膜"],["Golgi apparatus (Radas Golgi); Endoplasmic reticulum (Retikulum endoplasma); Lysosome (Lisosom)","高尔基体；内质网；溶酶体"],["Tissue (Tisu); Organ (Organ); System (Sistem); Differentiation (Pembezaan); Stem cell (Sel stem)","组织；器官；系统；分化；干细胞"],["Binary fission (Pembelahan dedua); Contractile vacuole (Vakuol berdenyut)","二分裂；伸缩泡"]],"","Tip: learn the Malay terms — the SPM paper is bilingual."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Writing 'mitochondria produce energy' — use 'release energy (ATP) through respiration'.","不要写“线粒体制造能量”，应为“通过呼吸释放能量(ATP)”"],["Saying the cell wall is selectively permeable — it is fully permeable; the plasma membrane is selectively permeable.","细胞壁是全透性，质膜才是选择透性"],["Forgetting that ribosomes have no membrane; mitochondria and chloroplasts have double membranes.","核糖体无膜；线粒体与叶绿体是双层膜"],["Describing the cell in general terms only — link a feature to a function (many mitochondria → much energy).","不要只写笼统，要把结构和功能联系起来"],["Confusing tissue and organ: a tissue is a group of similar cells; an organ is a group of different tissues.","混淆组织与器官"]],"","Tip: for 'compare plant and animal cell' questions, give similarities and differences in a table."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Which organelle releases energy through aerobic respiration? J: Mitochondrion.","问：哪种细胞器通过有氧呼吸释放能量？答：线粒体"],["S: Why do pancreatic cells have much RER and Golgi apparatus? J: They synthesise and secrete many enzymes (proteins); RER makes/transports them and the Golgi modifies and packages them.","问：胰脏细胞为何多粗面内质网和高尔基体？答：合成分泌大量酶，内质网合成运输，高尔基体修饰包装"],["S: State two structures present in plant cells but absent in animal cells. J: Cell wall and chloroplast (also large permanent vacuole).","问：植物特有的两结构？答：细胞壁、叶绿体（还有大液泡）"],["S: What is the function of the contractile vacuole in Amoeba? J: To expel excess water that enters by osmosis (osmoregulation).","问：变形虫伸缩泡作用？答：排出渗入的多余水分（渗透调节）"],["S: Arrange the levels of organisation. J: Cell → tissue → organ → system → organism.","问：组织层次顺序？答：细胞→组织→器官→系统→生物体"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-3":[["Structure of the Plasma Membrane","质膜结构",[["Fluid mosaic model (Singer and Nicolson, 1972): the membrane is a fluid phospholipid bilayer with proteins scattered like a mosaic.","流动镶嵌模型：磷脂双层可流动，蛋白质镶嵌其中"],["Phospholipid: hydrophilic (water-loving) phosphate head faces the watery outside/inside; hydrophobic (water-hating) fatty acid tails face inward.","磷脂：亲水头朝向水环境；疏水尾朝内"],["Proteins: channel and carrier proteins transport substances; receptor proteins bind hormones; enzymes; glycoproteins/glycolipids for cell recognition. Cholesterol stabilises the membrane.","蛋白质：通道/载体蛋白运输；受体蛋白；酶；糖蛋白识别；胆固醇稳定膜"],["Selectively permeable: small and non-polar molecules (O₂, CO₂, lipids) pass through the bilayer; large or charged molecules and ions need proteins; very large molecules cannot pass.","选择透性：小分子、非极性物质可穿过；大分子或带电离子需蛋白质"],["The membrane is about 7–10 nm thick and can only be seen with an electron microscope.","质膜厚约7–10 nm，需电子显微镜观察"]],"","Tip: draw the bilayer with heads outside and tails inside, and label proteins, glycoprotein and cholesterol."],["Passive and Active Transport: Concepts","被动与主动运输：概念",[["Passive transport: movement down a concentration gradient (high → low); needs no energy (ATP). It includes simple diffusion, osmosis and facilitated diffusion.","被动运输：顺浓度梯度；不耗ATP；包括简单扩散、渗透、协助扩散"],["Simple diffusion: net movement of molecules from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration, e.g. O₂ into cells, CO₂ out of cells.","简单扩散：分子从高浓度到低浓度的净移动"],["Osmosis: net movement of water molecules from a hypotonic solution (lower solute concentration) to a hypertonic solution (higher solute concentration) across a selectively permeable membrane.","渗透：水分子经选择透性膜从低渗溶液(溶质少)向高渗溶液(溶质多)的净移动"],["Facilitated diffusion: ions, glucose and amino acids move down the concentration gradient through channel or carrier proteins; no ATP.","协助扩散：离子、葡萄糖等经通道/载体蛋白顺梯度运输，不耗ATP"],["Active transport: movement against the concentration gradient (low → high) using carrier proteins and energy (ATP), e.g. absorption of glucose by intestinal cells, mineral ions by root hair cells, Na⁺–K⁺ pump.","主动运输：逆浓度梯度；需载体蛋白与ATP；如小肠吸收葡萄糖、根毛吸收矿物质"]],"","Tip: diffusion = particles; osmosis = water only, across a membrane."],["Factors Affecting Rate of Diffusion","影响扩散速率的因素",[["Concentration gradient: the steeper the gradient, the faster the diffusion.","浓度梯度越大，扩散越快"],["Temperature: higher temperature gives molecules more kinetic energy, so diffusion is faster.","温度越高，分子动能越大，扩散越快"],["Surface area to volume ratio: larger ratio → faster exchange (e.g. villi, alveoli, root hairs).","表面积/体积比越大，交换越快（绒毛、肺泡、根毛）"],["Distance: the shorter the diffusion distance (thin membranes), the faster the diffusion. Size of molecules: smaller molecules diffuse faster.","距离越短越快；分子越小越快"],["Active transport rate depends on the availability of ATP (oxygen and respiration) and the number of carrier proteins.","主动运输速率取决于ATP供应和载体蛋白数量"]],"","Tip: cyanide stops ATP production, so active transport stops — a classic exam link."],["Bulk Transport and Comparison of Transport Types","大量运输与运输方式比较",[["Endocytosis: the cell membrane engulfs large particles into vesicles (phagocytosis: solids; pinocytosis: liquids). Exocytosis: vesicles fuse with the membrane and release substances out (e.g. enzymes, hormones).","胞吞：质膜包裹大颗粒形成囊泡（吞噬/胞饮）；胞吐：囊泡与质膜融合排出物质"],["Simple diffusion: down the gradient, no carrier, no ATP. Facilitated diffusion: down the gradient, uses protein, no ATP.","简单扩散：无载体；协助扩散：用蛋白质；都不耗能"],["Active transport: against the gradient, uses carrier protein and ATP. Osmosis: movement of water only.","主动运输：逆梯度，需载体与ATP；渗透：仅水"],["Bulk transport needs energy (ATP) and a membrane that can form vesicles. (Extension: may be covered as additional content in some textbooks.)","大量运输耗能；（拓展内容，部分课本涉及）"]],"","Tip: create a table: direction of movement, protein needed, ATP needed, example."],["Osmosis in Animal and Plant Cells","动植物细胞的渗透作用",[["Animal cell in a hypotonic solution: water enters → the cell swells and may burst (e.g. red blood cell haemolysis).","动物细胞置于低渗液：吸水膨胀甚至破裂（红细胞溶血）"],["Animal cell in a hypertonic solution: water leaves → the cell shrinks and the membrane becomes crinkled (crenation). In an isotonic solution: no net movement.","高渗液：失水皱缩（锯齿状）；等渗液：无净移动"],["Plant cell in a hypotonic solution: water enters the vacuole → turgid; the cell wall stops bursting; turgor pressure supports the plant.","植物细胞置于低渗液：吸水膨胀变胀满；细胞壁防止破裂；膨压支持植物"],["Plant cell in a hypertonic solution: water leaves → the vacuole shrinks, the plasma membrane pulls away from the cell wall = plasmolysis (the cell is flaccid).","高渗液：失水，质膜与细胞壁分离＝质壁分离"],["When a plasmolysed cell is placed in water, it regains turgor = deplasmolysis.","把质壁分离的细胞放入清水，恢复膨胀＝质壁分离复原"]],"","Tip: plasmolysis = the plasma membrane pulls away from the wall — not 'the wall shrinks'."],["Osmosis in Unicellular Organisms and Plants","单细胞生物与植物的渗透作用",[["Freshwater Amoeba/Paramecium: surroundings are hypotonic → water enters by osmosis → contractile vacuoles pump it out to prevent bursting.","淡水变形虫/草履虫：环境低渗，水渗入，伸缩泡排出防止胀破"],["Turgor pressure keeps herbaceous plants upright and keeps the guard cells turgid so stomata open.","膨压让草本植物挺直；保卫细胞膨胀使气孔张开"],["Wilting: when water loss exceeds uptake, cells lose turgor and the plant droops; it recovers when watered.","萎蔫：失水多于吸水，细胞失去膨压；浇水后恢复"],["Root hair cells absorb water by osmosis because the cell sap is hypertonic to the soil water; mineral salts are absorbed by active transport.","根毛细胞液比土壤水高渗，水经渗透吸收；矿物质经主动运输吸收"]],"","Tip: osmosis uptake of water + active transport of mineral ions in root hairs."],["Investigation: Concentration of Cell Sap","探究：细胞液浓度",[["Aim: to determine the concentration of the cell sap of a potato/sweet potato by osmosis.","目的：用渗透法测定薯类细胞液浓度"],["Method: cut equal-sized strips; weigh each; immerse in sucrose solutions of 0.0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8 M for 30 minutes; blot and re-weigh.","方法：切相同大小薯条称重；浸入0、0.2、0.4、0.6、0.8 M蔗糖液30分钟；吸干再称重"],["Percentage change in mass = (final mass − initial mass) ÷ initial mass × 100%.","质量变化% ＝（终质量−初质量）÷初质量×100%"],["Plot % change in mass (y) against sucrose concentration (x). The point where the curve cuts the x-axis (0% change) = concentration of the cell sap (isotonic).","画质量变化%对浓度的曲线；与x轴交点（变化0）＝细胞液浓度（等渗）"],["Strips gain mass in dilute solutions (hypotonic) and lose mass in concentrated solutions (hypertonic). Fixed variables: size of strips, volume of solution, time, temperature.","稀溶液中增重（低渗），浓溶液中失重（高渗）；固定变量：薯条大小、溶液体积、时间、温度"]],"","Tip: remember to blot the strips dry before weighing."],["Worked Example: Osmosis Calculation","例题：渗透计算",[["Q: A strip has initial mass 5.0 g and final mass 4.5 g in 0.6 M sucrose. Change = (4.5 − 5.0) ÷ 5.0 × 100 = −10%.","题：5.0 g→4.5 g，变化＝−10%"],["The negative value means water left the strip: 0.6 M sucrose is hypertonic to the cell sap.","负值表示失水：0.6 M蔗糖相对细胞液为高渗"],["Q: A strip gains 8% in distilled water. Explain. A: The cell sap is hypertonic to distilled water, so water enters the cells by osmosis and the cells become turgid.","题：蒸馏水中增重8%？答：细胞液相对蒸馏水高渗，水渗入使细胞膨胀"],["Q: A plant wilts after too much fertiliser is added. A: The soil solution becomes hypertonic to the root cell sap, so water leaves the roots by osmosis.","题：施肥过多植物萎蔫？答：土壤溶液高渗，根细胞失水"]],"","Tip: always compare the solute concentration of the two sides and state the direction of water movement."],["Applications in Daily Life","日常应用",[["Food preservation: salting fish, sugar in jam and pickles create a hypertonic environment; microorganisms lose water by osmosis and cannot grow.","食物保存：盐、糖造成高渗环境，微生物失水无法生长"],["Vegetables kept in water become crisp and turgid; vegetables sprinkled with salt become soft and limp.","蔬菜泡水挺脆；撒盐变软"],["Intravenous (saline) drips are isotonic (0.9% NaCl) so red blood cells do not swell or shrink.","生理盐水点滴为等渗(0.9% NaCl)，红细胞不胀不缩"],["Excess fertiliser or salt water damages crops; salt on slugs/leeches causes them to lose water.","过量肥料或盐水伤害作物；盐使蛞蝓失水"],["Kidney dialysis uses a partially permeable membrane for diffusion of waste (urea) out of the blood.","肾透析用半透膜使尿素扩散出血液"]],"","Tip: describe application as: hypertonic/hypotonic environment → direction of water → effect."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Diffusion (Resapan); Osmosis (Osmosis); Active transport (Pengangkutan aktif)","扩散；渗透；主动运输"],["Hypotonic (Hipotonik); Hypertonic (Hipertonik); Isotonic (Isotonik)","低渗；高渗；等渗"],["Plasmolysis (Plasmolisis); Turgid (Segah); Flaccid (Lembik); Turgor pressure (Tekanan turgor)","质壁分离；胀满；萎软；膨压"],["Selectively permeable membrane (Membran separa telap); Concentration gradient (Kecerunan kepekatan)","选择透性膜；浓度梯度"],["Facilitated diffusion (Resapan berbantu); Carrier protein (Protein pembawa)","协助扩散；载体蛋白"]],"","Tip: 'Resapan' = diffusion in KSSM Malay; 'Osmosis' stays the same."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying water moves from hypertonic to hypotonic. Correct: water moves from hypotonic (lower solute) to hypertonic (higher solute).","方向写反：水从低渗流向高渗"],["Confusing diffusion with osmosis; osmosis involves water and a selectively permeable membrane.","混淆扩散与渗透"],["Writing 'the cell wall shrinks' for plasmolysis; it is the protoplast/plasma membrane that pulls away.","质壁分离是质膜/原生质体脱离细胞壁"],["Forgetting that active transport needs ATP and carrier proteins and goes against the gradient.","忘记主动运输需ATP和载体、逆梯度"],["Graph questions: the isotonic point is where % change in mass = 0 (the curve crosses the x-axis).","图表题：等渗点＝质量变化0的位置"]],"","Tip: explain with the words 'solute concentration', 'net movement', 'selectively permeable membrane'."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: State the model of the plasma membrane. J: Fluid mosaic model.","问：质膜模型？答：流动镶嵌模型"],["S: Why does a red blood cell burst in distilled water? J: Distilled water is hypotonic; water enters by osmosis and the cell, without a cell wall, bursts.","问：红细胞放蒸馏水为何破裂？答：低渗，水渗入，无细胞壁而破裂"],["S: Give two differences between facilitated diffusion and active transport. J: Facilitated diffusion is down the gradient and needs no ATP; active transport is against the gradient and needs ATP.","问：协助扩散与主动运输差异？答：前者顺梯度不耗ATP；后者逆梯度耗ATP"],["S: Explain why salted fish does not spoil easily. J: Salt creates a hypertonic environment, so microorganisms lose water by osmosis and die or cannot grow.","问：咸鱼为何不易变质？答：盐造成高渗环境，微生物失水死亡或无法繁殖"],["S: What is plasmolysis? J: The plasma membrane pulls away from the cell wall when a plant cell loses water in a hypertonic solution.","问：质壁分离？答：植物细胞在高渗液中失水，质膜与细胞壁分离"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-4":[["Chemical Elements and Biomolecules","化学元素与生物分子",[["The main elements in living things: carbon (C), hydrogen (H), oxygen (O), nitrogen (N); also phosphorus (P), sulphur (S), calcium, iron, magnesium.","主要元素：C、H、O、N；还有P、S、Ca、Fe、Mg"],["Organic compounds (contain carbon): carbohydrates, proteins, lipids, nucleic acids. Inorganic: water and mineral salts.","有机物：糖类、蛋白质、脂质、核酸；无机物：水、矿物质"],["Large molecules (polymers) are built from small units (monomers) by condensation (water is released) and broken down by hydrolysis (water is added).","大分子由小单位通过缩合(失水)形成，经水解(加水)分解"],["Carbohydrates: C, H, O (ratio about 1:2:1). Lipids: C, H, O (less oxygen). Proteins: C, H, O, N (some S). Nucleic acids: C, H, O, N, P.","糖类C、H、O；脂质C、H、O（氧较少）；蛋白质C、H、O、N；核酸含P"]],"","Tip: remember the elements to identify the biomolecule: N → protein; P → nucleic acid."],["Water: Properties and Functions","水：性质与功能",[["Water is a polar molecule; hydrogen bonds form between water molecules.","水是极性分子，分子间形成氢键"],["Universal solvent: dissolves many substances; medium for chemical reactions; transports nutrients, hormones and wastes (blood plasma, xylem sap).","万能溶剂：溶解物质；反应介质；运输养分、激素、废物"],["High specific heat capacity: absorbs much heat with small temperature change → stable body and aquatic temperature.","高比热容：吸热温度变化小，稳定体温与水域温度"],["High latent heat of vaporisation: evaporation (sweating, transpiration) cools the organism.","高汽化潜热：蒸发(出汗、蒸腾)降温"],["Cohesion and adhesion: water columns in xylem; reactant in hydrolysis and photosynthesis; lubricant (tears, synovial fluid); maintains turgor and the shape of cells.","内聚与黏附：木质部水柱；水解与光合的反应物；润滑剂；维持膨压"]],"","Tip: write the property AND its biological importance."],["Carbohydrates: Types and Structure","糖类：种类与结构",[["Monosaccharides (C₆H₁₂O₆): glucose, fructose, galactose — sweet, soluble, reducing sugars.","单糖：葡萄糖、果糖、半乳糖，还原糖"],["Disaccharides: maltose = glucose + glucose; sucrose = glucose + fructose; lactose = glucose + galactose. Formed by condensation with a glycosidic bond (water released).","二糖：麦芽糖、蔗糖、乳糖；缩合形成糖苷键"],["Polysaccharides: starch (storage in plants), glycogen (storage in animal liver and muscle), cellulose (cell wall). They are polymers of glucose, insoluble and not sweet.","多糖：淀粉(植物储存)、糖原(动物储存)、纤维素(细胞壁)；不溶不甜"],["Reducing sugars: all monosaccharides, maltose, lactose. Non-reducing sugar: sucrose.","还原糖：单糖、麦芽糖、乳糖；非还原糖：蔗糖"],["Hydrolysis breaks a disaccharide or polysaccharide into monosaccharides (with water; enzymes or acid).","水解把二糖/多糖分解成单糖"]],"","Tip: sucrose is a non-reducing sugar — a favourite trick in food-test questions."],["Carbohydrates: Functions and Food Tests","糖类：功能与食物测试",[["Functions: main source of energy (about 17 kJ per gram); structural (cellulose in plant walls, chitin in insect exoskeleton and fungal walls); storage; glycoproteins in cell recognition.","功能：主要能量来源(约17 kJ/g)；结构(纤维素、几丁质)；储存；糖蛋白识别"],["Benedict's test (reducing sugar): add Benedict's solution and heat in a water bath. Blue → green → yellow → orange → brick-red precipitate (more reducing sugar = redder).","本尼迪克特试验：加热，蓝→绿→黄→橙→砖红沉淀"],["Non-reducing sugar (sucrose): Benedict's test is negative (stays blue). Boil with dilute hydrochloric acid, neutralise with sodium hydrogencarbonate, then test again → brick-red.","非还原糖：先呈阴性；与稀盐酸煮沸，用碳酸氢钠中和后再测→砖红"],["Iodine test (starch): add iodine solution; brown/yellow → blue-black.","碘试验(淀粉)：棕黄→蓝黑"],["Dietary fibre (cellulose) is not digested by humans but prevents constipation.","膳食纤维人体无法消化，但防便秘"]],"","Tip: Benedict's — HEAT is required; iodine — no heating."],["Proteins: Structure","蛋白质：结构",[["Proteins contain C, H, O, N (and sometimes S). The monomer is an amino acid.","蛋白质含C、H、O、N（有时S）；单体为氨基酸"],["Amino acid: amino group (–NH₂), carboxyl group (–COOH), a hydrogen atom and an R group attached to the central carbon. There are 20 types.","氨基酸：氨基、羧基、氢和R基连在中心碳；共20种"],["Peptide bond: formed between the carboxyl group of one amino acid and the amino group of another by condensation → dipeptide → polypeptide.","肽键：缩合形成，二肽→多肽"],["Essential amino acids cannot be made by the body and must come from food (e.g. lysine, tryptophan); non-essential amino acids can be made in the body.","必需氨基酸需从食物摄取；非必需氨基酸体内可合成"],["Levels: primary (sequence of amino acids); secondary (α-helix or β-pleated sheet); tertiary (3-D folding by R-group bonds); quaternary (more than one polypeptide, e.g. haemoglobin).","层次：一级(序列)；二级(α螺旋/β折叠)；三级(三维折叠)；四级(多条多肽，如血红蛋白)"]],"","Tip: sequence of amino acids decides the 3-D shape, and the shape decides the function."],["Proteins: Functions, Denaturation and Biuret Test","蛋白质：功能、变性与双缩脲试验",[["Functions: enzymes; hormones (insulin); antibodies; transport (haemoglobin, carrier proteins); structure (collagen, keratin); contraction (actin, myosin); growth and repair.","功能：酶、激素、抗体、运输、结构、收缩、生长与修复"],["Denaturation: heat, extreme pH, heavy metals or alcohol break the bonds that hold the 3-D shape; the protein loses its shape and function (e.g. cooking an egg).","变性：高温、极端pH、重金属破坏空间结构，失去功能"],["Biuret test: add sodium hydroxide, then a few drops of dilute copper(II) sulphate; blue → purple/violet indicates protein.","双缩脲试验：加NaOH再加稀CuSO₄，蓝→紫"],["Energy value of protein: about 17 kJ per gram (used for energy only when carbohydrates and fats are lacking).","蛋白质能量约17 kJ/g"],["Sources: meat, fish, eggs, milk, legumes. Deficiency: kwashiorkor.","来源：肉、鱼、蛋、奶、豆类；缺乏：夸休可尔症"]],"","Tip: denaturation is irreversible in most cases — do not confuse with the temporary inactivity at low temperature."],["Lipids","脂质",[["Triglyceride (fat/oil): 1 glycerol + 3 fatty acids joined by ester bonds (condensation).","三酸甘油酯：1甘油+3脂肪酸，酯键"],["Saturated fats: no C=C double bonds; solid at room temperature; animal sources (butter); raise bad cholesterol (LDL). Unsaturated fats: C=C double bonds; liquid oils; plant sources (olive, sunflower).","饱和脂肪：无双键、常温固态、动物来源；不饱和脂肪：有双键、液态、植物来源"],["Phospholipid: glycerol + 2 fatty acids + a phosphate group; hydrophilic head, hydrophobic tails; forms the cell membrane bilayer.","磷脂：甘油+2脂肪酸+磷酸；亲水头疏水尾；构成膜"],["Steroids: cholesterol (membrane; makes sex hormones, vitamin D, bile salts). Wax: waterproof coating (cuticle).","类固醇：胆固醇；蜡：防水涂层"],["Functions: energy store (about 38 kJ per gram); insulation; protect organs; solvent for vitamins A, D, E, K; membrane structure; hormones.","功能：储能(约38 kJ/g)；隔热；保护器官；溶解脂溶性维生素；膜结构；激素"]],"","Tip: lipids give twice as much energy per gram as carbohydrates and proteins."],["Lipid Tests and Health","脂质测试与健康",[["Sudan III test: add Sudan III to the sample; a red/orange layer or droplets forms on top = lipid present.","苏丹III试验：出现红/橙色油层或油滴"],["Emulsion test: shake the sample with ethanol, then add water; a cloudy white emulsion = lipid present.","乳化试验：加乙醇振荡再加水，出现白色浑浊"],["Cholesterol: LDL (low-density lipoprotein) deposits cholesterol in artery walls (atherosclerosis); HDL removes cholesterol.","胆固醇：LDL沉积血管壁(动脉粥样硬化)；HDL清除"],["Health issues: excess saturated fat and trans fat cause obesity, coronary heart disease and high blood pressure.","健康：过量饱和脂肪与反式脂肪导致肥胖、冠心病、高血压"],["Practise a balanced diet, regular exercise and choose unsaturated fats.","均衡饮食、运动、选不饱和脂肪"]],"","Tip: Sudan III — red/orange oil on top; emulsion test — cloudy white."],["Nucleic Acids: DNA and RNA","核酸：DNA与RNA",[["Nucleotide = pentose sugar + phosphate group + nitrogenous base.","核苷酸＝五碳糖+磷酸+含氮碱基"],["DNA: deoxyribose sugar; bases A, T, C, G; double helix with two polynucleotide strands; complementary base pairing A–T (2 hydrogen bonds), C–G (3 hydrogen bonds).","DNA：脱氧核糖；A、T、C、G；双螺旋；A–T、C–G配对"],["RNA: ribose sugar; bases A, U, C, G; single stranded. Types: mRNA (carries the genetic code), tRNA (brings amino acids), rRNA (part of ribosomes).","RNA：核糖；A、U、C、G；单链；mRNA、tRNA、rRNA"],["DNA stores genetic information; a gene is a segment of DNA that codes for a polypeptide. Protein synthesis overview: transcription (DNA → mRNA in the nucleus) → translation (mRNA → polypeptide at a ribosome).","DNA储存遗传信息；基因编码多肽；蛋白质合成：转录→翻译"],["Chargaff: A = T and C = G in DNA, so (A + G) ÷ (T + C) = 1.","查加夫规则：A＝T，C＝G"]],"","Tip: RNA has uracil (U) instead of thymine (T) and ribose instead of deoxyribose."],["Worked Example: Food Test Table and DNA","例题：食物测试与DNA",[["Q: A food sample gives brick-red precipitate with Benedict's, no colour change with iodine, purple with Biuret. It contains reducing sugar and protein but no starch.","题：本尼迪克特砖红、碘无变化、双缩脲紫色：含还原糖与蛋白质，无淀粉"],["Q: A sample is blue with Benedict's but after boiling with HCl it turns brick-red. It contains a non-reducing sugar (sucrose).","题：先蓝，酸水解后砖红：含蔗糖"],["Q: A DNA strand has 30% adenine. Thymine = 30%; cytosine + guanine = 40% (20% each).","题：DNA腺嘌呤30%：胸腺嘧啶30%；C、G各20%"],["Q: Why do plants store energy as starch but not glucose? A: Starch is insoluble and does not affect the osmotic balance, and it is compact.","题：为何储存淀粉而非葡萄糖？答：不溶、不影响渗透压、紧凑"]],"","Tip: write the test, the reagent, the condition and the colour change."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Carbohydrate (Karbohidrat); Protein (Protein); Lipid (Lipid); Nucleic acid (Asid nukleik)","糖类；蛋白质；脂质；核酸"],["Monosaccharide (Monosakarida); Disaccharide (Disakarida); Polysaccharide (Polisakarida)","单糖；二糖；多糖"],["Amino acid (Asid amino); Peptide bond (Ikatan peptida); Denaturation (Penyahaslian)","氨基酸；肽键；变性"],["Triglyceride (Trigliserida); Phospholipid (Fosfolipid); Cholesterol (Kolesterol)","三酸甘油酯；磷脂；胆固醇"],["Condensation (Kondensasi); Hydrolysis (Hidrolisis); Benedict's test (Ujian Benedict)","缩合；水解；本尼迪克特试验"]],"","Tip: learn the colour changes in both languages."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Forgetting to heat in Benedict's test, or to neutralise after acid hydrolysis of sucrose.","本尼迪克特试验忘记加热；酸水解后忘记中和"],["Saying sucrose is a reducing sugar.","把蔗糖当成还原糖"],["Confusing a peptide bond (proteins) with a glycosidic bond (carbohydrates) and an ester bond (lipids).","混淆肽键、糖苷键、酯键"],["Writing that enzymes/proteins are 'killed' by heat — use 'denatured'.","蛋白质受热应写“变性”，不是“杀死”"],["Thinking cholesterol is always harmful — it is needed for membranes and hormones.","胆固醇并非全坏，膜和激素需要它"]],"","Tip: draw a molecule diagram when asked about peptide or glycosidic bond formation."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Name the monomers of starch, proteins and DNA. J: Glucose, amino acids and nucleotides.","问：淀粉、蛋白质、DNA单体？答：葡萄糖、氨基酸、核苷酸"],["S: What colour change shows the presence of starch? J: Brown/yellow to blue-black with iodine solution.","问：淀粉颜色变化？答：碘液由棕黄变蓝黑"],["S: Why is water a good solvent in organisms? J: It is polar so it dissolves many substances, allowing transport and chemical reactions in solution.","问：水为何是好溶剂？答：极性，能溶解许多物质，利于运输与反应"],["S: Compare saturated and unsaturated fats. J: Saturated: no double bonds, solid, animal, raise LDL. Unsaturated: double bonds, liquid, plant, healthier.","问：饱和与不饱和脂肪？答：前者无双键固态动物来源；后者有双键液态植物来源"],["S: State two differences between DNA and RNA. J: DNA has deoxyribose, thymine and is double stranded; RNA has ribose, uracil and is single stranded.","问：DNA与RNA两差异？答：DNA脱氧核糖、T、双链；RNA核糖、U、单链"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-5":[["Metabolism: Anabolism and Catabolism","新陈代谢：合成与分解",[["Metabolism: all chemical reactions in living organisms; it consists of anabolism and catabolism.","新陈代谢：生物体内所有化学反应"],["Anabolism: building complex molecules from simpler ones (condensation); requires energy. Examples: photosynthesis, protein synthesis, glycogen formation.","合成代谢：小分子合成大分子，耗能：光合、蛋白合成、糖原形成"],["Catabolism: breaking down complex molecules into simpler ones (hydrolysis); releases energy. Examples: cellular respiration, digestion, breakdown of glycogen.","分解代谢：大分子分解，释放能量：呼吸、消化、糖原分解"],["Metabolism is controlled by enzymes; each reaction occurs in sequence in a metabolic pathway.","代谢由酶控制，按代谢途径进行"],["Energy released by catabolism is used to build ATP; ATP supplies energy for anabolism.","分解代谢释放的能量合成ATP；ATP为合成代谢供能"]],"","Tip: anabolism = 'build up', catabolism = 'break down' — do not reverse."],["ATP: The Energy Currency","ATP：能量货币",[["ATP (adenosine triphosphate) = adenine + ribose + three phosphate groups.","ATP＝腺嘌呤+核糖+3个磷酸"],["ATP → ADP + Pi + energy (hydrolysis, releases energy). ADP + Pi + energy → ATP (phosphorylation).","ATP水解释放能量；ADP+Pi+能量→ATP"],["ATP is formed in the mitochondria (respiration) and chloroplasts (photosynthesis); it is a small, soluble, quickly available energy source.","ATP在线粒体、叶绿体中生成；小、可溶、能迅速提供能量"],["Uses of ATP: active transport, muscle contraction, protein synthesis, cell division, nerve impulse transmission, bioluminescence.","ATP用途：主动运输、肌肉收缩、蛋白合成、细胞分裂、神经冲动"],["Energy cannot be stored as ATP for long; it is regenerated continuously.","ATP不能长久储存，需不断再生"]],"","Tip: the energy is released when the terminal phosphate bond is broken."],["Enzymes: Properties and Mechanism","酶：特性与作用机制",[["Enzymes are biological catalysts made of protein; they speed up reactions by lowering the activation energy and are not used up.","酶是蛋白质催化剂，降低活化能加快反应，不被消耗"],["Properties: required in small amounts; specific (one enzyme, one substrate/type of reaction); work at optimum temperature and pH; reversible reactions; can be denatured; names usually end in –ase.","特性：用量少；专一；有最适温度与pH；可逆；可变性；多以-ase结尾"],["Lock-and-key hypothesis: the substrate fits the active site of the enzyme → enzyme–substrate complex → products form and leave → the enzyme can be reused.","锁钥假说：底物契合活性位点→酶-底物复合物→产物释放→酶可重复使用"],["Intracellular enzymes work inside cells (e.g. catalase, respiration enzymes); extracellular enzymes work outside cells (e.g. digestive enzymes amylase, pepsin).","胞内酶在细胞内；胞外酶在细胞外（消化酶）"],["Example: amylase: starch → maltose; protease: protein → polypeptides/amino acids; lipase: fats → fatty acids and glycerol; catalase: hydrogen peroxide → water + oxygen.","例：淀粉酶、蛋白酶、脂肪酶、过氧化氢酶"]],"","Tip: enzymes lower activation energy — they do NOT supply energy."],["Factors Affecting Enzyme Activity (1)","影响酶活性的因素（1）",[["Temperature: the rate increases with temperature up to the optimum (about 37 °C for human enzymes) because molecules have more kinetic energy and collide more.","温度：升至最适(人体酶约37 °C)速率增加：碰撞更多"],["Above the optimum, the enzyme is denatured (active site loses shape) and the rate falls sharply, usually above 60 °C. At low temperature the enzyme is inactive but not denatured.","超过最适温度酶变性，速率骤降；低温酶不活跃但不变性"],["pH: each enzyme has an optimum pH (pepsin about pH 2; salivary amylase about pH 7; trypsin about pH 8). Extreme pH denatures the enzyme.","pH：各酶有最适pH：胃蛋白酶约2；唾液淀粉酶约7；胰蛋白酶约8；极端pH使酶变性"],["The rate–temperature graph rises to a peak and then falls steeply; the rate–pH graph is bell-shaped.","速率-温度图先升后陡降；速率-pH图呈钟形"]],"","Tip: low temperature = inactive; high temperature = denatured."],["Factors Affecting Enzyme Activity (2)","影响酶活性的因素（2）",[["Substrate concentration: the rate increases as substrate concentration increases until all active sites are occupied (saturated); then the rate levels off — the enzyme concentration becomes the limiting factor.","底物浓度：增加至活性位点饱和后趋平，此时酶浓度为限制因素"],["Enzyme concentration: with excess substrate, the rate increases in proportion to the enzyme concentration because more active sites are available.","酶浓度：底物充足时，速率随酶浓度成比例增加"],["Inhibitors (heavy metal ions such as Hg²⁺, cyanide) block the active site and reduce enzyme activity.","抑制剂（重金属离子、氰化物）阻碍活性位点，降低酶活性"],["Cofactors/coenzymes (e.g. vitamins, Mg²⁺) may be needed for enzyme activity.","辅因子/辅酶（维生素、Mg²⁺）有助酶活性"]],"","Tip: explain a plateau using 'all active sites occupied'."],["Investigations: Enzyme Activity","探究：酶活性",[["Effect of temperature on amylase: mix starch + amylase at different temperatures (e.g. 10, 30, 40, 50, 70 °C); test with iodine every 30 s; record the time taken for the blue-black colour to disappear.","温度对淀粉酶：在不同温度混合，每30秒取样加碘，记录蓝黑消失时间"],["Effect of pH on amylase/catalase: use buffers (pH 3, 5, 7, 9, 11); measure time or volume of oxygen released from H₂O₂ using catalase from liver/yeast/potato.","pH对酶：用缓冲液，测时间或氧气体积"],["Manipulated variable: temperature or pH; responding variable: time taken (rate = 1 ÷ time) or volume of O₂; fixed: enzyme and substrate concentration/volume.","操纵：温度或pH；反应：所需时间（速率=1÷时间）；固定：酶与底物浓度/体积"],["Optimum temperature/pH = the condition with the shortest time (fastest rate).","最适温度/pH＝时间最短的条件"]],"","Tip: rate = 1 ÷ time. A shorter time means a higher rate."],["Applications of Enzymes in Daily Life","酶在日常生活的应用",[["Detergents: protease, lipase and amylase remove protein, fat and starch stains; they work at low temperature, saving energy.","洗衣剂：蛋白酶、脂肪酶、淀粉酶去渍，低温有效节能"],["Food industry: rennin/chymosin to make cheese; papain and bromelain tenderise meat; amylase in bread, beer and syrup; pectinase clears fruit juice; lactase makes lactose-free milk.","食品：凝乳酶做奶酪；木瓜蛋白酶嫩肉；淀粉酶；果胶酶澄清果汁；乳糖酶"],["Medicine and others: streptokinase dissolves blood clots; enzymes in diagnostic kits (glucose oxidase); leather tanning and textiles (protease, amylase).","医药及其他：链激酶溶血栓；葡萄糖氧化酶；皮革、纺织"],["Immobilised enzymes (fixed on beads) can be reused, so they are cheaper and easy to separate from the product.","固定化酶可重复使用，成本低且易分离"],["Advantages of enzymes in industry: work at mild conditions, are specific, and are biodegradable.","工业优点：条件温和、专一、可生物降解"]],"","Tip: for each application give the enzyme + the substrate + the benefit."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Metabolism (Metabolisme); Anabolism (Anabolisme); Catabolism (Katabolisme)","新陈代谢；合成代谢；分解代谢"],["Enzyme (Enzim); Substrate (Substrat); Active site (Tapak aktif); Product (Hasil)","酶；底物；活性位点；产物"],["Denaturation (Penyahaslian); Optimum temperature (Suhu optimum); Optimum pH (pH optimum)","变性；最适温度；最适pH"],["Activation energy (Tenaga pengaktifan); Inhibitor (Perencat); Immobilised enzyme (Enzim tak bergerak)","活化能；抑制剂；固定化酶"]],"","Tip: 'tapak aktif' = active site."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Writing that enzymes are 'killed' or 'destroyed' by heat — use 'denatured'. At low temperature, enzymes are inactive, not denatured.","写“酶被杀死”；低温酶不变性只是不活跃"],["Saying enzymes provide energy for the reaction — they lower the activation energy.","酶不提供能量，而是降低活化能"],["Forgetting that the enzyme is not used up and can be reused.","忘记酶可重复使用"],["Graph questions: explain the plateau with 'all active sites occupied' and the fall with 'denatured'.","图表题：趋平＝活性位点饱和；下降＝变性"],["Mixing up anabolism (needs energy) and catabolism (releases energy).","混淆合成与分解代谢"]],"","Tip: for 'explain the graph' questions use: Region → Observation → Reason."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Define metabolism. J: All the chemical reactions that take place in the cells of living organisms.","问：何为新陈代谢？答：生物细胞内所有化学反应"],["S: State the lock-and-key hypothesis. J: The substrate fits the active site of the enzyme because their shapes are complementary, forming an enzyme–substrate complex.","问：锁钥假说？答：底物与活性位点形状互补，形成酶-底物复合物"],["S: Why does the rate of an enzyme-catalysed reaction fall at 70 °C? J: The enzyme is denatured, the active site changes shape and substrates cannot fit.","问：70 °C速率为何下降？答：酶变性，活性位点改变，底物无法结合"],["S: Give one use of protease in daily life. J: In detergents to remove protein stains / tenderise meat.","问：蛋白酶一项用途？答：洗衣剂去蛋白渍/嫩肉"],["S: Why is ATP called the energy currency? J: It releases energy quickly when hydrolysed, and is used in many cell activities.","问：ATP为何称能量货币？答：水解快速释能，用于许多细胞活动"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-6":[["Why Cells Divide; Chromosomes","细胞为何分裂；染色体",[["Cell division is needed for growth, replacement of dead cells, repair of damaged tissues and reproduction.","细胞分裂用于生长、替换死细胞、修复组织与繁殖"],["Chromatin (long thin DNA + histone proteins) coils and condenses into chromosomes during division. Each chromosome has two sister chromatids joined at a centromere after DNA replication.","染色质在分裂时螺旋浓缩成染色体；复制后有两条姐妹染色单体，由着丝点相连"],["Diploid (2n): two sets of chromosomes (human 2n = 46 = 23 pairs; 22 pairs of autosomes + 1 pair of sex chromosomes). Haploid (n): one set (gametes, human n = 23).","二倍体：成对染色体（人46条）；单倍体：一套（配子23条）"],["Homologous chromosomes: a pair, one from each parent, with the same genes in the same sequence (not necessarily identical alleles).","同源染色体：一对，来自父母，基因位置相同"],["Two types of division: mitosis (body cells) and meiosis (gamete formation).","两种分裂：有丝分裂（体细胞）、减数分裂（配子）"]],"","Tip: chromosome number is counted by the number of centromeres."],["The Cell Cycle and Interphase","细胞周期与间期",[["Cell cycle: interphase (G₁, S, G₂) + mitosis (M) + cytokinesis.","细胞周期：间期（G₁、S、G₂）+有丝分裂+胞质分裂"],["G₁: cell grows, makes organelles and proteins. S: DNA replicates (each chromosome becomes two chromatids). G₂: cell prepares for division; makes spindle proteins and ATP.","G₁生长；S期DNA复制；G₂准备分裂"],["Interphase is the longest stage (about 90% of the cycle) — the cell is not dividing but is very active.","间期最长（约90%），细胞很活跃"],["Checkpoints control the cycle; if DNA is damaged the cycle stops. Loss of control leads to tumours/cancer.","检查点控制周期；失控导致肿瘤/癌症"],["Cells that no longer divide are in G₀ (e.g. mature neurones).","不再分裂的细胞处于G₀期"]],"","Tip: DNA replication occurs in the S phase of interphase — not during mitosis."],["Mitosis: Prophase and Metaphase","有丝分裂：前期与中期",[["Prophase: chromosomes condense and become visible as two chromatids; nucleolus disappears; nuclear membrane breaks down; spindle fibres form; centrioles move to the poles (animal cell).","前期：染色体浓缩可见；核仁消失；核膜瓦解；纺锤丝形成；中心粒移向两极"],["Metaphase: chromosomes line up at the equator (metaphase plate); spindle fibres attach to the centromeres.","中期：染色体排列在赤道面；纺锤丝连着着丝点"],["Metaphase is the best stage for counting and studying chromosomes (karyotype).","中期最适合观察和计数染色体"],["Plant cells have no centrioles but still form a spindle.","植物细胞无中心粒但仍形成纺锤丝"]],"","Tip: remember PMAT — Prophase, Metaphase, Anaphase, Telophase."],["Mitosis: Anaphase, Telophase and Cytokinesis","有丝分裂：后期、末期与胞质分裂",[["Anaphase: centromeres divide; sister chromatids separate and are pulled to opposite poles by the shortening spindle fibres.","后期：着丝点分裂，姐妹染色单体被拉向两极"],["Telophase: chromatids (now chromosomes) reach the poles and uncoil; nuclear membrane and nucleolus reappear; spindle fibres disappear.","末期：染色体到达两极解螺旋；核膜、核仁重现；纺锤丝消失"],["Cytokinesis (animal cell): the cell membrane constricts inwards to form a cleavage furrow. Plant cell: a cell plate forms at the equator and develops into a new cell wall.","胞质分裂：动物细胞形成分裂沟；植物细胞形成细胞板，发展为新细胞壁"],["Result: two daughter cells, genetically identical to the parent cell, each with the same number of chromosomes (2n).","结果：两个与母细胞遗传相同的子细胞，染色体数不变"]],"","Tip: anaphase — chromatids separate; telophase — nuclei re-form."],["Importance of Mitosis","有丝分裂的重要性",[["Growth of multicellular organisms (increase in cell number).","多细胞生物生长"],["Replacement of dead or worn-out cells (e.g. skin, blood cells) and repair of wounds.","替换死亡细胞、修复伤口"],["Asexual reproduction in unicellular organisms (Amoeba) and in plants (vegetative propagation); budding in yeast and Hydra.","无性生殖：变形虫、植物营养繁殖、酵母出芽"],["Maintains the same chromosome number and the genetic stability of daughter cells.","维持染色体数目与遗传稳定"],["Stem cells divide by mitosis and then differentiate.","干细胞通过有丝分裂后再分化"]],"","Tip: write 'genetically identical' and 'same chromosome number'."],["Meiosis I and Meiosis II","减数分裂I与II",[["Meiosis takes place in the reproductive organs (testes and ovaries; anthers and ovules) and produces gametes (haploid). One diploid cell → four haploid cells, genetically different.","减数分裂在生殖器官进行，一个二倍体细胞→四个遗传不同的单倍体细胞"],["Meiosis I (reduction division): Prophase I — homologous chromosomes pair (bivalent); crossing over occurs at chiasmata. Metaphase I — bivalents at the equator. Anaphase I — homologous chromosomes separate. Telophase I — two haploid cells.","减数分裂I：前期I同源染色体配对、交叉互换；中期I排赤道；后期I同源染色体分离；末期I两个单倍体细胞"],["Meiosis II (like mitosis): chromatids separate; four haploid cells (n) formed.","减数分裂II：姐妹染色单体分离，形成四个单倍体细胞"],["Crossing over: exchange of genetic material between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes. Independent assortment: random orientation of bivalents at metaphase I.","交叉互换：同源染色体非姐妹染色单体交换片段；自由组合：中期I随机排列"]],"","Tip: meiosis I separates homologous chromosomes; meiosis II separates sister chromatids."],["Importance of Meiosis; Mitosis vs Meiosis","减数分裂的重要性；与有丝分裂比较",[["Maintains chromosome number: gametes are haploid (n); fertilisation restores the diploid (2n) number in the zygote.","维持染色体数：配子单倍体，受精恢复二倍体"],["Produces variation through crossing over, independent assortment and random fertilisation — important for evolution and adaptation.","通过交叉互换、自由组合、随机受精产生变异"],["Mitosis: 1 division; 2 daughter cells; diploid; identical; body cells; no crossing over. Meiosis: 2 divisions; 4 daughter cells; haploid; different; gamete formation; crossing over occurs.","有丝：1次分裂、2个子细胞、二倍体、相同、体细胞；减数：2次、4个、单倍体、不同、配子、有交叉互换"],["Non-disjunction (failure of chromosomes to separate) can cause Down syndrome (trisomy 21: 47 chromosomes).","染色体不分离可致唐氏综合征（21三体，47条）"]],"","Tip: comparison questions need a table — number of divisions, number and type of cells, chromosome number, variation."],["Cell Division and Human Health: Cancer and Stem Cells","细胞分裂与健康：癌症与干细胞",[["Cancer: uncontrolled cell division forms a tumour. Benign tumour: stays in one place, not life-threatening. Malignant tumour: invades other tissues and spreads (metastasis).","癌症：失控分裂形成肿瘤；良性不扩散，恶性会侵袭转移"],["Causes (carcinogens): tobacco smoke, ultraviolet and ionising radiation, certain chemicals (asbestos, aflatoxin), viruses (HPV), genetic factors, unhealthy lifestyle.","致癌因素：烟草、紫外线/电离辐射、化学物、病毒、遗传、不良生活方式"],["Treatment: surgery, chemotherapy, radiotherapy, targeted therapy and stem cell transplant. Prevention: avoid smoking, healthy diet, exercise, sun protection, vaccination (HPV), regular screening (mammogram, Pap smear, self-examination).","治疗：手术、化疗、放疗、靶向治疗、干细胞移植；预防：戒烟、健康饮食、运动、防晒、疫苗、定期检查"],["Stem cells: used to treat leukaemia, burns and degenerative diseases; ethical issues include use of embryos, cloning and cost.","干细胞用于治疗白血病、烧伤等；伦理：使用胚胎、克隆、成本"]],"","Tip: give causes, effects and prevention separately for 'health issue' questions."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Mitosis (Mitosis); Meiosis (Meiosis); Cell cycle (Kitar sel); Interphase (Interfasa)","有丝分裂；减数分裂；细胞周期；间期"],["Chromosome (Kromosom); Chromatid (Kromatid); Centromere (Sentromer); Spindle fibre (Gentian gelendong)","染色体；染色单体；着丝点；纺锤丝"],["Diploid (Diploid); Haploid (Haploid); Homologous chromosomes (Kromosom homolog)","二倍体；单倍体；同源染色体"],["Crossing over (Pindah silang); Tumour (Tumor); Cancer (Kanser); Stem cell (Sel stem)","交叉互换；肿瘤；癌症；干细胞"]],"","Tip: 'kromatid adik beradik' = sister chromatids."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Confusing chromosomes and chromatids: after replication one chromosome has two chromatids; in anaphase each chromatid becomes a chromosome.","混淆染色体与染色单体"],["Saying DNA replicates in prophase — it replicates in the S phase of interphase.","DNA复制在间期S期，不在前期"],["Forgetting crossing over, independent assortment and random fertilisation as sources of variation.","遗漏变异来源"],["Mixing up the sequence of stages: always PMAT; meiosis I then meiosis II.","阶段顺序：PMAT"],["Writing 'meiosis produces identical cells' — it produces genetically different haploid cells.","减数分裂产生的是遗传不同的细胞"]],"","Tip: when identifying stages in a diagram, look at the chromosome position and the nuclear membrane."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: How many chromosomes are present in a human sperm cell? J: 23.","问：人精子含多少染色体？答：23"],["S: In which stage do sister chromatids separate in mitosis? J: Anaphase.","问：有丝分裂哪一期姐妹染色单体分离？答：后期"],["S: State two differences between mitosis and meiosis. J: Mitosis gives two identical diploid cells; meiosis gives four genetically different haploid cells.","问：两差异？答：有丝＝2个相同二倍体；减数＝4个不同单倍体"],["S: How does meiosis cause variation? J: Crossing over and independent assortment of homologous chromosomes (plus random fertilisation).","问：减数分裂如何产生变异？答：交叉互换、同源染色体自由组合（加随机受精）"],["S: Differentiate benign and malignant tumours. J: Benign stays in one place; malignant invades other tissues and spreads.","问：良性与恶性肿瘤？答：良性局限；恶性侵袭扩散"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-7":[["Cellular Respiration and ATP","细胞呼吸与ATP",[["Cellular respiration: a series of enzyme-controlled reactions that break down glucose (organic molecules) to release energy, which is used to produce ATP.","细胞呼吸：酶控制的反应分解葡萄糖，释放能量合成ATP"],["Respiration is not the same as breathing (breathing is the exchange of gases between the organism and the environment).","呼吸作用≠呼吸（呼吸是气体交换）"],["Two types: aerobic respiration (with oxygen) and anaerobic respiration/fermentation (without oxygen).","两类：有氧呼吸、无氧呼吸/发酵"],["Energy is used for active transport, muscle contraction, synthesis of molecules, cell division, nerve impulses and maintaining body temperature.","能量用于主动运输、肌肉收缩、合成、细胞分裂、神经冲动、维持体温"],["Glucose is the main respiratory substrate; other substrates are fats and proteins.","主要底物是葡萄糖；也可用脂肪与蛋白质"]],"","Tip: write 'energy is released and used to form ATP' — energy is not 'made'."],["Investigating Respiration","探究呼吸作用",[["Carbon dioxide test: limewater turns milky/cloudy; hydrogen carbonate indicator changes from red to yellow as CO₂ increases.","CO₂检测：石灰水变浑浊；碳酸氢盐指示剂红→黄"],["Respiration in germinating seeds: place germinating seeds (and dead/boiled seeds as control) in a flask; use limewater or a respirometer to detect CO₂ or O₂ uptake.","发芽种子的呼吸：以煮熟种子作对照，用石灰水或呼吸计检测"],["Heat released can be shown with a thermos flask containing germinating seeds and a thermometer (temperature rises).","发芽种子在保温瓶中放热，温度上升"],["Respirometer: absorbs CO₂ (potassium hydroxide); the movement of coloured liquid shows the volume of oxygen consumed.","呼吸计：KOH吸收CO₂，有色液体移动显示耗氧量"]],"","Tip: always include a control (boiled seeds) to show the result is due to living tissue."],["Aerobic Respiration: Overview and Equation","有氧呼吸：概述与方程式",[["Word equation: glucose + oxygen → carbon dioxide + water + energy (ATP).","文字方程式：葡萄糖+氧→二氧化碳+水+能量(ATP)"],["Chemical equation: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O + 38 ATP (value used in SPM; some references give about 30–32 ATP).","化学方程式：C₆H₁₂O₆+6O₂→6CO₂+6H₂O+38 ATP（SPM用38；有资料写30–32）"],["Occurs in the cytoplasm (glycolysis) and the mitochondria (link reaction, Krebs cycle and electron transport chain).","场所：细胞质（糖酵解）与线粒体"],["Complete oxidation of glucose: releases much energy; end products are carbon dioxide and water.","葡萄糖彻底氧化：释放大量能量；产物CO₂和水"]],"","Tip: in SPM answers, quote 38 ATP for aerobic and 2 ATP for anaerobic respiration."],["Aerobic Respiration: Stages","有氧呼吸：阶段",[["Glycolysis (cytoplasm, no oxygen needed): glucose (6C) → 2 pyruvate (3C); net gain 2 ATP and 2 NADH.","糖酵解（细胞质）：葡萄糖→2丙酮酸；净得2 ATP、2 NADH"],["Link reaction (mitochondrial matrix): pyruvate → acetyl-CoA + CO₂ + NADH.","连接反应：丙酮酸→乙酰辅酶A+CO₂+NADH"],["Krebs cycle (matrix): acetyl-CoA is oxidised; CO₂ released; produces ATP, NADH and FADH₂.","克雷布斯循环（基质）：释放CO₂，产生ATP、NADH、FADH₂"],["Electron transport chain (inner membrane/cristae): NADH and FADH₂ pass electrons along carriers; energy forms most ATP (about 34); oxygen is the final electron acceptor and combines with hydrogen to form water.","电子传递链（内膜/嵴）：产生大部分ATP；氧为最终电子受体，与氢结合成水"],["Mitochondrion: double membrane; folded inner membrane (cristae) increases the surface area; the matrix contains enzymes.","线粒体：双膜；嵴增大表面积；基质含酶"]],"","Tip: oxygen is only used in the final stage (electron transport chain)."],["Anaerobic Respiration (Fermentation)","无氧呼吸（发酵）",[["Alcoholic fermentation (yeast, plants in waterlogged soil): glucose → 2 ethanol + 2 CO₂ + 2 ATP.","酒精发酵（酵母、水涝植物）：葡萄糖→2乙醇+2CO₂+2 ATP"],["Lactic acid fermentation (muscle cells during vigorous exercise; Lactobacillus): glucose → 2 lactic acid + 2 ATP.","乳酸发酵（剧烈运动的肌肉；乳酸菌）：葡萄糖→2乳酸+2 ATP"],["Occurs in the cytoplasm; glucose is only partially broken down, so only 2 ATP are released (much less than 38).","发生在细胞质；葡萄糖不完全分解，仅得2 ATP"],["Lactic acid builds up in muscles → muscle fatigue and cramp. Oxygen debt: extra oxygen needed after exercise to break down lactic acid in the liver; breathing remains fast until the debt is repaid.","乳酸积累→疲劳抽筋；氧债：运动后需额外氧气分解乳酸，呼吸保持急促"]],"","Tip: muscle = lactic acid (no CO₂); yeast = ethanol + CO₂."],["Applications of Fermentation","发酵的应用",[["Bread: yeast produces CO₂, which makes the dough rise; ethanol evaporates during baking.","面包：酵母产生CO₂使面团膨胀"],["Alcoholic drinks and tapai (fermented tapioca/rice): yeast converts sugar into ethanol.","酒类与塔排：酵母把糖转化为乙醇"],["Yoghurt and cheese: Lactobacillus converts lactose into lactic acid, which coagulates milk protein. Also pickles, soy sauce, tempeh.","酸奶、奶酪：乳酸菌把乳糖变乳酸使乳蛋白凝固"],["Biofuel: yeast ferments sugar from plants to produce bioethanol.","生物燃料：发酵产生生物乙醇"]],"","Tip: name the microorganism, substrate and product for each application."],["Comparison: Aerobic vs Anaerobic Respiration","有氧与无氧呼吸比较",[["Oxygen: required (aerobic) / not required (anaerobic). Site: cytoplasm and mitochondria / cytoplasm only.","氧：需要/不需要；场所：细胞质+线粒体/仅细胞质"],["Breakdown of glucose: complete / incomplete.","葡萄糖：彻底/不彻底"],["Products: CO₂ and water / ethanol and CO₂ (yeast) or lactic acid (muscle).","产物：CO₂和水/乙醇+CO₂或乳酸"],["Energy: 38 ATP per glucose / 2 ATP per glucose; more efficient / less efficient.","能量：38 ATP/2 ATP"],["Both: start with glycolysis, occur in all living cells, are controlled by enzymes and produce ATP.","共同点：都有糖酵解、酶控制、产生ATP"]],"","Tip: set the comparison out in a table with the same headings for both."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Respiration (Respirasi); Aerobic respiration (Respirasi aerob); Anaerobic respiration (Respirasi anaerob)","呼吸作用；有氧；无氧"],["Glycolysis (Glikolisis); Krebs cycle (Kitar Krebs); Electron transport chain (Rantai pengangkutan elektron)","糖酵解；克雷布斯循环；电子传递链"],["Fermentation (Penapaian); Lactic acid (Asid laktik); Ethanol (Etanol); Oxygen debt (Hutang oksigen)","发酵；乳酸；乙醇；氧债"],["Mitochondrion (Mitokondrion); Cristae (Krista); Matrix (Matriks)","线粒体；嵴；基质"]],"","Tip: 'penapaian' = fermentation."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Confusing respiration (cellular process) with breathing (gas exchange).","混淆呼吸作用与呼吸"],["Writing 'energy is produced' — energy is released from glucose and stored in ATP.","能量是释放，不是制造"],["Saying muscle cells produce alcohol — they produce lactic acid; yeast produces ethanol + CO₂.","肌肉产乳酸；酵母产乙醇+CO₂"],["Forgetting that glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm for both aerobic and anaerobic respiration.","忘记糖酵解在细胞质，两种呼吸都有"],["Oxygen debt is repaid after exercise (breathing stays fast), not during.","氧债运动后偿还"]],"","Tip: show the equation with the correct balancing: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Write the overall equation for aerobic respiration. J: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O + 38 ATP.","问：有氧呼吸总方程式？答：C₆H₁₂O₆+6O₂→6CO₂+6H₂O+38 ATP"],["S: Where does the electron transport chain occur? J: On the inner membrane (cristae) of the mitochondrion.","问：电子传递链在哪？答：线粒体内膜（嵴）"],["S: Why does dough rise when yeast is added? J: Yeast respires anaerobically and releases CO₂, which forms bubbles in the dough.","问：酵母使面团膨胀的原因？答：无氧呼吸释放CO₂形成气泡"],["S: What is oxygen debt? J: The extra oxygen needed after vigorous exercise to break down lactic acid.","问：氧债？答：剧烈运动后分解乳酸所需的额外氧气"],["S: Why is anaerobic respiration less efficient? J: Glucose is only partly broken down so only 2 ATP are produced.","问：无氧呼吸为何效率低？答：葡萄糖不完全分解，只产生2 ATP"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-8":[["Respiratory Surfaces and Types of Respiratory Systems","呼吸表面与呼吸系统类型",[["A good gas exchange surface has: a large surface area; a thin wall (one cell thick); a moist surface so gases dissolve; a rich blood supply (capillaries) to maintain the concentration gradient; ventilation.","良好的气体交换表面：面积大、壁薄(一层细胞)、湿润、血液丰富、有通气"],["Amoeba: gases diffuse directly across the cell surface membrane (large SA:V ratio, no transport system).","变形虫：气体经细胞膜直接扩散"],["Earthworm: gas exchange through the moist, thin skin; the mucus keeps the skin moist; blood capillaries under the skin carry the gases.","蚯蚓：湿润薄皮肤；黏液保湿；皮下毛细血管运输"],["Insects (grasshopper): tracheal system — spiracles → tracheae (chitin rings keep open) → tracheoles that deliver oxygen directly to the cells; abdominal movements ventilate.","昆虫：气管系统——气门→气管（几丁质环）→微气管直接供氧；腹部运动通气"],["Fish: gills (gill filaments with gill lamellae); amphibians: moist skin and lungs; mammals: lungs.","鱼：鳃；两栖：皮肤与肺；哺乳：肺"]],"","Tip: insects' blood does not transport oxygen — tracheoles reach the cells directly."],["Gills of Fish and Counter-Current Flow","鱼鳃与逆流交换",[["Each gill has many gill filaments; each filament has many gill lamellae with a very thin epithelium and a dense network of capillaries → very large surface area.","鳃丝与鳃片：上皮薄、毛细血管多，面积大"],["Water flows over the gills in the opposite direction to the flow of blood in the capillaries (counter-current flow). This maintains a concentration gradient along the whole length of the lamella, so more oxygen diffuses into the blood.","水流与血流方向相反（逆流），整个鳃片都维持浓度梯度，吸收更多氧"],["Ventilation: mouth opens and floor of the mouth lowers, operculum closed → water enters. Mouth closes, floor rises, operculum opens → water flows over gills and out.","通气：口张开口底下降，鳃盖关→水入；口闭口底升，鳃盖开→水流过鳃排出"],["Oxygen in water is only about 1/30 that of air, so fish need efficient gills.","水中氧约为空气的1/30，鱼需高效鳃"]],"","Tip: explain counter-current as 'blood always meets water with higher oxygen concentration'."],["Mechanism of Breathing in Humans","人体呼吸运动",[["Inhalation: external intercostal muscles contract and internal intercostal muscles relax → rib cage moves upwards and outwards; diaphragm contracts and flattens → thoracic cavity volume increases → air pressure inside falls below atmospheric pressure → air flows in.","吸气：外肋间肌收缩、肋骨上提外展；膈肌收缩变平→胸腔容积增大→压力降低→空气进入"],["Exhalation: external intercostal muscles relax, internal intercostal muscles contract → rib cage moves downwards and inwards; diaphragm relaxes and curves upwards (dome) → volume decreases → pressure rises above atmospheric → air flows out.","呼气：肋骨下降内收；膈肌放松拱起→容积减小→压力升高→空气排出"],["Breathing is controlled by the medulla oblongata, which responds to the level of carbon dioxide in the blood.","呼吸受延髓控制，感应血中CO₂浓度"],["During exercise, more CO₂ → faster and deeper breathing to remove CO₂ and bring in more O₂.","运动时CO₂增多→呼吸更快更深"]],"","Tip: remember 'volume ↑ → pressure ↓ → air in' and the reverse."],["Human Respiratory System: Structure and Function","人体呼吸系统：结构与功能",[["Nasal cavity: hairs trap dust; mucus traps microorganisms; blood capillaries warm the air; moistens air. Pharynx → larynx (vocal cords) → trachea.","鼻腔：鼻毛挡尘、黏液粘住微生物、毛细血管暖气、湿润"],["Trachea: C-shaped cartilage rings keep it open; ciliated epithelium sweeps mucus with trapped dust upwards; goblet cells secrete mucus.","气管：C形软骨环保持通畅；纤毛上皮向上扫出黏液；杯状细胞分泌黏液"],["Bronchi → bronchioles → alveoli (air sacs). Lungs are protected by the rib cage; pleural membranes with pleural fluid reduce friction.","支气管→细支气管→肺泡；胸膜与胸膜液减少摩擦"],["Alveoli: about 300 million; wall one cell thick; moist inner lining (with surfactant); covered by a network of capillaries; very large total surface area (about 70 m²).","肺泡：约3亿个；壁一层细胞；湿润；毛细血管网；总面积大"]],"","Tip: link each alveolar feature to 'faster diffusion'."],["Gas Exchange and Transport of Gases","气体交换与运输",[["In the alveoli, oxygen diffuses from the air (high concentration) into the blood (low), and carbon dioxide diffuses from the blood into the alveolar air.","肺泡中O₂扩散入血，CO₂扩散入肺泡"],["Oxygen combines with haemoglobin in red blood cells to form oxyhaemoglobin (about 97% transported this way); in tissues oxyhaemoglobin releases oxygen to the cells.","氧与血红蛋白结合成氧合血红蛋白；在组织处释放"],["Carbon dioxide is transported mainly as hydrogen carbonate ions in the plasma (about 70%), some bound to haemoglobin and some dissolved in plasma.","CO₂主要以碳酸氢根离子随血浆运输(约70%)"],["Inhaled air: O₂ 21%, CO₂ 0.04%, N₂ 78%, less water vapour. Exhaled air: O₂ about 16%, CO₂ about 4%, N₂ 78%, saturated with water vapour and warmer.","吸入气：O₂ 21%、CO₂ 0.04%；呼出气：O₂约16%、CO₂约4%、水汽饱和"],["Limewater turns cloudy faster with exhaled air, showing it has more CO₂.","呼出气使石灰水更快变浑浊"]],"","Tip: both gases move by diffusion — no ATP is needed."],["Health Issues of the Respiratory System (1)","呼吸系统健康问题（1）",[["Smoking: tar (carcinogen, destroys cilia), nicotine (addictive, raises blood pressure), carbon monoxide (binds haemoglobin to form carboxyhaemoglobin, reducing oxygen transport).","吸烟：焦油致癌破坏纤毛；尼古丁成瘾升血压；一氧化碳与血红蛋白结合"],["Asthma: bronchioles narrow due to allergens (pollen, dust, smoke); wheezing and breathlessness; treated with inhalers (bronchodilators).","哮喘：过敏原使细支气管收缩；喘息；用吸入器"],["Bronchitis: inflamed bronchi with excess mucus and persistent cough; caused by smoking, infection or pollution.","支气管炎：支气管发炎、黏液多、咳嗽"],["Emphysema: alveolar walls break down, reducing the surface area; breathlessness; mainly due to long-term smoking.","肺气肿：肺泡壁破坏、面积减少"]],"","Tip: cause → effect → prevention for every disease."],["Health Issues of the Respiratory System (2)","呼吸系统健康问题（2）",[["Lung cancer: uncontrolled division of lung cells due to carcinogens such as tar; symptoms include chronic cough and blood in sputum.","肺癌：焦油等致癌物使细胞失控分裂；慢性咳嗽、痰中带血"],["Tuberculosis (TB): caused by bacteria Mycobacterium tuberculosis, spread by droplets; prevent with BCG vaccine and treatment with antibiotics.","结核病：结核杆菌、飞沫传播；卡介苗预防，抗生素治疗"],["Pneumonia: infection of the alveoli by bacteria or viruses; alveoli fill with fluid.","肺炎：肺泡感染积液"],["Prevention: do not smoke, avoid polluted air (haze, wear masks), exercise regularly, vaccinate, ensure ventilation, regular medical check-ups.","预防：不吸烟、避免空气污染（戴口罩）、运动、接种、通风、体检"]],"","Tip: air pollutants — CO, SO₂, NO₂, particulates (PM2.5) — worsen asthma and bronchitis."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Respiratory system (Sistem respirasi); Alveolus (Alveolus); Trachea (Trakea); Bronchus (Bronkus)","呼吸系统；肺泡；气管；支气管"],["Diaphragm (Diafragma); Intercostal muscle (Otot interkostal); Rib cage (Sangkar rusuk)","膈肌；肋间肌；胸廓"],["Gill (Insang); Spiracle (Spirakel); Trachea of insect (Trakea serangga); Counter-current (Arus lawan)","鳃；气门；昆虫气管；逆流"],["Haemoglobin (Hemoglobin); Asthma (Asma); Emphysema (Emfisema); Bronchitis (Bronkitis)","血红蛋白；哮喘；肺气肿；支气管炎"]],"","Tip: 'insang' = gills."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying 'air is sucked in by the lungs' — the lungs have no muscles; air enters because the volume of the thoracic cavity increases and the pressure drops.","肺没有肌肉，空气进入是因胸腔容积增大、压力降低"],["Confusing the changes in the diaphragm and ribs for inhalation and exhalation.","混淆吸气呼气时膈肌肋骨变化"],["Insect tracheoles: oxygen goes directly to cells; blood does not carry oxygen.","昆虫微气管直接供氧"],["Forgetting counter-current flow in the gills of fish.","忘记鱼鳃逆流"],["Writing 'carbon monoxide combines with oxygen' — it binds permanently to haemoglobin.","一氧化碳与血红蛋白结合，不是与氧"]],"","Tip: draw the diagram of inhalation and exhalation, with arrows for rib and diaphragm movement."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: State two adaptations of alveoli for gas exchange. J: Wall one cell thick; moist; rich capillary network; large surface area.","问：肺泡两项适应？答：壁薄、湿润、毛细血管丰富、面积大"],["S: What happens to the diaphragm during inhalation? J: It contracts and flattens.","问：吸气时膈肌？答：收缩变平"],["S: Why do fish use counter-current flow? J: To maintain a concentration gradient and absorb more oxygen.","问：鱼为何用逆流？答：保持浓度梯度，吸收更多氧"],["S: How does carbon monoxide affect the body? J: It binds haemoglobin, forming carboxyhaemoglobin, so less oxygen is carried.","问：一氧化碳危害？答：与血红蛋白结合，运氧减少"],["S: Which structure in the trachea sweeps dust upwards? J: Cilia of the ciliated epithelium.","问：气管内何物把灰尘扫上去？答：纤毛上皮的纤毛"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-9":[["The Human Digestive System","人体消化系统",[["Alimentary canal: mouth → pharynx → oesophagus → stomach → small intestine (duodenum, jejunum, ileum) → large intestine (colon, rectum) → anus.","消化道：口→咽→食道→胃→小肠→大肠→肛门"],["Accessory organs: salivary glands, liver, gall bladder and pancreas (food does not pass through them).","辅助器官：唾液腺、肝、胆囊、胰"],["Peristalsis: wave-like contractions of the muscles of the alimentary canal push food along.","蠕动：消化道肌肉波浪收缩推送食物"],["Digestion is the breakdown of large insoluble food molecules into small soluble molecules that can be absorbed. Mechanical digestion: chewing, churning, bile emulsification. Chemical digestion: enzymes.","消化：把不溶大分子变成可吸收小分子；机械与化学消化"]],"","Tip: the liver, pancreas and gall bladder are not part of the alimentary canal."],["Digestion in the Mouth and Stomach","口腔与胃的消化",[["Mouth: teeth chew food (mechanical); saliva contains salivary amylase, which digests starch to maltose at about pH 7; the tongue forms a bolus.","口腔：牙齿咀嚼；唾液淀粉酶把淀粉分解成麦芽糖(pH约7)"],["Stomach: muscular walls churn food; gastric glands secrete gastric juice containing hydrochloric acid (pH about 2; kills bacteria and activates pepsin), pepsin (protein → polypeptides) and mucus (protects the stomach wall).","胃：肌肉搅拌；胃液含盐酸(杀菌、激活胃蛋白酶)、胃蛋白酶、黏液"],["Food becomes a semi-liquid called chyme, which is released gradually into the duodenum.","食物成为食糜，逐渐进入十二指肠"],["Rennin (in infants) clots milk protein.","凝乳酶使乳蛋白凝固（婴儿）"]],"","Tip: pepsin works at acidic pH; amylase in the mouth works at neutral pH."],["Digestion in the Small Intestine","小肠的消化",[["Bile (made in the liver, stored in the gall bladder): contains no enzymes; emulsifies fats into small droplets (larger surface area for lipase) and neutralises the acidic chyme (provides optimum pH for enzymes).","胆汁：无酶；乳化脂肪、中和酸性食糜"],["Pancreatic juice (alkaline): pancreatic amylase (starch → maltose), trypsin (protein → peptides), lipase (fats → fatty acids + glycerol).","胰液：胰淀粉酶、胰蛋白酶、脂肪酶"],["Intestinal juice (brush border enzymes): maltase (maltose → glucose), sucrase (sucrose → glucose + fructose), lactase (lactose → glucose + galactose), peptidase (peptides → amino acids), lipase.","肠液：麦芽糖酶、蔗糖酶、乳糖酶、肽酶、脂肪酶"],["End products: carbohydrates → glucose (and other monosaccharides); proteins → amino acids; fats → fatty acids and glycerol.","终产物：葡萄糖、氨基酸、脂肪酸和甘油"]],"","Tip: bile is not an enzyme — it emulsifies fats."],["Enzymes of Digestion: Summary Table","消化酶总表",[["Salivary amylase — mouth — starch → maltose. Pepsin — stomach — proteins → polypeptides.","唾液淀粉酶—口—淀粉→麦芽糖；胃蛋白酶—胃—蛋白→多肽"],["Pancreatic amylase — small intestine — starch → maltose. Trypsin — small intestine — proteins → peptides. Pancreatic lipase — fats → fatty acids + glycerol.","胰淀粉酶、胰蛋白酶、胰脂肪酶（小肠）"],["Maltase, sucrase, lactase — disaccharides → monosaccharides. Peptidase — peptides → amino acids.","麦芽糖酶、蔗糖酶、乳糖酶；肽酶"],["Optimum pH: salivary amylase 7; pepsin 2; pancreatic enzymes 8.","最适pH：唾液淀粉酶7；胃蛋白酶2；胰酶8"]],"","Tip: learn the enzyme, the source, the substrate and the product."],["Absorption in the Small Intestine","小肠的吸收",[["The ileum is adapted for absorption: very long (about 6 m); inner wall has folds, villi and microvilli → large surface area.","回肠适应吸收：长；有皱褶、绒毛、微绒毛"],["Villus wall is one cell thick (short diffusion distance); rich network of blood capillaries; lacteal (lymph vessel) for fats; muscles move the villus to mix contents.","绒毛壁一层细胞；毛细血管丰富；乳糜管；肌肉摆动"],["Glucose, amino acids, mineral salts and water-soluble vitamins are absorbed into the blood capillaries by diffusion and active transport (glucose and amino acids by active transport and facilitated diffusion).","葡萄糖、氨基酸、矿物质、水溶性维生素进入毛细血管"],["Fatty acids and glycerol are absorbed into the epithelial cells, recombine to form triglycerides and enter the lacteal; later they reach the bloodstream.","脂肪酸和甘油吸收后重组为三酸甘油酯进入乳糜管"],["Large intestine: absorbs water and mineral salts; bacteria make vitamin K; forms faeces.","大肠：吸收水和矿物质；细菌合成维生素K；形成粪便"]],"","Tip: say 'large surface area, thin wall, capillaries and lacteals' when describing the villus."],["Assimilation","同化作用",[["Blood from the small intestine goes to the liver through the hepatic portal vein.","血液经肝门静脉到肝脏"],["Glucose: used for respiration; excess converted to glycogen (stored in the liver and muscles) by insulin; blood glucose level is regulated.","葡萄糖：供呼吸；多余转为糖原储存"],["Amino acids: used to synthesise proteins (enzymes, plasma proteins, tissues); excess are deaminated in the liver; the nitrogen part forms urea.","氨基酸：合成蛋白质；多余的在肝脏脱氨基，形成尿素"],["Fats: used for energy, as part of cell membranes, stored in adipose tissue (insulation and protection).","脂肪：供能、构成膜、储存于脂肪组织"],["The liver also detoxifies drugs and alcohol, stores vitamins and iron, and makes bile.","肝脏解毒、储存维生素与铁、制造胆汁"]],"","Tip: assimilation = absorbed food is used by the body's cells."],["Egestion and Constipation","排遗与便秘",[["Faeces: undigested food (cellulose/fibre), dead cells, bacteria, bile pigments and water; stored in the rectum and expelled through the anus.","粪便：未消化食物(纤维)、死细胞、细菌、胆色素、水"],["Egestion (removal of undigested food) is different from excretion (removal of metabolic wastes such as urea, CO₂).","排遗≠排泄"],["Constipation: hard faeces, difficult to pass; due to low fibre diet, insufficient water, lack of exercise.","便秘：粪便硬；缺纤维、缺水、缺运动"],["Prevention: eat fibre-rich food (vegetables, fruits, whole grains), drink enough water, exercise.","预防：多吃纤维、喝水、运动"]],"","Tip: fibre adds bulk and stimulates peristalsis."],["Balanced Diet: Classes of Food","均衡饮食：食物类别",[["Carbohydrates: energy (rice, bread). Proteins: growth and repair (fish, eggs, beans). Lipids: energy, insulation. Water; dietary fibre.","碳水化合物供能；蛋白质生长修复；脂质供能保温；水；纤维"],["Vitamin A: night vision — deficiency: night blindness. Vitamin C: healthy gums, wound healing — scurvy. Vitamin D: absorb calcium — rickets. Vitamin B₁ — beriberi. Vitamin K — blood clotting.","维生素A夜盲；C坏血病；D佝偻病；B₁脚气病；K凝血"],["Minerals: calcium (bones, teeth, clotting), iron (haemoglobin — anaemia), iodine (thyroxine — goitre), phosphorus (bones, ATP), sodium and potassium (nerve impulses).","矿物质：钙、铁（贫血）、碘（甲状腺肿）、磷、钠钾"],["Malaysian Healthy Plate (Suku-Suku Separuh): ¼ carbohydrate, ¼ protein, ½ fruits and vegetables.","马来西亚健康餐盘：¼碳水、¼蛋白、½蔬果"]],"","Tip: match each vitamin with its function AND deficiency disease."],["Energy Value, BMI and Diet Planning","能量值、BMI与饮食规划",[["Energy values: carbohydrate and protein ≈ 17 kJ g⁻¹; fat ≈ 38 kJ g⁻¹.","能量值：糖类蛋白质17 kJ/g；脂肪38 kJ/g"],["Energy requirement depends on age, gender, body size, activity level and health (pregnancy, illness).","能量需求取决于年龄、性别、体型、活动量与健康状况"],["BMI = mass (kg) ÷ height² (m²). Common classification: below 18.5 underweight; 18.5–24.9 normal; 25–29.9 overweight; 30 and above obese.","BMI＝体重÷身高²；<18.5过轻；18.5–24.9正常；25–29.9过重；≥30肥胖"],["Example: 70 kg, 1.75 m → BMI = 70 ÷ 3.0625 = 22.9 (normal).","例：70 kg，1.75 m→BMI 22.9（正常）"],["Food test for vitamin C: add DCPIP solution; blue DCPIP is decolourised by vitamin C (the more drops decolourised, the more vitamin C).","维生素C测试：DCPIP褪色"]],"","Tip: calculate BMI with height in metres, not centimetres."],["Health Issues Related to Digestion and Eating Habits","消化与饮食习惯相关健康问题",[["Obesity: excess energy intake stored as fat; leads to heart disease, diabetes, hypertension.","肥胖：能量摄入过多；导致心脏病、糖尿病、高血压"],["Anorexia nervosa: refusing food due to fear of gaining weight; bulimia nervosa: binge eating followed by vomiting.","厌食症；暴食症"],["Gastritis and peptic ulcer: stomach lining inflamed/eroded by excess acid or Helicobacter pylori; avoid irregular meals, spicy food and stress.","胃炎、胃溃疡：胃酸过多或幽门螺杆菌"],["Food poisoning and diarrhoea: caused by contaminated food and water (Salmonella, Vibrio cholerae); practise food hygiene.","食物中毒、腹泻：食物水污染"],["Kwashiorkor (protein deficiency) and marasmus (energy and protein deficiency) in malnutrition.","夸休可尔症与消瘦症"]],"","Tip: give a cause, a symptom and a preventive measure."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Digestion (Pencernaan); Absorption (Penyerapan); Assimilation (Asimilasi); Egestion (Penyahtinjaan)","消化；吸收；同化；排遗"],["Villus (Vilus); Lacteal (Lakteal); Bile (Hempedu); Peristalsis (Peristalsis)","绒毛；乳糜管；胆汁；蠕动"],["Balanced diet (Gizi seimbang); Fibre (Serat); Body mass index (Indeks jisim badan)","均衡饮食；纤维；BMI"],["Amylase (Amilase); Protease (Protease); Lipase (Lipase); Pepsin (Pepsin)","淀粉酶；蛋白酶；脂肪酶；胃蛋白酶"]],"","Tip: 'gizi seimbang' = balanced diet."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying bile digests fat — it emulsifies fat (no enzyme).","胆汁不是消化酶，是乳化脂肪"],["Confusing absorption (into blood/lymph), assimilation (use by cells) and egestion (removal of faeces).","混淆吸收、同化、排遗"],["Putting fatty acids and glycerol into blood capillaries — they enter the lacteal.","脂肪酸和甘油进乳糜管"],["Writing the end products of protein digestion as 'polypeptides' — the end product is amino acids.","蛋白质终产物是氨基酸"],["Using cm instead of m when calculating BMI.","BMI算错单位"]],"","Tip: for enzyme tables write enzyme, source, substrate, product."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: State the function of bile. J: Emulsifies fats and neutralises acidic chyme.","问：胆汁功能？答：乳化脂肪、中和酸性食糜"],["S: Name the end products of digestion of starch, protein and fat. J: Glucose; amino acids; fatty acids and glycerol.","问：淀粉、蛋白、脂肪终产物？答：葡萄糖；氨基酸；脂肪酸和甘油"],["S: Explain how the villus is adapted for absorption. J: Large surface area, one-cell-thick wall, rich capillaries and a lacteal, muscle for movement.","问：绒毛如何适应吸收？答：面积大、壁薄、毛细血管与乳糜管丰富、可摆动"],["S: What causes scurvy? J: Deficiency of vitamin C.","问：坏血病原因？答：缺乏维生素C"],["S: Calculate the BMI of a person of 60 kg and 1.5 m. J: 60 ÷ 2.25 = 26.7 (overweight).","问：60 kg、1.5 m的BMI？答：26.7（过重）"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-10":[["Types of Circulatory Systems","循环系统的类型",[["Large organisms have a small surface area to volume ratio, so they need a transport system to carry oxygen, nutrients, wastes and hormones.","大型生物表面积/体积比小，需要运输系统"],["Open circulatory system (insects): blood (haemolymph) flows out of the heart into the body cavity (haemocoel) and bathes the tissues directly; low pressure; does not carry oxygen.","开放式：血淋巴流入体腔直接浸润组织；压力低；不运氧"],["Closed circulatory system (earthworm, fish, humans): blood flows only inside blood vessels; higher pressure and faster, more efficient transport.","封闭式：血液只在血管内流动，高压快速高效"],["Single circulation (fish): the blood passes through the heart once per complete circuit (heart with 2 chambers: 1 atrium and 1 ventricle); pressure drops after the gills.","单循环(鱼)：血液每周经心脏一次；心脏2室"],["Double circulation (mammals): the blood passes through the heart twice per circuit: pulmonary circulation (heart → lungs → heart) and systemic circulation (heart → body → heart); 4-chambered heart; oxygenated and deoxygenated blood do not mix.","双循环(哺乳)：肺循环+体循环；心脏4室；含氧与缺氧血液不混合"]],"","Tip: double circulation maintains high pressure to the body after the lungs."],["The Human Heart and Blood Vessels","人心脏与血管",[["Heart: 4 chambers — right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, left ventricle; septum separates left and right sides. Left ventricle has the thickest wall (pumps blood to the whole body).","心脏4室；左心室壁最厚"],["Valves: tricuspid valve (right), bicuspid/mitral valve (left) and semilunar valves prevent backflow; tendons (chordae tendineae) hold the valves; coronary arteries supply the heart muscle.","瓣膜防回流；腱索；冠状动脉供应心肌"],["Flow: vena cava → right atrium → right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs → pulmonary vein → left atrium → left ventricle → aorta → body.","路径：腔静脉→右心房→右心室→肺动脉→肺→肺静脉→左心房→左心室→主动脉"],["Artery: thick, muscular, elastic wall; narrow lumen; high pressure; carries blood away from the heart. Vein: thin wall; wide lumen; valves; low pressure. Capillary: one cell thick wall; site of exchange.","动脉：壁厚有弹性；静脉：壁薄有瓣；毛细血管：一层细胞，交换场所"],["Pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood; pulmonary vein carries oxygenated blood (exceptions to the rule).","肺动脉含缺氧血；肺静脉含氧血（例外）"]],"","Tip: arteries = away from the heart; veins = to the heart."],["Composition and Functions of Blood","血液成分与功能",[["Plasma (55%): water, plasma proteins (albumin, fibrinogen), glucose, amino acids, mineral ions, hormones, urea, CO₂. Transports substances and heat.","血浆(55%)：水、蛋白、葡萄糖、激素等；运输物质与热"],["Red blood cells: biconcave, no nucleus, contain haemoglobin; transport oxygen (about 5 million per mm³); made in bone marrow; live about 120 days.","红细胞：双凹无核，含血红蛋白运氧；骨髓制造；寿命约120天"],["White blood cells: phagocytes engulf pathogens; lymphocytes produce antibodies; fewer than red blood cells.","白细胞：吞噬细胞吞噬病原体；淋巴细胞产生抗体"],["Platelets: cell fragments that help blood clot.","血小板：协助凝血"],["Functions of blood: transport, protection (immunity, clotting), regulation of body temperature and pH.","功能：运输、保护、调节体温与pH"]],"","Tip: red blood cells — oxygen; white — defence; platelets — clotting."],["Mechanism of the Heartbeat","心跳机制",[["Cardiac muscle is myogenic: it contracts on its own without nerve stimulation.","心肌具自发性收缩"],["The sinoatrial (SA) node in the wall of the right atrium is the pacemaker; it sends electrical impulses that make both atria contract (atrial systole).","窦房结是起搏点，使两心房收缩"],["The impulse reaches the atrioventricular (AV) node, which delays it slightly so the ventricles fill; then it passes down the bundle of His and the Purkinje fibres → both ventricles contract from the base (apex) upwards (ventricular systole).","房室结延迟→希氏束→浦肯野纤维→心室自心尖向上收缩"],["Heart rate is regulated by the medulla (autonomic nervous system) and hormones: sympathetic nerves and adrenaline increase the rate; the vagus nerve decreases it.","心率由延髓/自主神经与激素调节：肾上腺素提高；迷走神经降低"],["Normal resting heart rate about 72 beats per minute; blood pressure about 120/80 mmHg (systolic/diastolic).","正常静息心率约72次/分；血压约120/80 mmHg"]],"","Tip: SA node → atria; AV node → bundle of His → Purkinje fibres → ventricles."],["Mechanism of Blood Clotting","凝血机制",[["When a blood vessel is damaged, platelets stick to the wound and release thromboplastin.","血管受损，血小板释放凝血活酶"],["Thromboplastin + calcium ions (and vitamin K) convert prothrombin (inactive) to thrombin (active enzyme).","凝血活酶+钙离子(维生素K)：凝血酶原→凝血酶"],["Thrombin converts soluble fibrinogen to insoluble fibrin threads, which form a mesh that traps blood cells to form a clot (scab).","凝血酶：纤维蛋白原→纤维蛋白，网住血细胞形成凝块"],["Importance: prevents excessive blood loss and entry of pathogens. Haemophilia: inherited disorder where blood clots very slowly. Thrombosis: a clot forms inside an unbroken vessel.","重要性：防失血与感染；血友病：凝血慢；血栓：血管内形成凝块"]],"","Tip: prothrombin → thrombin; fibrinogen → fibrin."],["Human Blood Groups","人类血型",[["ABO system: Group A — antigen A on red cells, anti-B antibody in plasma. Group B — antigen B, anti-A. Group AB — antigens A and B, no antibodies. Group O — no antigens, anti-A and anti-B.","ABO血型：A型抗原A，抗体anti-B；B型相反；AB型两抗原无抗体；O型无抗原，两抗体"],["Group O is the universal donor (no antigens); group AB is the universal recipient (no antibodies).","O型万能供血者；AB型万能受血者"],["Agglutination (clumping) occurs if the recipient's antibodies meet the donor's antigens — can block blood vessels.","抗原抗体相遇发生凝集"],["Rhesus factor: Rh-positive (antigen D present) and Rh-negative. An Rh⁻ mother carrying an Rh⁺ baby may form antibodies, which can harm a second Rh⁺ baby (haemolytic disease of the newborn).","Rh血型：Rh⁻母亲怀Rh⁺胎儿，二胎可能受害"]],"","Tip: draw a table of antigens and antibodies for each group."],["Health Issues of the Circulatory System","血液循环系统的健康问题",[["Atherosclerosis: fatty deposits (cholesterol) build up in artery walls, narrowing the lumen; may cause blood clots.","动脉粥样硬化：胆固醇沉积使管腔变窄"],["Coronary heart disease: blocked coronary arteries → heart muscle lacks oxygen → angina or heart attack. Stroke: blocked or burst artery in the brain. Hypertension: persistently high blood pressure.","冠心病；中风；高血压"],["Anaemia: low haemoglobin (iron deficiency); leukaemia: cancer of white blood cells.","贫血；白血病"],["Prevention: balanced diet low in saturated fats and salt, regular exercise, no smoking, controlling stress, regular check-ups; blood donation saves lives.","预防：低盐低饱和脂肪饮食、运动、不吸烟、减压、体检；献血"]],"","Tip: causes → effects → prevention; do not mix up atherosclerosis and arteriosclerosis wording."],["The Lymphatic System","淋巴系统",[["Tissue fluid: forms when blood plasma (without large proteins and cells) leaks out of capillaries; it bathes the cells to deliver oxygen and nutrients and collect wastes.","组织液：血浆渗出毛细血管，浸润细胞"],["Some tissue fluid returns to the blood capillaries; the rest enters lymph capillaries and becomes lymph, which flows through lymph vessels (with valves) to lymph nodes and then joins the blood near the heart.","部分回毛细血管；其余成淋巴，经淋巴管、淋巴结，最后汇入血液"],["Functions: returns tissue fluid to the blood (prevents oedema); defence — lymph nodes contain lymphocytes and phagocytes that destroy pathogens; transports fats from the lacteals.","功能：回收组织液防水肿；淋巴结防御；运输脂肪"],["Lymph flows by the contraction of skeletal muscles and one-way valves, not by a pump.","淋巴靠骨骼肌收缩与瓣膜流动，无泵"]],"","Tip: lymph is similar to plasma but contains fewer proteins and has many lymphocytes."],["Health Issues of the Lymphatic System","淋巴系统健康问题",[["Lymphoedema: swelling due to blocked lymph vessels (after surgery, infection).","淋巴水肿：淋巴管阻塞"],["Filariasis (elephantiasis): caused by Wuchereria bancrofti worms spread by mosquitoes; blocks lymph vessels leading to swelling of legs.","丝虫病（象皮病）：丝虫经蚊传播阻塞淋巴管"],["Lymphoma: cancer of the lymphatic tissue. Swollen lymph nodes often indicate infection.","淋巴瘤；淋巴结肿大常示感染"],["Prevention of filariasis: control mosquitoes, use repellent and bed nets, treatment of infected people.","预防：防蚊、驱蚊、治疗"]],"","Tip: link the cause (parasite) with the effect (blocked vessel) and the preventive measure."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Circulatory system (Sistem peredaran); Artery (Arteri); Vein (Vena); Capillary (Kapilari)","循环系统；动脉；静脉；毛细血管"],["Atrium (Atrium); Ventricle (Ventrikel); Valve (Injap); Pacemaker (Perentak jantung)","心房；心室；瓣膜；起搏点"],["Blood clotting (Pembekuan darah); Platelet (Platelet); Fibrinogen (Fibrinogen); Antibody (Antibodi)","凝血；血小板；纤维蛋白原；抗体"],["Lymph (Limfa); Tissue fluid (Bendalir tisu); Blood group (Kumpulan darah)","淋巴；组织液；血型"]],"","Tip: 'vena' = vein."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying arteries always carry oxygenated blood — the pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood.","动脉不一定含氧：肺动脉含缺氧血"],["Confusing the left and right sides of the heart in a diagram (the diagram is viewed as facing the person).","图示左右心要从被观察者角度"],["Mixing up prothrombin/thrombin and fibrinogen/fibrin in the clotting sequence.","混淆凝血各物质"],["Group O has no antigens, but has both antibodies; AB has both antigens, no antibodies.","O型无抗原有两抗体；AB型相反"],["Forgetting that the SA node, not the brain, starts each heartbeat.","每次心跳由窦房结启动"]],"","Tip: for sequences (heartbeat, clotting, blood flow) use numbered steps."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Which chamber has the thickest wall? Why? J: Left ventricle; it pumps blood at high pressure to the whole body.","问：哪个腔壁最厚？为何？答：左心室，需把血液以高压送往全身"],["S: Name the pacemaker of the heart. J: The sinoatrial (SA) node.","问：心脏起搏点？答：窦房结"],["S: What is the role of fibrin in blood clotting? J: Forms a mesh of insoluble threads that traps blood cells to form a clot.","问：纤维蛋白作用？答：形成网状不溶丝，网住血细胞形成凝块"],["S: Why can a person with group O blood donate to others? J: Red blood cells have no antigens A or B, so no agglutination occurs.","问：O型为何可供血给他人？答：红细胞无A、B抗原，不凝集"],["S: Give two functions of the lymphatic system. J: Returns tissue fluid to the blood; destroys pathogens in the lymph nodes; transports fats.","问：淋巴系统两功能？答：回收组织液；淋巴结防御；运输脂肪"]],"",""]],"bio|T4-11":[["Body Defence: Overview and First Line", "身体防御：概览与第一道防线", [["Pathogens (bacteria, viruses, fungi, protozoa) cause disease; the body has three lines of defence.", "病原体致病；身体有三道防线"], ["First line (non-specific, prevents entry): intact skin (keratin layer is a physical barrier); sebum and sweat (acidic, kills microbes).", "第一道（非特异性）：皮肤、皮脂和汗液"], ["Mucus in the nose and trachea traps microbes; cilia sweep the mucus upward; lysozyme in tears and saliva digests bacterial cell walls.", "黏液、纤毛、溶菌酶"], ["Hydrochloric acid in the stomach (pH about 2) kills most microbes swallowed with food.", "胃酸杀菌"], ["Blood clotting at a wound seals the skin so pathogens cannot enter.", "凝血封住伤口"]], "", "Tip: first line = stops entry; second and third lines = act after entry."], ["Second and Third Line of Defence", "第二、第三道防线", [["Second line (non-specific, inside the body): phagocytosis by white blood cells (neutrophils, macrophages); inflammation; fever; interferon.", "第二道（非特异性）：吞噬、炎症、发热、干扰素"], ["Phagocytosis: the phagocyte engulfs the pathogen into a vacuole, lysosomes fuse with it and digest it with enzymes.", "吞噬：包裹→溶酶体消化"], ["Inflammation: damaged tissue releases histamine; blood vessels widen and become more permeable, so more phagocytes reach the site (redness, heat, swelling, pain).", "炎症：组胺使血管扩张、通透性增加"], ["Fever slows microbe growth and speeds up defence reactions; interferon is released by virus-infected cells to protect neighbouring cells.", "发热；干扰素保护邻近细胞"], ["Third line (specific): lymphocytes produce antibodies against a particular antigen and form memory cells.", "第三道（特异性）：淋巴细胞产生抗体并形成记忆细胞"]], "", "Tip: specific = targets one antigen only; non-specific = same response to any pathogen."], ["Lymphocytes: B Cells and T Cells", "淋巴细胞：B 细胞与 T 细胞", [["Antigen: a foreign substance (usually protein on a pathogen's surface) that triggers an immune response.", "抗原：触发免疫反应的外来物质"], ["B lymphocytes (made and matured in bone marrow): on stimulation they divide and differentiate into plasma cells (secrete antibodies) and memory B cells.", "B 细胞：分化为浆细胞和记忆 B 细胞"], ["T lymphocytes (mature in the thymus): helper T cells activate B cells and phagocytes; cytotoxic (killer) T cells destroy infected cells and cancer cells; memory T cells remember the antigen.", "T 细胞：辅助 T、细胞毒 T、记忆 T"], ["Humoral immunity = antibodies in body fluids (B cells); cell-mediated immunity = T cells attack cells directly.", "体液免疫（B）；细胞免疫（T）"]], "", "Tip: B cells → antibodies; T cells → destroy infected cells."], ["Antibodies and Their Action", "抗体及其作用", [["Antibody: a Y-shaped protein made by plasma cells; each antibody has binding sites that fit only one specific antigen (like a lock and key).", "抗体：Y 形蛋白质，与特定抗原互补结合"], ["Neutralisation: antibodies bind toxins or viruses so they cannot harm cells or enter them.", "中和：使毒素/病毒失效"], ["Agglutination: antibodies clump pathogens together so phagocytes can engulf them more easily.", "凝集：使病原体聚集"], ["Precipitation: antibodies make soluble antigens insoluble so they settle out and are removed.", "沉淀：可溶抗原变不溶"], ["Opsonisation: antibodies coat pathogens, making them easier for phagocytes to recognise and ingest.", "调理：标记病原体便于吞噬"]], "", "Tip: name the action AND say what happens to the pathogen."], ["Primary and Secondary Immune Response", "初次与再次免疫反应", [["Primary response (first exposure): slow, a lag of several days before antibodies appear; low concentration of antibodies; memory cells formed.", "初次：慢、抗体量少，形成记忆细胞"], ["Secondary response (second exposure): memory cells respond quickly; antibodies appear sooner, in much larger amounts and last longer.", "再次：快、量多、持久"], ["This is why booster doses give stronger and longer protection.", "加强针的原理"], ["Graph: antibody concentration against time shows a small, late peak (primary) and a much higher, earlier peak (secondary).", "图：初次峰小而晚；再次峰高而早"]], "", "Tip: when you draw the graph, label both axes and both peaks."], ["Types of Immunity", "免疫的类型", [["Active natural immunity: body makes its own antibodies after infection by a pathogen; long-lasting.", "主动自然：感染后自己产生抗体"], ["Active artificial immunity: body makes antibodies after a vaccine; long-lasting.", "主动人工：接种疫苗"], ["Passive natural immunity: antibodies passed from mother to baby through the placenta and breast milk (colostrum); short-term.", "被动自然：胎盘和母乳传抗体"], ["Passive artificial immunity: ready-made antibodies injected (antiserum, e.g. against snake venom or tetanus); immediate but short-term, no memory cells.", "被动人工：注射抗血清"], ["Active = body makes antibodies and memory cells; passive = antibodies are given, so protection is not lasting.", "主动有记忆细胞；被动无"]], "", "Tip: active = own antibodies; passive = borrowed antibodies."], ["Vaccination", "疫苗接种", [["A vaccine contains weakened or killed pathogens, or their antigens, which cause no disease but stimulate antibody and memory cell production.", "疫苗：减毒/灭活病原体或抗原"], ["Examples in the Malaysian immunisation programme: BCG (tuberculosis), hepatitis B, DPT (diphtheria, pertussis, tetanus), polio, MMR (measles, mumps, rubella), HPV.", "国家免疫计划例子"], ["Herd immunity: when most of the population is immune, the spread of disease is slowed and non-immune people are protected.", "群体免疫"], ["Vaccines are given in a schedule with booster doses so memory cells give a strong secondary response.", "按程序接种并加强"]], "", "Tip: vaccine = prevention; antiserum = treatment."], ["Health Issues Related to Human Immunity", "人体免疫相关健康问题", [["Allergy: an over-reaction of the immune system to harmless substances (allergens such as pollen, dust mites, food); histamine causes sneezing, rashes, swelling.", "过敏：对无害物质过度反应，释放组胺"], ["Autoimmune disease: the immune system attacks the body's own cells (e.g. rheumatoid arthritis, type 1 diabetes, lupus).", "自身免疫病：攻击自身细胞"], ["HIV/AIDS: HIV infects and destroys helper T cells, so the immune system weakens and the person gets opportunistic infections. Spread through blood, sexual contact and from mother to child; not by casual contact.", "艾滋病：HIV 破坏辅助 T 细胞"], ["Organ transplant: the recipient's immune system may reject the foreign organ, so tissue matching and immunosuppressant drugs are used.", "器官移植排斥"]], "", "Tip: HIV is the virus; AIDS is the syndrome that develops later."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Pathogen (Patogen); Antigen (Antigen); Antibody (Antibodi); Phagocytosis (Fagositosis)", "病原体；抗原；抗体；吞噬"], ["Lymphocyte (Limfosit); Plasma cell (Sel plasma); Memory cell (Sel memori)", "淋巴细胞；浆细胞；记忆细胞"], ["Agglutination (Aglutinasi); Precipitation (Pemendakan); Neutralisation (Peneutralan)", "凝集；沉淀；中和"], ["Vaccine (Vaksin); Active immunity (Keimunan aktif); Passive immunity (Keimunan pasif); Allergy (Alahan)", "疫苗；主动免疫；被动免疫；过敏"]], "", "Tip: 'keimunan' = immunity."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Confusing antigen (on the pathogen) with antibody (made by the body).", "混淆抗原与抗体"], ["Saying vaccines contain antibodies — they contain antigens (weakened or killed pathogens).", "疫苗含抗原而非抗体"], ["Saying antibiotics work on viruses; they work only on bacteria.", "抗生素对病毒无效"], ["Mixing up active and passive immunity: passive gives no memory cells.", "主动被动混淆"], ["Writing HIV and AIDS as the same thing.", "HIV 与 AIDS 不同"]], "", "Tip: for 'explain' questions give point + reason."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: What is the difference between an antigen and an antibody? J: An antigen is a foreign substance that triggers an immune response; an antibody is a protein made by plasma cells that binds a specific antigen.", "问：抗原与抗体区别？答：抗原是触发免疫的外来物；抗体是浆细胞产生、与其结合的蛋白质"], ["S: Why is the secondary response faster than the primary response? J: Memory cells already exist and quickly divide into plasma cells that make large amounts of antibody.", "问：再次反应为何更快？答：已有记忆细胞，迅速产生大量抗体"], ["S: Why does a vaccine give active immunity? J: The body makes its own antibodies and memory cells after the antigens are injected.", "问：疫苗为何是主动免疫？答：身体自己产生抗体和记忆细胞"], ["S: How does HIV weaken the body? J: It destroys helper T cells, so antibody production and the immune response fail.", "问：HIV 如何削弱身体？答：破坏辅助 T 细胞，免疫失效"], ["S: Give two examples of passive natural immunity. J: Antibodies passed through the placenta; antibodies in breast milk (colostrum).", "问：被动自然免疫两例？答：胎盘抗体；母乳抗体"]], "", ""]],"bio|T4-12":[["Coordination and Response", "协调与反应", [["Stimulus: a change in the environment detected by receptors; response: the reaction by an effector (muscle or gland).", "刺激由感受器接收；效应器（肌肉/腺体）做出反应"], ["Coordination pathway: stimulus → receptor → sensory neuron → central nervous system (CNS) → motor neuron → effector → response.", "协调路径"], ["Two systems coordinate the body: the nervous system (fast, short-lived, by electrical impulses) and the endocrine system (slower, longer-lasting, by hormones in the blood).", "神经系统快而短暂；内分泌慢而持久"]], "", "Tip: always write the pathway in order."], ["The Human Nervous System", "人体神经系统", [["Central nervous system (CNS) = brain + spinal cord; peripheral nervous system (PNS) = cranial and spinal nerves linking the CNS to the body.", "中枢=脑+脊髓；外周=脑神经和脊神经"], ["Cerebrum: thinking, memory, speech, voluntary actions, senses. Cerebellum: balance and muscle coordination. Medulla oblongata: involuntary actions (heartbeat, breathing). Hypothalamus: body temperature, water balance, hunger.", "大脑；小脑；延髓；下丘脑"], ["Spinal cord: carries impulses between body and brain; controls reflex actions.", "脊髓：传导并控制反射"], ["PNS: somatic (voluntary, to skeletal muscles) and autonomic (involuntary, to internal organs) — sympathetic prepares for 'fight or flight', parasympathetic restores rest.", "躯体与自主神经；交感与副交感"]], "", "Tip: sympathetic = speeds up; parasympathetic = slows down."], ["Neurons", "神经元", [["Neuron parts: cell body (nucleus), dendrites (receive impulses), axon (carries impulses away), myelin sheath (insulates and speeds up conduction), nodes of Ranvier.", "神经元结构：细胞体、树突、轴突、髓鞘、郎飞结"], ["Sensory neuron: receptor → CNS. Relay (interneuron): within CNS. Motor neuron: CNS → effector.", "感觉、联络、运动神经元"], ["Myelinated neurons conduct impulses faster because the impulse jumps between nodes of Ranvier.", "髓鞘使冲动在郎飞结间跳跃，传导更快"]], "", "Tip: dendrite = in; axon = out."], ["Synapse and Transmission of Impulses", "突触与冲动传递", [["Synapse: the junction between two neurons, with a small gap called the synaptic cleft.", "突触：两神经元之间的连接，有突触间隙"], ["1 Impulse reaches the axon terminal. 2 Synaptic vesicles release neurotransmitter (e.g. acetylcholine) into the cleft. 3 It diffuses across and binds receptors on the next neuron. 4 A new impulse starts in the next neuron.", "四步：到达→释放递质→扩散结合受体→产生新冲动"], ["Impulses pass in one direction only because neurotransmitters are released only by the presynaptic neuron.", "单向传递"], ["Enzymes then break down the neurotransmitter so the response stops.", "酶分解递质，终止反应"]], "", "Tip: an impulse is electrical; across the synapse it is chemical."], ["Voluntary and Involuntary Actions", "随意与不随意动作", [["Voluntary action: controlled by the cerebrum, e.g. kicking a ball; pathway goes through the brain.", "随意动作：大脑控制"], ["Reflex action: fast, automatic, protective, not controlled by the brain, e.g. withdrawing the hand from a hot object.", "反射：快速、自动、保护性"], ["Reflex arc: stimulus → receptor → sensory neuron → spinal cord (relay neuron) → motor neuron → effector → response. The brain is informed afterwards, so we feel the pain later.", "反射弧：经脊髓；之后才通知大脑"], ["Other reflexes: blinking, knee jerk, pupil constriction in bright light.", "其他反射：眨眼、膝跳、瞳孔缩小"]], "", "Tip: reflex goes through the spinal cord, not the brain."], ["Health Issues of the Nervous System", "神经系统健康问题", [["Alzheimer's disease: neurons degenerate, causing memory loss and confusion.", "阿尔茨海默病：神经元退化，记忆丧失"], ["Parkinson's disease: loss of dopamine-producing neurons, causing tremors and stiff muscles.", "帕金森病：多巴胺神经元减少，颤抖僵硬"], ["Epilepsy: sudden abnormal electrical activity in the brain, causing seizures.", "癫痫：脑异常放电"], ["Effects of drugs and alcohol: slow reactions and damage neurons; caffeine and nicotine are stimulants.", "药物与酒精影响神经系统"]], "", "Tip: link each disease to the neuron change that causes it."], ["The Endocrine System", "内分泌系统", [["Endocrine glands are ductless; they secrete hormones directly into the blood, which carries them to target organs.", "内分泌腺无导管，激素入血"], ["Pituitary (master gland): growth hormone, ADH, TSH, FSH, LH. Thyroid: thyroxine (metabolic rate). Pancreas (islets of Langerhans): insulin and glucagon. Adrenal: adrenaline. Ovary: oestrogen, progesterone. Testis: testosterone.", "垂体、甲状腺、胰岛、肾上腺、卵巢、睾丸"], ["Negative feedback: when the level of a hormone or substance is too high, secretion is reduced, keeping conditions stable.", "负反馈调节"], ["Nervous vs endocrine: impulses vs hormones; fast vs slow; short vs long effect; specific target vs target organs.", "神经与内分泌比较"]], "", "Tip: hormone = chemical messenger carried in blood."], ["Blood Glucose Control", "血糖调节", [["After a meal, blood glucose rises → pancreas secretes insulin → liver converts glucose to glycogen and cells take up more glucose → blood glucose falls.", "餐后：胰岛素使血糖下降"], ["When blood glucose is low → pancreas secretes glucagon → liver converts glycogen back to glucose → blood glucose rises.", "血糖低：胰高血糖素使其上升"], ["Diabetes mellitus: type 1 — pancreas makes little or no insulin; type 2 — cells respond poorly to insulin. Symptoms: frequent urination, thirst, tiredness.", "糖尿病：1 型缺胰岛素；2 型胰岛素抵抗"]], "", "Tip: insulin lowers; glucagon raises."], ["Health Issues of the Endocrine System", "内分泌系统健康问题", [["Diabetes mellitus: managed with diet, exercise, medication or insulin injections.", "糖尿病：饮食、运动、药物或胰岛素"], ["Goitre: swollen thyroid caused by lack of iodine; prevented by iodised salt.", "甲状腺肿：缺碘；食用加碘盐"], ["Gigantism and dwarfism: too much / too little growth hormone in childhood; acromegaly: too much in adults.", "巨人症、侏儒症、肢端肥大症"]], "", "Tip: name the hormone AND whether it is too much or too little."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Stimulus (Rangsangan); Receptor (Reseptor); Effector (Efektor); Neuron (Neuron); Synapse (Sinaps)", "刺激；感受器；效应器；神经元；突触"], ["Reflex action (Tindakan refleks); Cerebrum (Serebrum); Cerebellum (Serebelum); Medulla oblongata (Medula oblongata)", "反射；大脑；小脑；延髓"], ["Hormone (Hormon); Insulin (Insulin); Glucagon (Glukagon); Diabetes mellitus (Diabetes melitus)", "激素；胰岛素；胰高血糖素；糖尿病"]], "", "Tip: 'saraf' = nerve."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying a reflex passes through the brain; it passes through the spinal cord.", "反射经脊髓而非大脑"], ["Confusing insulin and glucagon, or writing that insulin 'removes' sugar without saying glucose → glycogen.", "混淆胰岛素与胰高血糖素"], ["Writing that hormones are carried by nerves; they are carried by blood.", "激素由血液运输"], ["Mixing up dendrite and axon direction.", "混淆树突与轴突方向"]], "", "Tip: draw a labelled reflex arc for 3-4 marks."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: State the pathway of a reflex action. J: Stimulus → receptor → sensory neuron → spinal cord (relay neuron) → motor neuron → effector → response.", "问：反射路径？答：刺激→感受器→感觉神经元→脊髓→运动神经元→效应器→反应"], ["S: Why do impulses travel in one direction across a synapse? J: Neurotransmitter is released only from the presynaptic neuron and binds receptors on the postsynaptic neuron.", "问：突触为何单向？答：递质只由突触前神经元释放"], ["S: How does insulin lower blood glucose? J: It makes the liver convert glucose to glycogen and cells absorb more glucose.", "问：胰岛素如何降血糖？答：肝将葡萄糖转为糖原，细胞多吸收葡萄糖"], ["S: State one difference between nervous and endocrine coordination. J: Nervous is fast with short-lived effects; endocrine is slower with longer-lasting effects.", "问：神经与内分泌差异？答：神经快而短；内分泌慢而长"]], "", ""]],"bio|T4-13":[["Homeostasis: Concept and Negative Feedback", "稳态：概念与负反馈", [["Homeostasis: the maintenance of a constant internal environment (temperature, blood glucose, water and salt content, pH, blood pressure) despite changes outside the body.", "稳态：维持内环境相对稳定"], ["Why it matters: enzymes work best within narrow ranges of temperature and pH; cells need a stable osmotic environment to avoid shrinking or bursting.", "意义：酶需稳定温度和 pH；细胞需稳定渗透环境"], ["Negative feedback: a change in a factor is detected by receptors → the control centre (brain) → effectors act to bring the factor back to the normal level (set point).", "负反馈：偏离→感受器→控制中心→效应器→回到正常"], ["Main organs: brain (hypothalamus), skin, liver, pancreas, kidneys; the nervous and endocrine systems coordinate them.", "主要器官：下丘脑、皮肤、肝、胰、肾"], ["Example loop: blood glucose rises → insulin released → glucose falls → insulin release decreases.", "例：血糖升高→胰岛素→血糖下降→胰岛素减少"]], "", "Tip: feedback is 'negative' because the response reverses the original change."], ["Regulation of Body Temperature", "体温调节", [["Normal core temperature about 37 °C; the hypothalamus is the thermoregulatory centre, receiving information from thermoreceptors in the skin and blood.", "正常体温约 37 °C；下丘脑为调节中枢"], ["When the body is too hot: sweat glands secrete more sweat (evaporation cools the skin); arterioles in the skin dilate (vasodilation) so more heat is lost by radiation; hairs lie flat.", "过热：出汗、血管舒张、毛发平伏"], ["When the body is too cold: sweating stops; arterioles constrict (vasoconstriction) so less heat is lost; skeletal muscles shiver to release heat; hairs stand up to trap an insulating layer of air; metabolic rate rises.", "过冷：血管收缩、颤抖、毛发竖立、代谢加快"], ["Behaviour also helps: wearing suitable clothes, seeking shade, drinking water.", "行为调节：衣着、遮阴、饮水"]], "", "Tip: vasodilation = more blood to the skin surface = more heat lost."], ["Osmoregulation: Water Balance and ADH", "渗透调节：水平衡与 ADH", [["Osmoregulation: control of the water and salt content (osmotic pressure) of the blood; the kidneys are the main organs.", "渗透调节：控制血液水和盐含量"], ["Dehydration or salty food: blood osmotic pressure rises → detected by osmoreceptors in the hypothalamus → posterior pituitary releases more ADH (antidiuretic hormone).", "血渗透压升高→下丘脑→垂体后叶释放更多 ADH"], ["ADH makes the distal convoluted tubule and collecting duct more permeable to water → more water reabsorbed → small volume of concentrated urine; you also feel thirsty.", "ADH 使远曲小管与集合管重吸收更多水→尿少而浓"], ["Drinking a lot of water: blood osmotic pressure falls → less ADH → less water reabsorbed → large volume of dilute urine.", "饮水多：ADH 减少→尿多而稀"]], "", "Tip: ADH = 'anti-diuretic': it reduces urine volume."], ["The Human Urinary System", "人体泌尿系统", [["Kidneys: a pair of bean-shaped organs that filter blood, remove urea and other wastes, and regulate water and salt balance.", "肾：滤血、排尿素、调节水盐"], ["Renal artery brings blood with urea to the kidney; renal vein takes away blood with less urea and a changed water and salt content.", "肾动脉带来含尿素的血；肾静脉带走已净化的血"], ["Ureter: carries urine from the kidney to the urinary bladder; bladder: stores urine; urethra: carries urine out of the body.", "输尿管、膀胱、尿道"], ["Kidney structure: cortex (outer, contains glomeruli), medulla (inner, loops of Henle and collecting ducts), pelvis (collects urine).", "肾结构：皮质、髓质、肾盂"], ["Urea is formed in the liver by deamination of excess amino acids; it is excreted because it is toxic in high concentration.", "尿素由肝脏脱氨基产生；浓度高有毒"]], "", "Tip: ureter = kidney → bladder; urethra = bladder → outside."], ["The Nephron: Structure", "肾单位：结构", [["The nephron is the structural and functional unit of the kidney; each kidney contains about one million.", "肾单位：肾的结构与功能单位"], ["Parts in order: Bowman's capsule with the glomerulus (a knot of capillaries) → proximal convoluted tubule (PCT) → loop of Henle → distal convoluted tubule (DCT) → collecting duct.", "顺序：肾小囊+肾小球→近曲小管→髓袢→远曲小管→集合管"], ["The afferent arteriole (into the glomerulus) is wider than the efferent arteriole (out), which raises the blood pressure in the glomerulus.", "入球小动脉比出球小动脉粗，使肾小球内压力高"], ["The glomerulus and Bowman's capsule wall act as a filter; the PCT has microvilli and many mitochondria for reabsorption.", "肾小球与囊壁如滤器；近曲小管有微绒毛和大量线粒体"]], "", "Tip: draw and label the nephron in the order the filtrate flows."], ["Urine Formation: Ultrafiltration", "尿的形成：超滤", [["Ultrafiltration happens in the glomerulus and Bowman's capsule: high hydrostatic pressure forces small molecules out of the blood into the capsule.", "超滤：高压使小分子滤出"], ["Filtrate contains water, glucose, amino acids, urea, mineral ions and vitamins.", "滤液含水、葡萄糖、氨基酸、尿素、无机盐"], ["Blood cells and large plasma proteins stay in the blood because they are too large to pass through the capillary wall and basement membrane.", "血细胞和大蛋白留在血液中"], ["If protein or blood appears in urine, the filter may be damaged (kidney disease).", "尿中出现蛋白或血：滤器受损"]], "", "Tip: filtrate is like plasma without large proteins."], ["Urine Formation: Reabsorption and Secretion", "尿的形成：重吸收与分泌", [["PCT: all glucose and amino acids are reabsorbed by active transport; most water and mineral ions are reabsorbed too.", "近曲小管：葡萄糖和氨基酸全部主动重吸收；大部分水和无机盐被重吸收"], ["Loop of Henle: creates a high salt concentration in the medulla so water can be reabsorbed from the collecting duct.", "髓袢：在髓质造成高盐环境"], ["DCT and collecting duct: water is reabsorbed under the control of ADH; salts adjusted by hormones such as aldosterone.", "远曲小管与集合管：水在 ADH 控制下重吸收"], ["Tubular secretion: some substances (H⁺, K⁺, drugs, excess ions) are added from the blood into the tubule.", "肾小管分泌：H⁺、K⁺、药物"], ["Urine = water + urea + excess salts; normally no glucose, amino acids or large proteins.", "尿：水、尿素、多余盐；正常无葡萄糖"]], "", "Tip: glucose in urine = diabetes mellitus (reabsorption capacity exceeded)."], ["Comparing Blood, Filtrate and Urine", "血浆、滤液与尿的比较", [["Protein: present in plasma; absent in filtrate and urine.", "蛋白质：血浆有；滤液、尿无"], ["Glucose: present in plasma and filtrate; absent in urine (all reabsorbed).", "葡萄糖：血浆、滤液有；尿无"], ["Urea: low in plasma; same concentration in filtrate; high in urine because water is reabsorbed.", "尿素：尿中浓度最高（水被重吸收）"], ["Water: reduced in urine compared with filtrate; the amount varies with ADH.", "水：尿中比滤液少"]], "", "Tip: a table with these columns is a common SPM question."], ["Worked Example: Reading a Urine Test", "例题：读懂尿检结果", [["Q: A patient's urine contains glucose. Give two possible reasons. A: (1) Not enough insulin, so blood glucose is very high and the PCT cannot reabsorb all of it; (2) damaged PCT carriers.", "题：尿中有葡萄糖，两个可能原因"], ["Q: Why does a person who sweats a lot produce less urine? A: Blood osmotic pressure rises → more ADH → more water reabsorbed → small volume of concentrated urine.", "题：大量出汗为何尿少"], ["Q: Why is there no protein in the filtrate? A: Protein molecules are too large to pass through the glomerular capillary wall.", "题：滤液为何无蛋白"], ["Answer pattern: state the change → name the hormone/organ → give the result.", "答题模式：变化→激素/器官→结果"]], "", "Tip: link every answer to ADH, filtration or reabsorption."], ["Health Issues of the Urinary System (1)", "泌尿系统健康问题 (1)", [["Kidney failure: kidneys can no longer filter blood, so urea and water build up. Causes: diabetes, high blood pressure, infections, harmful drugs.", "肾衰竭：糖尿病、高血压、感染、药物"], ["Haemodialysis: the patient's blood flows through a dialysis machine; urea and excess salts diffuse across a partially permeable membrane into the dialysis fluid, which has no urea and normal glucose and salt concentrations.", "血液透析：尿素扩散入透析液"], ["Kidney transplant: a healthy donor kidney is placed in the patient; immunosuppressant drugs reduce rejection.", "肾移植：需抗排斥药"], ["Dialysis is temporary and expensive; a transplant is a longer-term solution but donors are limited.", "透析是暂时的；移植更长期"]], "", "Tip: dialysis fluid keeps glucose at normal level so glucose is not lost."], ["Health Issues of the Urinary System (2)", "泌尿系统健康问题 (2)", [["Urinary tract infection (UTI): bacteria infect the bladder or urethra, causing burning pain; treated with antibiotics; drinking enough water helps prevent it.", "泌尿道感染：抗生素；多喝水预防"], ["Kidney stones: crystals of salts such as calcium oxalate form in the kidney; cause severe pain; prevent by drinking enough water.", "肾结石：多喝水预防"], ["Diabetes insipidus: too little ADH, causing very large amounts of dilute urine and extreme thirst.", "尿崩症：ADH 不足"], ["Healthy habits: drink enough water, do not hold urine for long, limit salt and avoid misuse of drugs.", "健康习惯：多喝水、不憋尿、少盐"]], "", "Tip: diabetes mellitus (sugar) ≠ diabetes insipidus (ADH)."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Homeostasis (Homeostasis); Negative feedback (Suap balik negatif); Osmoregulation (Osmoregulasi); ADH (Hormon antidiuretik)", "稳态；负反馈；渗透调节；抗利尿激素"], ["Nephron (Nefron); Glomerulus (Glomerulus); Bowman's capsule (Kapsul Bowman); Loop of Henle (Gelung Henle)", "肾单位；肾小球；肾小囊；髓袢"], ["Ultrafiltration (Penurasan ultra); Reabsorption (Penyerapan semula); Urea (Urea); Dialysis (Dialisis)", "超滤；重吸收；尿素；透析"]], "", "Tip: 'buah pinggang' = kidney."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying ADH increases urine; it decreases urine volume by increasing water reabsorption.", "ADH 使尿减少而非增多"], ["Writing that glucose is filtered out and lost; it is filtered but fully reabsorbed in the PCT.", "葡萄糖被滤出但全部重吸收"], ["Mixing up ureter and urethra.", "混淆输尿管与尿道"], ["Forgetting to mention the hypothalamus detects the change in blood osmotic pressure.", "忘记下丘脑感知渗透压"], ["Saying vasodilation makes the body warmer; it lets heat escape.", "血管舒张是散热"]], "", "Tip: for feedback questions always give the full loop."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Name the process that forms the filtrate and where it happens. J: Ultrafiltration, in the glomerulus and Bowman's capsule, by high blood pressure.", "问：滤液如何形成？答：肾小球与肾小囊，高压超滤"], ["S: Why is there no glucose in the urine of a healthy person? J: All glucose is reabsorbed in the PCT by active transport.", "问：健康人尿为何无葡萄糖？答：近曲小管主动重吸收"], ["S: Explain how the body responds to dehydration. J: Osmotic pressure rises → hypothalamus → more ADH → more water reabsorbed → little concentrated urine.", "问：脱水时如何反应？答：渗透压升→ADH 增→重吸收水→尿少而浓"], ["S: State two ways the body loses less heat in cold weather. J: Vasoconstriction; shivering/hair erection reduces heat loss.", "问：寒冷时两种减少散热方式？答：血管收缩；毛发竖立"], ["S: Why is dialysis fluid free of urea? J: So urea diffuses from the blood into the fluid down its concentration gradient.", "问：透析液为何无尿素？答：使尿素顺浓度梯度扩散"]], "", ""]],"bio|T4-14":[["Types of Skeleton", "骨骼的类型", [["Hydrostatic skeleton: a fluid-filled body cavity under pressure, acted on by muscles; found in earthworms, jellyfish and sea anemones.", "静水骨骼：体腔液压+肌肉；蚯蚓、水母"], ["Exoskeleton: a hard outer covering of chitin; protects the body and prevents water loss; limits growth, so the animal moults (ecdysis); found in insects and crustaceans.", "外骨骼：几丁质；需蜕皮；昆虫、甲壳类"], ["Endoskeleton: an internal skeleton of bone and cartilage that grows with the body; found in vertebrates (fish, birds, humans).", "内骨骼：骨与软骨，随身体生长；脊椎动物"], ["Functions of a skeleton: support, protection of organs, movement (with muscles), shape of the body.", "功能：支持、保护、运动、塑形"], ["Bone also makes blood cells (red bone marrow) and stores calcium and phosphorus.", "骨髓造血；储存钙和磷"]], "", "Tip: link each skeleton to an example animal."], ["The Human Skeleton", "人体骨骼", [["Axial skeleton: skull (protects brain), vertebral column (protects spinal cord, supports body), ribs and sternum (protect heart and lungs).", "中轴骨：颅骨、脊柱、肋骨、胸骨"], ["Appendicular skeleton: pectoral girdle (scapula, clavicle) and pelvic girdle with the limbs; attaches arms and legs to the axial skeleton.", "附肢骨：肩带、骨盆带和四肢"], ["Bone is living tissue: a hard matrix of calcium phosphate (hardness) and collagen (flexibility), with bone cells and blood vessels.", "骨是活组织：钙盐+胶原蛋白"], ["Cartilage is flexible, found at the nose, ears, ends of bones and between vertebrae (discs) to absorb shock.", "软骨：柔韧、减震"]], "", "Tip: skull, ribs and vertebrae protect; limbs move."], ["Joints", "关节", [["Immovable (fibrous) joints: bones fused, e.g. the skull sutures, giving protection.", "不动关节：颅骨缝"], ["Slightly movable (cartilaginous) joints: e.g. between vertebrae, allow limited bending.", "微动关节：椎骨之间"], ["Freely movable (synovial) joints: ball-and-socket (shoulder, hip: movement in all directions), hinge (elbow, knee: one plane), pivot (neck: rotation), gliding (wrist, ankle: sliding).", "可动关节：球窝、铰链、枢轴、滑动"], ["Synovial joint parts: cartilage (reduces friction), synovial fluid (lubricates), synovial membrane (makes the fluid), joint capsule, ligaments (join bone to bone).", "滑膜关节结构：软骨、滑液、滑膜、关节囊、韧带"]], "", "Tip: ligament = bone to bone; tendon = muscle to bone."], ["Skeletal Muscles and Antagonistic Pairs", "骨骼肌与拮抗肌", [["Skeletal muscle is voluntary, striated and multinucleate; attached to bones by tendons (strong, inelastic).", "骨骼肌：随意、横纹、多核；肌腱连骨"], ["Muscles can only pull by contracting; they cannot push, so they work in antagonistic pairs: when one contracts the other relaxes.", "肌肉只能收缩拉动，需拮抗配对工作"], ["Bending the arm: biceps contracts, triceps relaxes → forearm is raised. Straightening the arm: triceps contracts, biceps relaxes.", "屈臂：二头肌收缩、三头肌放松；伸臂相反"], ["The bone acts as a lever, the joint as the fulcrum and the muscle supplies the effort.", "骨为杠杆，关节为支点，肌肉提供力"]], "", "Tip: name which muscle contracts AND which relaxes."], ["Types of Muscle", "肌肉的类型", [["Skeletal muscle: voluntary, striated, attached to bones, contracts quickly but tires.", "骨骼肌：随意、横纹、易疲劳"], ["Smooth muscle: involuntary, no striations, found in walls of the intestine, blood vessels and bladder; slow, sustained contraction.", "平滑肌：不随意、无横纹；内脏壁"], ["Cardiac muscle: involuntary, striated, branched fibres, found only in the heart; contracts rhythmically without tiring.", "心肌：不随意、横纹、有分支；只在心脏"]], "", "Tip: only skeletal muscle is voluntary."], ["How a Muscle Contracts", "肌肉如何收缩", [["A muscle fibre contains myofibrils made of repeating units called sarcomeres, with thin actin filaments and thick myosin filaments.", "肌原纤维由肌节组成：肌动蛋白、肌球蛋白"], ["During contraction, myosin heads attach to actin and pull the actin filaments inward (sliding filament model); the sarcomere shortens.", "滑动丝学说：肌节缩短"], ["Energy comes from ATP made by respiration; calcium ions trigger the attachment.", "能量来自 ATP；钙离子触发"], ["Lactic acid builds up in muscle during vigorous exercise when oxygen is limited, causing fatigue and cramp.", "剧烈运动缺氧→乳酸积累→疲劳"]], "", "Tip: the filaments slide; they do not shorten themselves."], ["Locomotion in Humans", "人体运动", [["Walking: leg muscles contract in turn; the pelvic girdle and hip and knee joints (ball-and-socket and hinge) move the legs; the foot arch absorbs shock.", "行走：腿肌轮流收缩；髋膝关节"], ["Muscle, bone and joint work together: nerve impulse → muscle contracts → pulls tendon → bone moves around the joint.", "神经冲动→肌收缩→肌腱→骨绕关节运动"], ["Balance is controlled by the cerebellum and the inner ear.", "平衡：小脑与内耳"], ["Regular exercise strengthens muscles and bones and keeps joints flexible.", "锻炼增强肌肉与骨骼"]], "", "Tip: write the full chain nerve → muscle → tendon → bone."], ["Locomotion in Other Animals", "其他动物的运动", [["Earthworm: circular muscles contract (body long and thin), longitudinal muscles contract (body short and fat); chaetae anchor the body in the soil; the hydrostatic skeleton gives support.", "蚯蚓：环肌与纵肌交替收缩，刚毛固定"], ["Fish: myotomes (W-shaped muscle blocks) contract alternately on each side to make the body wave; the streamlined body, fins and swim bladder help swimming and buoyancy.", "鱼：肌节交替收缩；流线型、鳍、鳔"], ["Bird: wings with feathers, light hollow bones, large pectoral muscles that power the downstroke.", "鸟：翼、中空骨、发达胸肌"], ["Insects: the thorax muscles move wings and legs attached to the exoskeleton.", "昆虫：胸部肌肉连外骨骼"]], "", "Tip: relate each adaptation to its function."], ["Comparing Skeleton Types and Joints", "骨骼与关节的比较", [["Hydrostatic: soft, flexible, no hard parts, limited support on land.", "静水骨骼：柔软，陆上支持有限"], ["Exoskeleton: rigid, protective, moulted; limits body size.", "外骨骼：坚硬，需蜕皮，限制体型"], ["Endoskeleton: grows with the animal, supports large bodies, muscles attach on the outside.", "内骨骼：随生长，支撑大型身体"], ["Hinge joint: one direction only; ball-and-socket: all directions.", "铰链一个方向；球窝多方向"]], "", "Tip: a comparison table (feature, example, advantage) is a typical question."], ["Health Issues of the Musculoskeletal System (1)", "肌肉骨骼系统健康问题 (1)", [["Osteoporosis: bones lose calcium and become porous and brittle; common in older women after menopause. Prevent with calcium, vitamin D and weight-bearing exercise.", "骨质疏松：缺钙；补钙、维生素 D、运动"], ["Arthritis: inflamed joints causing pain and stiffness; osteoarthritis (cartilage wears away) and rheumatoid arthritis (autoimmune).", "关节炎：骨关节炎与类风湿"], ["Rickets (children) and osteomalacia (adults): lack of vitamin D or calcium makes bones soft and bent.", "佝偻病/骨软化：缺维生素 D 或钙"], ["Gout: uric acid crystals in joints cause severe pain.", "痛风：尿酸结晶"]], "", "Tip: calcium + vitamin D for bone health."], ["Health Issues of the Musculoskeletal System (2)", "肌肉骨骼系统健康问题 (2)", [["Scoliosis: abnormal sideways curvature of the spine; poor posture and heavy bags can make it worse.", "脊柱侧弯：姿势不良"], ["Muscular dystrophy: genetic disease where muscles progressively weaken.", "肌肉萎缩症：遗传病"], ["Fracture, sprain (torn ligament) and strain (torn muscle or tendon): treat with rest, ice, compression and elevation; fractures need a cast.", "骨折、扭伤、拉伤：休息、冰敷、加压、抬高"], ["Healthy habits: balanced diet, regular exercise, correct posture, avoid injury and smoking.", "健康习惯"]], "", "Tip: sprain = ligament; strain = muscle."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Skeleton (Rangka); Exoskeleton (Rangka luar); Endoskeleton (Rangka dalam); Hydrostatic skeleton (Rangka hidrostatik)", "骨骼；外骨骼；内骨骼；静水骨骼"], ["Joint (Sendi); Ligament (Ligamen); Tendon (Tendon); Cartilage (Rawan)", "关节；韧带；肌腱；软骨"], ["Antagonistic muscles (Otot antagonis); Biceps (Bisep); Triceps (Trisep); Osteoporosis (Osteoporosis)", "拮抗肌；二头肌；三头肌；骨质疏松"]], "", "Tip: 'otot' = muscle; 'tulang' = bone."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Mixing up ligament (bone–bone) and tendon (muscle–bone).", "混淆韧带与肌腱"], ["Saying muscles 'push' bones; muscles only pull by contracting.", "肌肉只能拉不能推"], ["Forgetting to state that the other muscle in the pair relaxes.", "忘记另一块肌放松"], ["Writing that all muscles are voluntary.", "并非所有肌肉都随意"], ["Confusing osteoporosis (bone loss) with arthritis (joint inflammation).", "混淆骨质疏松与关节炎"]], "", "Tip: draw the arm with both muscles labelled."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Why do muscles work in antagonistic pairs? J: Muscles can only contract to pull; a second muscle is needed to pull the bone back.", "问：肌肉为何成对？答：只能收缩拉动，需另一块拉回"], ["S: State two functions of synovial fluid. J: Lubricates the joint and reduces friction; supplies nutrients to the cartilage.", "问：滑液两功能？答：润滑减摩擦；供养软骨"], ["S: Explain how the earthworm moves. J: Circular muscles contract → body long and thin; longitudinal muscles contract → body short and fat; chaetae grip the soil.", "问：蚯蚓如何运动？答：环肌、纵肌交替收缩，刚毛固定"], ["S: Why is the exoskeleton a disadvantage for growth? J: It is rigid, so the animal must moult.", "问：外骨骼为何不利生长？答：坚硬，需蜕皮"], ["S: How can osteoporosis be prevented? J: Calcium, vitamin D and weight-bearing exercise.", "问：如何预防骨质疏松？答：钙、维生素 D、负重运动"]], "", ""]],"bio|T4-15":[["Male Reproductive System", "男性生殖系统", [["Testes: in the scrotum (about 2–3 °C below body temperature, good for sperm); seminiferous tubules make sperm; interstitial cells make testosterone.", "睾丸：阴囊内；曲细精管产精子；间质细胞产睾酮"], ["Epididymis: stores and matures sperm. Sperm duct (vas deferens): carries sperm to the urethra. Urethra: passage for semen and urine.", "附睾储存成熟精子；输精管；尿道"], ["Seminal vesicle: fluid rich in fructose (energy for sperm). Prostate gland: alkaline fluid that neutralises acidity of the vagina. Cowper's gland: neutralises acidic urine in the urethra.", "精囊（果糖）；前列腺（碱性）；尿道球腺"], ["Semen = sperm + fluids from the glands; the fluids nourish and help sperm swim.", "精液=精子+腺体分泌液"]], "", "Tip: fructose = energy for sperm."], ["Female Reproductive System", "女性生殖系统", [["Ovaries: produce ova and the hormones oestrogen and progesterone.", "卵巢：产卵子、雌激素、孕酮"], ["Oviduct (Fallopian tube): funnel catches the ovum; cilia and muscle contractions move it; fertilisation happens here.", "输卵管：纤毛推送；受精场所"], ["Uterus: thick muscular wall; lining (endometrium) rich in blood vessels receives the embryo. Cervix: ring of muscle at the uterus opening. Vagina: receives sperm; birth canal.", "子宫（内膜）、子宫颈、阴道"]], "", "Tip: fertilisation in the oviduct; implantation in the uterus."], ["Structure of Sperm and Ovum", "精子与卵子的结构", [["Sperm: head with nucleus and acrosome (enzymes to digest the ovum's layers); middle piece packed with mitochondria (ATP); tail (flagellum) for swimming.", "精子：头（顶体酶）、中段（线粒体）、尾"], ["Ovum: large, round, cytoplasm rich in food (yolk); nucleus; surrounded by zona pellucida and follicle cells (corona radiata); cannot move.", "卵子：体积大、营养丰富、不能运动"], ["Sperm are small, numerous and motile; the ovum is large and few: one per month.", "精子小而多；卵子大而少"]], "", "Tip: relate every structure to its function."], ["Spermatogenesis", "精子发生", [["Occurs in the seminiferous tubules from puberty onwards and continues throughout life.", "发生于曲细精管；青春期后持续"], ["Spermatogonium (2n) → mitosis → primary spermatocyte (2n) → meiosis I → 2 secondary spermatocytes (n) → meiosis II → 4 spermatids (n) → differentiation → 4 sperm.", "精原→初级精母→次级精母→精细胞→4 个精子"], ["FSH stimulates sperm production; LH stimulates interstitial cells to secrete testosterone, which maintains sperm production and male characteristics.", "FSH 促精子产生；LH 促睾酮分泌"], ["One primary spermatocyte gives four equal-sized sperm.", "一个初级精母细胞→四个精子"]], "", "Tip: 4 sperm from 1 cell; 1 ovum from 1 cell."], ["Oogenesis", "卵子发生", [["Oogonia divide by mitosis before birth; primary oocytes (2n) begin meiosis but stop at prophase I until puberty.", "出生前形成初级卵母细胞，停在前期 I"], ["Each month, one primary oocyte completes meiosis I → secondary oocyte (n) + small first polar body; the secondary oocyte stops at metaphase II and is released at ovulation.", "减数分裂 I→次级卵母细胞+第一极体；排卵"], ["Meiosis II is completed only if a sperm enters → ovum (n) + second polar body.", "受精后才完成减数分裂 II"], ["One primary oocyte gives only one ovum; polar bodies degenerate, so the cytoplasm and food are kept in the ovum.", "一个初级卵母细胞→一个卵子"]], "", "Tip: compare spermatogenesis and oogenesis in a table."], ["The Menstrual Cycle (1): Phases", "月经周期 (1)：各阶段", [["Average length 28 days, controlled by FSH, LH, oestrogen and progesterone.", "约 28 天，由四种激素控制"], ["Days 1–5 menstruation: endometrium breaks down and leaves with blood.", "第 1–5 天：月经"], ["Days 6–13 follicular phase: FSH → follicle grows and secretes oestrogen → endometrium repairs and thickens.", "卵泡期：FSH→卵泡→雌激素"], ["Day 14 ovulation: a surge of LH makes the follicle release the secondary oocyte.", "第 14 天：LH 峰引起排卵"], ["Days 15–28 luteal phase: the follicle becomes the corpus luteum, secreting progesterone (and oestrogen) to maintain the thick endometrium.", "黄体期：黄体分泌孕酮"]], "", "Tip: LH surge → ovulation."], ["The Menstrual Cycle (2): Hormones", "月经周期 (2)：激素调节", [["High oestrogen inhibits FSH (negative feedback) and, at its peak, stimulates the LH surge.", "雌激素抑制 FSH；峰值触发 LH 峰"], ["High progesterone inhibits FSH and LH, so no new follicle develops in the luteal phase.", "孕酮抑制 FSH、LH"], ["If there is no fertilisation, the corpus luteum degenerates → progesterone falls → endometrium breaks down → menstruation.", "未受精：黄体退化→月经"], ["If fertilisation occurs, the embryo secretes hCG which keeps the corpus luteum active; later the placenta secretes progesterone, so menstruation stops.", "受精：hCG 维持黄体；胎盘接手"]], "", "Tip: progesterone maintains the endometrium."], ["Fertilisation, Implantation and Placenta", "受精、着床与胎盘", [["Fertilisation: a sperm releases acrosome enzymes, enters the secondary oocyte and the nuclei fuse → zygote (2n); the ovum then completes meiosis II.", "受精：顶体酶；核融合→合子"], ["The zygote divides by mitosis (cleavage) while moving down the oviduct → morula → blastocyst, which implants in the endometrium about 6–7 days after fertilisation.", "卵裂→桑葚胚→囊胚→着床"], ["Placenta: exchange of oxygen, nutrients, carbon dioxide, urea and antibodies by diffusion; maternal and foetal blood do not mix; it also secretes progesterone and oestrogen.", "胎盘：物质交换，母胎血不混；分泌激素"], ["Umbilical cord: 2 arteries (deoxygenated blood to the placenta) and 1 vein (oxygenated blood to the foetus). Amniotic fluid cushions shock and keeps temperature constant.", "脐带：2 动脉+1 静脉；羊水缓冲"]], "", "Tip: umbilical vein carries oxygenated blood."], ["Foetal Development and Birth", "胎儿发育与分娩", [["Pregnancy about 40 weeks: embryo (first 8 weeks, organs form) → foetus (growth and maturing).", "妊娠约 40 周：胚胎→胎儿"], ["Substances that can cross the placenta and harm the foetus: alcohol, nicotine, drugs, rubella virus, HIV.", "可通过胎盘的有害物质"], ["Birth: oestrogen and oxytocin cause uterine contractions; the cervix widens, the baby is born, then the placenta (afterbirth).", "分娩：催产素引起宫缩"], ["Lactation: prolactin makes milk; oxytocin releases it; breast milk has antibodies and balanced nutrients.", "泌乳：催乳素；母乳含抗体"], ["Antenatal care, folic acid and avoiding smoking and alcohol give a healthy baby.", "产前检查、叶酸、戒烟戒酒"]], "", "Tip: hormone = job; link each to the stage."], ["Formation of Twins", "双胞胎的形成", [["Identical (monozygotic) twins: one zygote splits into two embryos after the first divisions; same genes, same sex.", "同卵双胞胎：同基因、同性别"], ["Fraternal (dizygotic) twins: two ova released in the same cycle are fertilised by two different sperms; different genes, may be different sexes.", "异卵双胞胎：两卵两精；基因不同"], ["Siamese twins: the embryo splits incompletely, leaving the twins joined.", "连体双胞胎：不完全分裂"], ["Identical twins are used in studies to compare the effect of genes and environment.", "同卵双胞胎用于研究遗传与环境"]], "", "Tip: identical = 1 zygote; fraternal = 2 zygotes."], ["Health Issues of the Reproductive System (1)", "生殖系统健康问题 (1)", [["Sexually transmitted infections (STIs): HIV/AIDS, syphilis, gonorrhoea, genital herpes, HPV; spread by sexual contact and some by infected blood or from mother to baby.", "性传播感染：艾滋、梅毒、淋病、疱疹、HPV"], ["Prevention: abstinence, faithfulness, safe practices, vaccination (HPV, hepatitis B), regular check-ups.", "预防：禁欲、忠诚、疫苗、检查"], ["Cancers: cervical cancer (caused by HPV; Pap smear screening, HPV vaccine), breast cancer (self-examination, mammogram), prostate cancer.", "癌症：宫颈癌、乳腺癌、前列腺癌"]], "", "Tip: early detection saves lives."], ["Health Issues of the Reproductive System (2)", "生殖系统健康问题 (2)", [["Infertility: the couple cannot conceive; causes include blocked oviducts, low sperm count, ovulation problems.", "不育：输卵管阻塞、精子少"], ["Treatments: hormone therapy, artificial insemination, in-vitro fertilisation (IVF: fertilisation in a laboratory dish, then the embryo is placed in the uterus).", "治疗：激素、人工授精、试管婴儿"], ["Contraception: barrier (condom), hormonal (pill), intrauterine device (IUD), sterilisation (vasectomy, tubal ligation), natural methods.", "避孕：避孕套、药丸、宫内节育器、绝育"], ["Only condoms protect against both pregnancy and STIs.", "只有避孕套兼防 STI 与怀孕"]], "", "Tip: evaluate each method with an advantage and a disadvantage."], ["Growth in Humans and Animals", "人和动物的生长", [["Growth: a permanent increase in size and mass; measured by height, mass or dry mass.", "生长：大小和质量的永久增加"], ["Human growth curve is S-shaped (sigmoid): rapid in infancy, a growth spurt in puberty (growth hormone and sex hormones), then constant in adults.", "人类呈 S 形曲线：婴儿期快、青春期突增"], ["Insects and other arthropods grow in steps (intermittent) because the rigid exoskeleton must be moulted.", "节肢动物阶梯式生长：蜕皮"], ["Complete metamorphosis: egg → larva → pupa → adult (butterfly). Incomplete: egg → nymph → adult (grasshopper).", "完全变态；不完全变态"]], "", "Tip: sketch both curves and label the stages."], ["Worked Example: Hormones in the Menstrual Cycle", "例题：月经周期与激素", [["Q: Which hormone causes ovulation? A: LH (surge at about day 14, triggered by high oestrogen).", "题：哪种激素引起排卵？答：LH"], ["Q: Why does the endometrium stay thick after ovulation? A: The corpus luteum secretes progesterone which maintains it.", "题：排卵后内膜为何保持增厚？答：孕酮"], ["Q: Explain why menstruation does not happen in pregnancy. A: hCG then placental progesterone maintain the endometrium and inhibit FSH and LH.", "题：孕期为何无月经？答：hCG/孕酮维持内膜"], ["Q: Why are only some women's cycles 28 days? A: Cycle length varies with stress, health and diet.", "周期因人而异"]], "", "Tip: name the hormone, the organ and the effect."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Testis (Testis); Ovary (Ovari); Oviduct (Oviduk); Uterus (Uterus); Placenta (Plasenta)", "睾丸；卵巢；输卵管；子宫；胎盘"], ["Spermatogenesis (Spermatogenesis); Oogenesis (Oogenesis); Ovulation (Ovulasi); Fertilisation (Persenyawaan)", "精子发生；卵子发生；排卵；受精"], ["Menstrual cycle (Kitar haid); Twins (Kembar); Contraception (Kontraseptif); Metamorphosis (Metamorfosis)", "月经周期；双胞胎；避孕；变态"]], "", "Tip: 'haid' = menstruation."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying fertilisation happens in the uterus; it happens in the oviduct.", "受精在输卵管"], ["Writing that maternal and foetal blood mix in the placenta; they do not.", "母胎血不混合"], ["Mixing up the roles of FSH, LH, oestrogen and progesterone.", "混淆四种激素"], ["Saying a primary oocyte gives four ova; it gives one.", "一个初级卵母细胞只得一个卵子"], ["Confusing identical (1 zygote) and fraternal (2 zygotes) twins.", "混淆同卵与异卵"]], "", "Tip: for the cycle graph, label days and hormone peaks."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Where does fertilisation occur and what is formed? J: In the oviduct; a zygote (2n).", "问：受精部位？答：输卵管；合子"], ["S: State two functions of the placenta. J: Exchange of nutrients, oxygen and wastes; secretes progesterone.", "问：胎盘两功能？答：物质交换；分泌孕酮"], ["S: Why does a primary spermatocyte produce four sperm but a primary oocyte only one ovum? J: Spermatogenesis divides equally; oogenesis divides unequally, keeping the cytoplasm in the ovum.", "问：为何一个精母→四精子、一个卵母→一卵？答：精子等分；卵子不等分，保留营养"], ["S: Explain how identical twins are formed. J: One zygote splits into two embryos after the first divisions.", "问：同卵双胞胎如何形成？答：一个合子分裂成两个胚胎"], ["S: State one advantage of IVF. J: Couples with blocked oviducts can have a child.", "问：试管婴儿一优点？答：输卵管堵塞也能怀孕"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-1":[["Organisation of Plant Organs and Tissues", "植物器官与组织的组织层次", [["Levels of organisation: cell → tissue → organ → organ system → plant.", "层次：细胞→组织→器官→系统→植物体"], ["Root system (anchors, absorbs water and minerals, stores food) and shoot system (stem, leaves, flowers, fruits).", "根系与茎系"], ["Three tissue systems: dermal (protection), vascular (transport) and ground (photosynthesis, storage, support).", "三大组织系统：保护、输导、基本"], ["Dermal tissue: epidermis with waxy cuticle that reduces water loss; root hairs absorb water; guard cells form stomata.", "保护组织：表皮、角质层、根毛、保卫细胞"]], "", "Tip: dermal = skin; vascular = pipes; ground = everything else."], ["Ground Tissue: Parenchyma, Collenchyma, Sclerenchyma", "基本组织：薄壁、厚角、厚壁组织", [["Parenchyma: living, thin-walled, large vacuole; stores food, photosynthesis (in leaves), fills spaces.", "薄壁组织：储存、光合"], ["Collenchyma: living cells with cell walls unevenly thickened with cellulose at the corners; gives flexible support to young stems and leaf stalks.", "厚角组织：角处纤维素加厚；柔性支持"], ["Sclerenchyma: dead cells with walls thickened by lignin; very strong and rigid; fibres and sclereids (nut shells, gritty pear).", "厚壁组织：木质素；死细胞；硬支持"], ["Sclerenchyma supports mature parts that have stopped growing; collenchyma supports growing parts.", "厚壁支持成熟部位；厚角支持生长部位"]], "", "Tip: living: parenchyma, collenchyma; dead: sclerenchyma."], ["Vascular Tissue: Xylem and Phloem", "输导组织：木质部与韧皮部", [["Xylem: vessels and tracheids; dead, hollow cells with no end walls, walls thickened with lignin; transports water and minerals upward and supports the plant.", "木质部：导管、管胞；死、中空、木质素；运水与矿物质并支持"], ["Phloem: sieve tube elements (living, with sieve plates, little cytoplasm) and companion cells (many mitochondria, supply ATP); transports sucrose and amino acids in both directions.", "韧皮部：筛管+伴胞；运输有机物，双向"], ["Vascular tissue forms vascular bundles; in roots xylem and phloem are in different bundles, in stems and leaves they lie together.", "维管束"]], "", "Tip: xylem = water up; phloem = food both ways."], ["Dicotyledon and Monocotyledon", "双子叶与单子叶植物", [["Dicot: two cotyledons, net venation, tap root, vascular bundles in a ring in the stem, has vascular cambium (secondary growth), e.g. hibiscus, bean.", "双子叶：网状脉、直根、维管束成环、有形成层"], ["Monocot: one cotyledon, parallel venation, fibrous roots, scattered vascular bundles, no vascular cambium (no secondary growth), e.g. maize, grass.", "单子叶：平行脉、须根、维管束散生、无形成层"], ["In a stem cross-section of a dicot, from outside inward: epidermis, cortex, ring of vascular bundles (phloem outside, xylem inside), pith.", "双子叶茎横切：表皮、皮层、维管束环、髓"], ["In a root cross-section, the xylem is in the centre, often shaped like a star in dicots.", "根横切：木质部居中"]], "", "Tip: phloem is outside, xylem inside in the stem."], ["Meristematic Tissue", "分生组织", [["Meristem: tissue of small, undifferentiated cells with thin walls, dense cytoplasm and large nuclei that keep dividing by mitosis.", "分生组织：未分化、持续分裂"], ["Apical meristem: at tips of roots and shoots; increases length (primary growth).", "顶端分生组织：初生生长，长度"], ["Lateral meristem: vascular cambium and cork cambium; increases width (secondary growth).", "侧生分生组织：次生生长，宽度"], ["Intercalary meristem: at the base of internodes and leaves in grasses; regrowth after grazing or cutting.", "居间分生组织：禾本科"]], "", "Tip: apical = taller; lateral = wider."], ["Primary Growth and the Root Tip", "初生生长与根尖", [["Primary growth: increase in length of roots and shoots from the apical meristem; occurs in all plants.", "初生生长：长度"], ["Root tip zones from the tip: root cap (protects), zone of cell division (meristem), zone of elongation (cells absorb water and lengthen), zone of differentiation (root hairs, xylem, phloem form).", "根尖四区：根冠、分生区、伸长区、成熟区"], ["Shoot apical meristem produces leaves, axillary buds and new stem; the terminal bud suppresses the lateral buds (apical dominance).", "茎尖；顶端优势"], ["Cells formed by mitosis elongate, then differentiate into specialised cells.", "分裂→伸长→分化"]], "", "Tip: root hairs appear in the differentiation zone."], ["Secondary Growth in Woody Dicots", "木本双子叶的次生生长", [["Secondary growth increases the girth of stems and roots, by lateral meristems; occurs in woody dicots and gymnosperms, not in monocots.", "次生生长：加粗；单子叶无"], ["Vascular cambium divides to form secondary xylem (inward, wood) and secondary phloem (outward).", "形成层：向内次生木质部；向外次生韧皮部"], ["Cork cambium forms cork (bark) which replaces the epidermis; cork cells are dead and waterproof.", "木栓形成层→木栓"], ["Growth rings: wide, pale spring wood (rapid growth, wide vessels) and narrow, dark autumn wood; one ring per year.", "年轮：春材宽浅；秋材窄深；一年一轮"]], "", "Tip: more xylem than phloem is formed, so wood is mostly xylem."], ["Growth Rings and Their Uses", "年轮的应用", [["Counting rings gives the age of a tree.", "数年轮得树龄"], ["Ring width shows climate: wide rings in warm wet years, narrow rings in cold or dry years.", "宽窄反映气候"], ["Dendrochronology: dating timber and studying past climate and fires from rings.", "树木年代学"], ["Tropical trees often have no clear rings because growth continues all year round.", "热带树常无明显年轮"]], "", "Tip: link ring width to rainfall and temperature."], ["Growth Curve of Annual Plants", "一年生植物的生长曲线", [["Annual plants (e.g. maize, bean) complete their life cycle in one season; the curve of growth against time is sigmoid (S-shaped).", "一年生植物：S 形曲线"], ["Lag phase: slow, seed absorbs water and begins to germinate. Log (exponential) phase: rapid growth, cells divide and elongate. Stationary phase: growth stops, photosynthesis equals respiration. Senescence phase: the plant ages and dies; mass decreases.", "滞后期、对数期、稳定期、衰老期"], ["Perennials grow in repeated cycles each year; trees show a seasonal pattern.", "多年生：周期性"]], "", "Tip: name each phase AND explain it."], ["Measuring Growth", "生长的测量", [["Height or length: easy, non-destructive, but does not show change in mass.", "高度：简便，不反映质量"], ["Fresh mass: affected by the water content.", "鲜重：受含水量影响"], ["Dry mass: the plants are dried in an oven at about 100 °C until the mass is constant; the most accurate, but destroys the plants.", "干重：最准确，但破坏植物"], ["Leaf area or number of leaves can also be used.", "叶面积、叶数"]], "", "Tip: dry mass is reliable because water content varies."], ["Worked Example: Growth Rate", "例题：生长速率", [["Q: Dry mass of seedlings rises from 0.5 g on day 0 to 2.0 g on day 10. Find the average growth rate. A: (2.0 − 0.5) ÷ 10 = 0.15 g per day.", "题：平均生长速率 = 0.15 g/天"], ["Q: Why is dry mass better than fresh mass? A: Fresh mass changes with water content; dry mass shows true organic matter.", "题：干重为何更好？答：鲜重受水分影响"], ["Q: Why does the curve flatten in the stationary phase? A: Photosynthesis equals respiration, or resources are limited.", "题：稳定期为何变平？答：光合=呼吸，或资源有限"]], "", "Tip: always show units and workings."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Meristem (Meristem); Xylem (Xilem); Phloem (Floem); Cambium (Kambium)", "分生组织；木质部；韧皮部；形成层"], ["Parenchyma (Parenkima); Collenchyma (Kolenkima); Sclerenchyma (Sklerenkima)", "薄壁；厚角；厚壁"], ["Primary growth (Pertumbuhan primer); Secondary growth (Pertumbuhan sekunder); Annual ring (Gelang tahunan)", "初生；次生；年轮"]], "", "Tip: 'tumbuhan' = plant."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying xylem transports food; xylem transports water and minerals.", "木质部不运有机物"], ["Mixing up apical (length) and lateral (width) meristems.", "混淆顶端与侧生分生组织"], ["Writing that monocots have secondary growth; they lack vascular cambium.", "单子叶无次生生长"], ["Saying collenchyma is dead; it is living, sclerenchyma is dead.", "厚角组织是活的"], ["Forgetting to give the unit and method for growth measurement.", "漏单位与方法"]], "", "Tip: for a stem cross-section, label from outside inward."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: State two differences between xylem and phloem. J: Xylem is dead, transports water and minerals upward, lignified; phloem is living, transports sucrose in both directions.", "问：木质部与韧皮部两差异？答：木质部死，运水；韧皮部活，运有机物"], ["S: Why is sclerenchyma a good support for mature stems? J: Its cell walls are thickened with lignin, making it strong and rigid.", "问：厚壁组织为何适合支持成熟茎？答：木质素使其坚硬"], ["S: What causes growth rings? J: Vascular cambium makes wide, pale xylem in spring and narrow, dark xylem in autumn.", "问：年轮成因？答：春宽秋窄的木质部"], ["S: Why do monocots not become woody? J: They lack vascular cambium, so no secondary growth.", "问：单子叶为何不木质化？答：无形成层"], ["S: Why is dry mass the best measure of growth? J: Water content varies, so dry mass shows real increase in organic matter.", "问：为何干重最佳？答：排除水分影响"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-2":[["External and Internal Structure of the Leaf", "叶的外部与内部结构", [["External parts: lamina (blade), petiole (stalk), midrib and veins, apex and margin; the broad flat lamina gives a large surface area for light and gas exchange.", "外部：叶片、叶柄、中脉、叶脉"], ["Internal layers (cross-section, from top): cuticle → upper epidermis → palisade mesophyll → spongy mesophyll (with vascular bundle) → lower epidermis with stomata.", "内部：角质层→上表皮→栅栏组织→海绵组织→下表皮"], ["Vascular bundle: xylem towards the upper side, phloem towards the lower side.", "维管束：木质部在上，韧皮部在下"], ["Leaves are thin so gases diffuse a short distance and light reaches all cells.", "叶薄：扩散距离短、光易透入"]], "", "Tip: label from the top surface downward."], ["Tissues of the Leaf and Their Adaptations", "叶的组织及其适应", [["Waxy cuticle: waterproof, reduces water loss. Upper epidermis: transparent, lets light through to the mesophyll.", "角质层防水；上表皮透明"], ["Palisade mesophyll: tall, closely packed cells near the upper surface with many chloroplasts → absorbs the most light for photosynthesis.", "栅栏组织：排列紧密、叶绿体多"], ["Spongy mesophyll: irregularly arranged cells with large air spaces and fewer chloroplasts → allows gas diffusion.", "海绵组织：细胞间隙大，利于气体扩散"], ["Lower epidermis: stomata, each bounded by two guard cells.", "下表皮：气孔和保卫细胞"]], "", "Tip: structure → function → result."], ["Stomata and Guard Cells", "气孔与保卫细胞", [["Guard cells are kidney-shaped, contain chloroplasts and have an unevenly thickened wall (the inner wall facing the stoma is thicker).", "保卫细胞：肾形、含叶绿体、内壁较厚"], ["Opening: in light, guard cells photosynthesise and take up K⁺ → water potential falls → water enters by osmosis → cells become turgid and bow outward → stoma opens.", "开启：光照→K⁺吸收→渗透吸水→膨胀→气孔开"], ["Closing: when water is short or in darkness, guard cells lose water, become flaccid and the stoma closes, reducing water loss.", "关闭：失水→松弛→气孔关"], ["Most stomata are on the lower epidermis, which is cooler and shaded, so less water is lost.", "气孔多在下表皮，减少失水"]], "", "Tip: turgid = open; flaccid = closed."], ["Gas Exchange in Leaves", "叶的气体交换", [["Gases diffuse through the stomata into the air spaces of the spongy mesophyll and dissolve in the film of moisture around the mesophyll cells.", "气体经气孔→细胞间隙→湿润细胞表面溶解"], ["In the day (bright light): photosynthesis is faster than respiration, so CO₂ diffuses in and O₂ diffuses out.", "白天：CO₂进，O₂出"], ["At night: only respiration occurs, so O₂ diffuses in and CO₂ diffuses out.", "夜间：O₂进，CO₂出"], ["Adaptations: large surface area, thin leaf, many stomata, air spaces, moist cell surfaces.", "适应：面积大、薄、气孔多、间隙、湿润表面"]], "", "Tip: say which process is faster, day or night."], ["Transpiration", "蒸腾作用", [["Transpiration: the loss of water vapour from the aerial parts of the plant, mainly through stomata (also through the cuticle and lenticels).", "蒸腾：水蒸气散失，主要经气孔"], ["Process: water evaporates from the wet mesophyll cell walls into the air spaces → diffuses out through stomata; water is pulled up the xylem (transpiration pull).", "水蒸发→扩散出气孔；木质部上拉"], ["Importance: cools the plant, carries water and minerals up, supplies water for photosynthesis, keeps cells turgid.", "意义：降温、运输、供水、保持膨压"], ["Too much transpiration leads to wilting.", "蒸腾过多导致萎蔫"]], "", "Tip: transpiration pull is a result of water loss from leaves."], ["Factors Affecting Transpiration", "影响蒸腾的因素", [["Light intensity: brighter light → more stomata open → faster transpiration.", "光强↑→蒸腾↑"], ["Temperature: higher temperature → faster evaporation and diffusion → faster rate.", "温度↑→蒸腾↑"], ["Humidity: lower air humidity → steeper water vapour gradient → faster rate.", "湿度↓→蒸腾↑"], ["Wind: moves moist air away → faster rate. Soil water: if short, stomata close and rate falls.", "风↑→蒸腾↑；缺水→气孔关"]], "", "Tip: say how the water vapour gradient changes."], ["Investigation: Measuring Transpiration with a Potometer", "探究：用蒸腾计测量蒸腾", [["Potometer measures water uptake, which is close to the water lost by transpiration.", "蒸腾计测吸水量，近似蒸腾量"], ["Method: cut a leafy shoot underwater at a slant, fit it airtight, introduce an air bubble, record how far the bubble moves in a fixed time under different conditions (fan, light, humidity).", "方法：水下斜切、密封、记录气泡位移"], ["Precautions: leaves dry, no air leaks, keep other variables constant, repeat and take the mean.", "注意：叶干、不漏气、控制变量、重复取平均"], ["Cobalt chloride paper changes from blue to pink when it absorbs water vapour, showing water loss from the leaf.", "氯化钴试纸：蓝→粉红"]], "", "Tip: variables — manipulated: condition; responding: distance moved by the bubble; fixed: shoot size."], ["Photosynthesis: Overview and Equation", "光合作用：概览与方程", [["Photosynthesis: plants use light energy absorbed by chlorophyll to make glucose from carbon dioxide and water, releasing oxygen.", "光合作用：叶绿素吸光，由 CO₂和水合成葡萄糖并释放 O₂"], ["Equation: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → (light, chlorophyll) → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂.", "方程：6CO₂+6H₂O→C₆H₁₂O₆+6O₂"], ["Takes place in the chloroplasts; glucose is converted to starch, sucrose or cellulose.", "在叶绿体中进行"], ["Test for starch with iodine solution: blue-black (positive); leaves are boiled in ethanol first to remove chlorophyll.", "碘液测淀粉：蓝黑；先用乙醇脱色"]], "", "Tip: write the equation and the conditions."], ["Light-Dependent and Light-Independent Reactions", "光反应与暗反应", [["Light-dependent reaction (in the grana): chlorophyll absorbs light → water splits (photolysis) into hydrogen and oxygen; oxygen is released; ATP and NADPH are formed.", "光反应（基粒）：水光解，产生 ATP、NADPH、O₂"], ["Light-independent reaction (in the stroma): CO₂ is fixed and reduced to glucose using ATP and NADPH (Calvin cycle); it does not need light directly but needs the products of the light reaction.", "暗反应（基质）：固定 CO₂→葡萄糖"], ["Adaptations of the chloroplast: grana give a large surface area for chlorophyll; the stroma contains the enzymes.", "叶绿体适应：基粒、基质含酶"]], "", "Tip: O₂ comes from water, not from CO₂."], ["Factors Affecting the Rate of Photosynthesis", "影响光合速率的因素", [["Light intensity: rate rises with intensity until another factor becomes limiting.", "光强"], ["CO₂ concentration: rate increases until a plateau (about 0.03% in air is limiting).", "CO₂ 浓度"], ["Temperature: rate increases to an optimum (about 30–35 °C), then falls as enzymes denature.", "温度：最适后酶变性"], ["Limiting factor: the factor in shortest supply that limits the rate; on a graph the curve flattens when another factor is limiting.", "限制因子：曲线变平"]], "", "Tip: say 'limiting factor' and name it."], ["Compensation Point", "补偿点", [["Compensation point: the light intensity at which the rate of photosynthesis equals the rate of respiration; there is no net gas exchange.", "补偿点：光合=呼吸"], ["Below it, respiration is faster than photosynthesis, so CO₂ is released; above it, photosynthesis is faster, so CO₂ is absorbed.", "低于补偿点：呼吸>光合"], ["Investigation: leaves in hydrogencarbonate indicator tubes at different light intensities; yellow = CO₂ high (respiration), red = no change (compensation point), purple = CO₂ low (photosynthesis).", "探究：指示剂 黄/红/紫"], ["Shade plants have a lower compensation point than sun plants.", "阴生植物补偿点更低"]], "", "Tip: red at the compensation point."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Palisade mesophyll (Mesofil palisad); Spongy mesophyll (Mesofil span); Stoma (Stoma); Guard cell (Sel pengawal)", "栅栏组织；海绵组织；气孔；保卫细胞"], ["Transpiration (Transpirasi); Potometer (Potometer); Chloroplast (Kloroplas); Photolysis (Fotolisis)", "蒸腾；蒸腾计；叶绿体；光解"], ["Compensation point (Titik pampasan); Limiting factor (Faktor pengehad)", "补偿点；限制因子"]], "", "Tip: 'daun' = leaf."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying oxygen from photosynthesis comes from carbon dioxide; it comes from water.", "O₂ 来自水"], ["Confusing transpiration (loss of water vapour) with evaporation only; link it to stomata and the transpiration pull.", "蒸腾与气孔关联"], ["Mixing up turgid and flaccid guard cells and the open or closed stoma.", "混淆膨胀与松弛"], ["Forgetting that at the compensation point there is no net gas exchange.", "补偿点无净气体交换"], ["Writing 'photosynthesis stops at night' without mentioning respiration continues.", "夜间呼吸继续"]], "", "Tip: use 'because' and link structure to function."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Why is the palisade mesophyll near the upper surface? J: To receive the most light; it has many chloroplasts and closely packed cells.", "问：栅栏组织为何近上表面？答：接受最多光，叶绿体多"], ["S: Explain how a stoma opens. J: Guard cells take up K⁺, water enters by osmosis, they become turgid and bow outward.", "问：气孔如何打开？答：吸 K⁺→渗透吸水→膨胀弯曲"], ["S: State two factors that increase the rate of transpiration. J: Higher temperature and lower humidity (also wind, brighter light).", "问：两个加快蒸腾的因素？答：温度高、湿度低"], ["S: Where does the light-dependent reaction take place and what is produced? J: In the grana; ATP, NADPH and oxygen.", "问：光反应场所与产物？答：基粒；ATP、NADPH、O₂"], ["S: What happens to gas exchange at the compensation point? J: CO₂ released by respiration equals CO₂ used in photosynthesis, so there is no net exchange.", "问：补偿点气体交换如何？答：无净交换"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-3":[["Plant Nutrients: Macronutrients and Micronutrients", "植物营养素：大量与微量元素", [["Plants make organic food by photosynthesis but also need inorganic nutrients (mineral ions) absorbed from the soil.", "植物还需从土壤吸收无机盐"], ["Macronutrients (needed in large amounts): nitrogen (N), phosphorus (P), potassium (K), magnesium (Mg), calcium (Ca), sulphur (S).", "大量元素：N、P、K、Mg、Ca、S"], ["Micronutrients (trace amounts): iron (Fe), manganese, zinc, copper, boron, molybdenum.", "微量元素：Fe、Mn、Zn、Cu、B、Mo"], ["Ions absorbed: nitrate (NO₃⁻), ammonium (NH₄⁺), phosphate (PO₄³⁻), K⁺, Mg²⁺, Ca²⁺, sulphate (SO₄²⁻).", "吸收形式：硝酸盐、磷酸盐等离子"]], "", "Tip: plants absorb ions, not the elements themselves."], ["Functions and Deficiency: Nitrogen, Phosphorus, Potassium", "功能与缺乏症：氮、磷、钾", [["Nitrogen: makes amino acids, proteins, chlorophyll, nucleic acids. Deficiency: stunted growth, yellowing (chlorosis) starting from older leaves.", "氮：蛋白质、叶绿素；缺乏：矮小、老叶变黄"], ["Phosphorus: makes ATP, DNA, phospholipids; promotes root growth. Deficiency: poor root growth, small leaves, dark green or purple leaves.", "磷：ATP、DNA；缺乏：根弱、叶紫"], ["Potassium: activates enzymes and controls opening of stomata. Deficiency: yellow leaf edges with brown dead spots (leaf scorch), weak stems.", "钾：酶激活、气孔；缺乏：叶缘焦枯"]], "", "Tip: N → leaves; P → roots; K → stomata and enzymes."], ["Functions and Deficiency: Magnesium, Calcium, Iron", "功能与缺乏症：镁、钙、铁", [["Magnesium: the central atom in chlorophyll. Deficiency: yellowing between the veins of older leaves.", "镁：叶绿素中心；缺乏：老叶脉间变黄"], ["Calcium: forms calcium pectate in the middle lamella of cell walls; needed for cell division. Deficiency: stunted growth, deformed young leaves, poor roots.", "钙：细胞壁中胶层；缺乏：幼叶畸形、根弱"], ["Iron: needed to make chlorophyll. Deficiency: young leaves turn yellow or white.", "铁：叶绿素合成；缺乏：幼叶变黄"], ["Mobile nutrients (N, P, K, Mg) are moved to young leaves, so symptoms appear on older leaves; immobile ones (Ca, Fe) show on young leaves.", "可移动元素症状在老叶；不可移动在幼叶"]], "", "Tip: old leaf symptoms = mobile element; young leaf = immobile."], ["Investigation: Water Culture Experiment", "探究：水培实验", [["Aim: to study the effect of a mineral deficiency on seedling growth.", "目的：研究缺乏某元素的影响"], ["Method: seedlings are grown in distilled water containing (a) all essential minerals (control), (b) all minerals except one, e.g. nitrate; the solution is aerated and the container covered with black paper to stop algae.", "方法：完全营养液（对照）与缺一元素；通气；遮光"], ["Variables: manipulated: the mineral missing; responding: height, leaf colour, root growth; fixed: volume of solution, light, temperature, seedling type.", "变量：操纵—缺的元素；响应—生长；固定—溶液体积、光、温度"], ["Observation after 2–3 weeks: plants without nitrate are stunted with yellow leaves; the control grows healthily.", "观察：缺氮矮小黄化"]], "", "Tip: the complete solution is the control."], ["Worked Example: Interpreting Deficiency Symptoms", "例题：判断缺素症状", [["Q: Old leaves are yellow and growth is stunted. Which mineral is lacking? A: Nitrogen (mobile; needed for chlorophyll and protein).", "题：老叶发黄、矮小→缺氮"], ["Q: Leaves yellow between veins, starting at older leaves. A: Magnesium (needed for chlorophyll).", "题：脉间黄化→缺镁"], ["Q: Young leaves are pale and the veins stay green. A: Iron (immobile, needed for chlorophyll formation).", "题：幼叶苍白→缺铁"], ["Answer pattern: symptom → mineral → function of mineral.", "答题：症状→元素→功能"]], "", "Tip: always state the function of the mineral."], ["Root Structure and Water Absorption", "根的结构与吸水", [["Root hairs: outgrowths of epidermal cells just behind the root tip; they greatly increase the surface area for absorption; thin walls and a large vacuole with concentrated cell sap.", "根毛：表皮细胞突起，面积大"], ["Water enters by osmosis: the soil water has a higher water potential than the cell sap, so water moves into the root hair, then from cell to cell down the water potential gradient.", "渗透吸水：水势梯度"], ["Path: soil → root hair → cortex → endodermis → xylem.", "路径：土壤→根毛→皮层→内皮层→木质部"], ["Roots also have a root cap to protect the tip and a branched system to cover a large soil area.", "根冠；根系分支"]], "", "Tip: water moves by osmosis from high to low water potential."], ["Absorption of Mineral Ions", "矿质离子的吸收", [["Ions are absorbed by active transport against the concentration gradient; it needs ATP, so root hair cells contain many mitochondria.", "主动运输：逆浓度梯度，需 ATP"], ["Some ions enter by diffusion when the soil concentration is higher than that in the cell.", "扩散：土壤浓度较高时"], ["Oxygen in the soil is needed for aerobic respiration to give ATP; in waterlogged soil, mineral uptake falls.", "土壤氧气→有氧呼吸→ATP；涝害"], ["Once inside the xylem, ions are transported upward with the water.", "进入木质部随水上行"]], "", "Tip: ions → active transport; water → osmosis."], ["Fertilisers and Soil Management", "肥料与土壤管理", [["Organic fertilisers (compost, manure): release nutrients slowly, improve soil structure and water retention.", "有机肥：缓释、改善土壤结构"], ["Inorganic (chemical) fertilisers: contain known amounts of NPK; act quickly but may be washed away.", "无机肥：见效快，易流失"], ["Excess fertiliser washed into rivers causes eutrophication: algal bloom → light is blocked → algae die → decomposers use up oxygen → fish die.", "过量肥料→富营养化→藻华→缺氧"], ["Good practice: crop rotation, planting legumes, correct amounts, mulching.", "良好做法：轮作、种豆科、适量"]], "", "Tip: describe the full eutrophication chain."], ["Diversity in Plant Nutrition: Overview", "植物营养方式的多样性", [["Most plants are autotrophs (photosynthesis).", "多数为自养"], ["Some plants have special modes: parasitic (Rafflesia, Cuscuta, mistletoe), carnivorous (Nepenthes, Drosera), epiphytic (orchids, staghorn fern), symbiotic with nitrogen-fixing bacteria (legumes) and saprophytic plants.", "寄生、食虫、附生、共生、腐生"], ["These adaptations are often related to the lack of nitrogen or light in the habitat.", "适应缺氮或缺光环境"]], "", "Tip: link each mode with an example from Malaysia."], ["Parasitic and Epiphytic Plants", "寄生与附生植物", [["Parasitic plants obtain food from a host through haustoria that penetrate the host's vascular tissue; e.g. Rafflesia (no chlorophyll, on Tetrastigma vine), Cuscuta (dodder) and mistletoe (partial parasite with some chlorophyll).", "寄生：吸器；大花草、菟丝子、槲寄生"], ["Parasites harm the host by taking water, minerals and food; they reduce the host's growth.", "寄生物危害宿主"], ["Epiphytes grow on other plants for support and light but do not take food from them, e.g. orchids and staghorn fern; their roots absorb rain water and humus.", "附生：只借支持；兰花、鹿角蕨"]], "", "Tip: parasite takes food; epiphyte only uses support."], ["Carnivorous Plants", "食虫植物", [["Carnivorous plants live in soil poor in nitrogen; they trap and digest insects for nitrogen compounds but still photosynthesise.", "食虫植物：缺氮土壤；仍光合"], ["Nepenthes (pitcher plant): pitcher with a slippery rim, nectar and digestive enzymes (protease) in the liquid; the insect slips and is digested.", "猪笼草：滑边、蜜、蛋白酶"], ["Drosera (sundew): sticky tentacles trap insects; Utricularia (bladderwort): bladder traps small aquatic animals.", "茅膏菜；狸藻"], ["Digestion produces amino acids and nitrates that are absorbed.", "消化产物被吸收"]], "", "Tip: they are autotrophs that supplement nitrogen."], ["Legumes and Nitrogen-Fixing Bacteria", "豆科植物与固氮菌", [["Legumes (bean, groundnut) have root nodules containing Rhizobium bacteria that convert atmospheric nitrogen into ammonium compounds (nitrogen fixation).", "豆科根瘤：根瘤菌固氮"], ["Mutualism: the bacteria get sugars and shelter from the plant; the plant gets nitrogen compounds.", "互利共生"], ["After the plant dies, nitrogen compounds enrich the soil, so legumes are used in crop rotation.", "轮作提高土壤氮"], ["Other bacteria: nitrifying bacteria change ammonium to nitrate; denitrifying bacteria return nitrogen to the air.", "硝化细菌；反硝化细菌"]], "", "Tip: Rhizobium = nodules = nitrogen fixation."], ["Key Terms and Common Mistakes", "重点术语与常见错误", [["Macronutrient (Makronutrien); Micronutrient (Mikronutrien); Chlorosis (Klorosis); Root hair (Akar rerambut); Eutrophication (Eutrofikasi)", "大量元素；微量元素；黄化；根毛；富营养化"], ["Parasite (Parasit); Epiphyte (Epifit); Carnivorous plant (Tumbuhan karnivor); Nitrogen fixation (Pengikatan nitrogen)", "寄生；附生；食虫植物；固氮"], ["Mistake: saying plants absorb minerals by osmosis; ions use active transport.", "离子是主动运输"], ["Mistake: saying carnivorous plants do not photosynthesise; they do.", "食虫植物也光合"], ["Mistake: confusing epiphytes with parasites.", "混淆附生与寄生"]], "", "Tip: 'tanah' = soil."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: State the function of magnesium and one deficiency symptom. J: It is needed to make chlorophyll; leaves turn yellow between veins.", "问：镁的功能与症状？答：叶绿素；脉间黄化"], ["S: Why do root hair cells have many mitochondria? J: To release ATP for active transport of mineral ions.", "问：根毛为何线粒体多？答：为主动运输提供 ATP"], ["S: Why is the water culture solution aerated? J: Roots need oxygen for aerobic respiration to provide ATP for ion uptake.", "问：水培为何通气？答：根需氧产生 ATP"], ["S: Why do pitcher plants trap insects? J: To obtain nitrogen compounds because the soil is poor in nitrogen.", "问：猪笼草为何捕虫？答：获取氮"], ["S: Explain the relationship between legumes and Rhizobium. J: Mutualism: bacteria fix nitrogen; the plant supplies sugars.", "问：豆科与根瘤菌关系？答：互利共生"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-4":[["Xylem: Structure and Adaptations", "木质部：结构与适应", [["Xylem consists of vessels, tracheids, fibres and parenchyma; vessels and tracheids carry water and minerals.", "木质部：导管、管胞、纤维、薄壁细胞"], ["Vessel elements are dead, hollow cells joined end to end with no end walls, forming a continuous tube that lets water flow without resistance.", "导管：死细胞、无端壁，连成管"], ["Walls are thickened with lignin in rings, spirals or networks; this makes the vessel strong, prevents it from collapsing under tension and supports the plant.", "木质素加厚，防塌陷并支持"], ["The lumen is narrow, which helps capillary action; pits in the walls let water move sideways between vessels.", "管腔窄利毛细作用；纹孔横向通水"]], "", "Tip: no cytoplasm, no end walls = free flow."], ["Phloem: Structure and Adaptations", "韧皮部：结构与适应", [["Phloem consists of sieve tube elements, companion cells, parenchyma and fibres.", "韧皮部：筛管、伴胞、薄壁、纤维"], ["Sieve tube elements are living but have no nucleus and little cytoplasm; the end walls (sieve plates) have pores so sap flows from cell to cell.", "筛管：活细胞，无核，筛板有孔"], ["Companion cells have a nucleus, dense cytoplasm and many mitochondria; they provide ATP for loading sucrose into the sieve tubes and are linked by plasmodesmata.", "伴胞：核、线粒体多，供 ATP"], ["Phloem transports sucrose and amino acids in both directions.", "运输蔗糖、氨基酸，双向"]], "", "Tip: companion cells keep the sieve tube alive."], ["Investigation: Transport in Xylem", "探究：木质部的运输", [["Method: stand a leafy stem (e.g. balsam or celery) in water with red dye (eosin) for a few hours; cut transverse and longitudinal sections and view under a microscope.", "方法：红墨水吸入；横切、纵切"], ["Observation: the dye shows only in the xylem vessels, in a ring in the stem; the leaf veins become red.", "观察：只有木质部被染红"], ["Conclusion: water and minerals are transported in the xylem.", "结论：水和矿物质经木质部运输"], ["Ringing experiment on a stem: removing a ring of bark (phloem) does not stop water going up; the leaves stay turgid.", "环剥：去韧皮部不影响水分上行"]], "", "Tip: the longitudinal section shows continuous red tubes."], ["The Path of Water in the Plant", "水在植物体内的路径", [["Soil water → root hair → cortex cells → endodermis → xylem of the root.", "土壤→根毛→皮层→内皮层→根木质部"], ["Root xylem → stem xylem → leaf vein → mesophyll cells → evaporates into air spaces → leaves through stomata (transpiration).", "根木质部→茎→叶脉→叶肉→蒸发→气孔"], ["Water may move through cell walls (apoplast) or through cytoplasm and plasmodesmata (symplast); at the endodermis the Casparian strip forces it through the cytoplasm.", "质外体与共质体；凯氏带"], ["A continuous stream of water from root to leaf is called the transpiration stream.", "蒸腾流"]], "", "Tip: write the path in order from soil to air."], ["Root Pressure and Capillary Action", "根压与毛细作用", [["Root pressure: active transport of ions into the xylem lowers its water potential, so water enters by osmosis and is pushed up; it is small and can only push water a few metres.", "根压：离子入木质部→渗透吸水→上推；力小"], ["Evidence: guttation (water droplets at leaf edges at night) and sap oozing from a cut stem.", "证据：吐水"], ["Capillary action: adhesion of water molecules to the xylem walls and cohesion between them pull water up the narrow vessels; limited to about one metre.", "毛细作用：附着与内聚；约一米"], ["Neither can lift water to the top of tall trees alone.", "二者都不足以到达高树顶"]], "", "Tip: small contribution; the main force is transpiration pull."], ["Transpiration Pull", "蒸腾拉力", [["Water evaporates from mesophyll cell walls → lowers the water potential of the cells → water is drawn from the xylem, creating tension (negative pressure) in the xylem.", "蒸腾使叶肉水势下降→拉水"], ["Cohesion (hydrogen bonds between water molecules) keeps the water column unbroken; adhesion to the walls supports the column.", "内聚（氢键）和附着维持水柱"], ["The pull is transmitted down the xylem to the roots, so water is pulled up the plant; this is the main force, enough for the tallest trees.", "主要动力"], ["More transpiration → faster water uptake; this is why a potometer can measure it.", "蒸腾越强，吸水越快"]], "", "Tip: say 'cohesion' and 'adhesion' by name."], ["Transport of Minerals and Wilting", "矿物质运输与萎蔫", [["Mineral ions dissolve in water and move up the xylem with the transpiration stream; some are redistributed in phloem.", "矿质随蒸腾流上行"], ["Wilting: when water loss from transpiration is faster than uptake, cells lose turgor and become flaccid; the plant droops, the stomata close.", "萎蔫：失水>吸水，膨压丧失"], ["Wilting reduces the surface exposed to sunlight and lowers transpiration; the plant recovers when watered.", "萎蔫减少蒸腾；浇水可恢复"], ["Turgor pressure keeps herbaceous plants upright.", "膨压支撑草本植物"]], "", "Tip: link turgor with support."], ["Translocation: Sources and Sinks", "同化物运输：源与库", [["Translocation: the transport of organic substances (mainly sucrose and amino acids) in the phloem.", "运输：有机物经韧皮部"], ["Source: where sugars are made or released (mature leaves, storage organs in spring). Sink: where sugars are used or stored (roots, fruits, growing tips, seeds).", "源：叶；库：根、果、芽"], ["Direction depends on the source and sink, so it can be upward or downward; it needs energy (ATP).", "方向由源库决定；需 ATP"], ["Sucrose is transported (not glucose) because it is soluble and chemically unreactive.", "蔗糖：可溶、稳定"]], "", "Tip: source = surplus; sink = demand."], ["Pressure Flow (Mass Flow) Hypothesis", "压流（质流）假说", [["At the source: sucrose is actively loaded into sieve tubes by companion cells → water potential falls → water enters from the xylem by osmosis → hydrostatic pressure rises.", "源端：主动装载蔗糖→渗透吸水→压力升高"], ["At the sink: sucrose is unloaded and used or stored → water potential rises → water leaves the sieve tube → pressure falls.", "库端：卸载→水移出→压力下降"], ["The pressure difference makes the sap flow by mass flow from source to sink.", "压力差驱动质流"], ["Evidence: sap flows out when a stem is cut; aphid stylets show sap under pressure; radioactive ¹⁴C moves in the phloem.", "证据：蚜虫口针、¹⁴C 追踪"]], "", "Tip: use the words 'loading', 'osmosis', 'pressure'."], ["Ringing Experiment (Girdling)", "环剥实验", [["Method: a ring of bark including the phloem is removed from a woody stem; the xylem stays.", "方法：环剥树皮（含韧皮部）"], ["Observation: after some days the bark above the ring swells; below the ring the bark and roots eventually die.", "观察：环上方膨大；下方死亡"], ["Explanation: sugars from the leaves cannot pass the ring and accumulate above it; the roots are starved of food.", "解释：糖积累在上方；根得不到养分"], ["The leaves stay alive because water still moves up the xylem.", "木质部仍运水"]], "", "Tip: conclusion = phloem carries organic food downward."], ["Comparing Xylem and Phloem", "木质部与韧皮部比较", [["Substances: xylem — water and minerals; phloem — sucrose and amino acids.", "物质：水、矿物质；有机物"], ["Direction: xylem — upward only; phloem — upward and downward.", "方向：单向上行；双向"], ["Cells: xylem — dead, lignified, no end walls; phloem — living (sieve tubes with sieve plates and companion cells).", "细胞：死、木质化；活、有筛板和伴胞"], ["Energy and force: xylem — passive (transpiration pull); phloem — needs ATP for loading.", "动力：被动；需 ATP"]], "", "Tip: use a table for 'differences' questions."], ["Phytoremediation: Types", "植物修复：类型", [["Phytoremediation: using plants to remove, degrade or contain pollutants in soil, water or air.", "植物修复：用植物去除或降解污染物"], ["Phytoextraction: hyperaccumulator plants absorb heavy metals (lead, cadmium) and store them in shoots; e.g. Indian mustard, sunflower.", "植物提取：芥菜、向日葵"], ["Rhizofiltration: roots of water hyacinth absorb metals and nutrients from polluted water.", "根系过滤：凤眼莲（水葫芦）"], ["Phytodegradation: plants and root microbes break down organic pollutants; phytostabilisation: roots hold contaminants in the soil; phytovolatilisation: pollutants released as vapour through leaves.", "降解、稳定、挥发"]], "", "Tip: name a plant and the pollutant."], ["Phytoremediation: Advantages and Limitations", "植物修复：优点与局限", [["Advantages: low cost, environmentally friendly, in-situ, improves soil, looks natural.", "优点：成本低、环保、原位"], ["Limitations: slow, only works at root depth, concentrations must be non-toxic to the plant.", "局限：慢、只到根深度、浓度不能过高"], ["Harvested plants contain concentrated pollutants and must be disposed of safely; otherwise they may enter the food chain.", "收获的植物须安全处理，避免进入食物链"], ["Used for mining sites, polluted rivers, oil spills and wastewater treatment.", "应用：矿区、河流、石油泄漏"]], "", "Tip: give one advantage and one limitation."], ["Worked Example: Explaining Experiments", "例题：解释实验", [["Q: Why does a cut leafy stem placed in red dye show red only in the xylem? A: Water and the dye are carried upward only by xylem vessels.", "题：为何只有木质部变红？答：水经木质部上行"], ["Q: A plant is in a hot, windy place. Explain why it wilts. A: Transpiration is faster than water uptake, so cells lose turgor.", "题：热风下为何萎蔫？答：蒸腾>吸水"], ["Q: State how sucrose enters the phloem at the leaf. A: Companion cells use ATP for active transport, then water enters by osmosis, causing mass flow.", "题：蔗糖如何进韧皮部？答：伴胞主动装载"]], "", "Tip: link each answer with the right process."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Xylem (Xilem); Phloem (Floem); Translocation (Translokasi); Transpiration pull (Tarikan transpirasi)", "木质部；韧皮部；同化物运输；蒸腾拉力"], ["Cohesion (Kohesi); Adhesion (Adhesi); Root pressure (Tekanan akar); Capillary action (Tindakan kapilari)", "内聚；附着；根压；毛细作用"], ["Phytoremediation (Fitoremediasi); Hyperaccumulator (Hiperpengumpul); Source (Sumber); Sink (Sinki)", "植物修复；超积累植物；源；库"]], "", "Tip: 'angkutan' = transport."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying phloem carries water; xylem carries water and phloem carries organic food.", "韧皮部不运水"], ["Writing that root pressure is the main force; it is transpiration pull.", "主要动力是蒸腾拉力"], ["Confusing cohesion (water–water) with adhesion (water–wall).", "混淆内聚与附着"], ["Saying translocation is only upward.", "同化物运输并非只向上"], ["Forgetting that phytoremediation plants must be disposed of safely.", "忘记安全处理"]], "", "Tip: for explanations of water movement, use the chain: transpiration → tension → cohesion → uptake."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: State two adaptations of xylem vessels. J: No end walls and no cytoplasm; lignified walls to prevent collapse.", "问：导管两适应？答：无端壁和细胞质；木质素加固"], ["S: Explain how transpiration pull works. J: Evaporation creates tension in the xylem; cohesion between water molecules pulls the water column up.", "问：蒸腾拉力如何作用？答：蒸发→张力；内聚拉动水柱"], ["S: What is the role of companion cells? J: Provide ATP for loading sucrose into sieve tubes.", "问：伴胞作用？答：为装载蔗糖供 ATP"], ["S: What does the ringing experiment show? J: Organic food is transported in the phloem; the bark above the ring swells.", "问：环剥说明什么？答：有机物经韧皮部运输"], ["S: Give one example of phytoremediation. J: Water hyacinth absorbing heavy metals from polluted water.", "问：植物修复一例？答：凤眼莲吸收重金属"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-5":[["Plant Responses: Stimuli and Types of Response", "植物的反应：刺激与反应类型", [["Plants respond to stimuli such as light, gravity, water, touch and chemicals; the responses are slow and usually involve growth, controlled by hormones.", "植物对光、重力、水、触碰等刺激做出反应，通常是生长，由激素控制"], ["Tropism: a directional growth response towards (positive) or away from (negative) the stimulus.", "向性：定向生长；正向性/负向性"], ["Nastic movement: a non-directional response whose direction does not depend on the direction of the stimulus.", "感性运动：方向与刺激方向无关"], ["Plants lack a nervous system, so responses are coordinated by plant hormones (phytohormones).", "由植物激素协调"]], "", "Tip: tropism = direction of stimulus matters; nastic = it does not."], ["Types of Tropism", "向性的类型", [["Phototropism (light): shoots positive, roots negative or indifferent.", "向光性：茎正；根负"], ["Geotropism / gravitropism (gravity): roots positive (grow down), shoots negative (grow up).", "向地性：根正；茎负"], ["Hydrotropism (water): roots grow towards moist soil (positive).", "向水性：根正"], ["Thigmotropism (touch): tendrils of climbers (e.g. passion fruit, pea) coil around a support.", "向触性：卷须缠绕"], ["Chemotropism (chemicals): the pollen tube grows towards the ovule.", "向化性：花粉管"]], "", "Tip: root and shoot respond in opposite ways to gravity."], ["Nastic Movements", "感性运动", [["Touch-sensitive plant (Mimosa pudica, 'semalu'): when touched, leaflets fold and the petiole droops; cells in the pulvinus lose water and turgor quickly.", "含羞草：触碰后叶片合拢；叶枕细胞失去膨压"], ["Flowers opening and closing in response to light or temperature (e.g. morning glory, tulip).", "花的开闭"], ["Stomata opening and closing; leaves of some plants fold at night (sleep movement).", "气孔开闭；叶的睡眠运动"], ["Advantage of Mimosa folding: reduces the surface area and frightens or protects against herbivores.", "优点：减少被食"]], "", "Tip: Mimosa response is fast because of turgor change, not growth."], ["Comparing Tropism and Nastic Movement", "向性与感性运动比较", [["Direction: tropism depends on the direction of the stimulus; nastic does not.", "方向：向性依刺激方向；感性不依"], ["Mechanism: tropism involves unequal growth (auxin); nastic often involves changes in turgor pressure.", "机制：不均等生长；膨压变化"], ["Speed: tropism is slow; nastic can be fast (Mimosa).", "速度：慢；可很快"], ["Example: shoot bending to light vs Mimosa leaflets folding.", "例：向光弯曲；含羞草合拢"]], "", "Tip: use a table with at least three differences."], ["Auxin and Phototropism", "生长素与向光性", [["Auxin (IAA) is made in the shoot tip (apical meristem), young leaves and seeds, then moves down the shoot.", "生长素：茎尖合成"], ["In shoots, auxin promotes cell elongation.", "茎中促进细胞伸长"], ["Unilateral light: auxin moves from the lit side to the shaded side → higher auxin concentration on the shaded side → cells there elongate more → the shoot bends towards the light.", "单侧光：生长素移向背光侧→背光侧伸长更快→向光弯曲"], ["The tip detects the light; the bending occurs in the zone of elongation below the tip.", "尖端感光；弯曲发生在伸长区"]], "", "Tip: the shaded side grows faster."], ["Auxin and Geotropism", "生长素与向地性", [["Horizontal root: gravity makes auxin accumulate on the lower side.", "横放根：生长素积累在下侧"], ["In the root, a high auxin concentration inhibits cell elongation → the lower side grows slower → the root bends downward (positive geotropism).", "根：高浓度抑制伸长→向下弯"], ["In the shoot, the same higher auxin concentration on the lower side promotes elongation → the shoot bends upward (negative geotropism).", "茎：下侧促进伸长→向上弯"], ["Roots are more sensitive to auxin than shoots; the same concentration can stimulate shoots and inhibit roots.", "根比茎对生长素更敏感"]], "", "Tip: say 'inhibits' for roots and 'promotes' for shoots."], ["Investigations on Auxin and Coleoptiles", "生长素的探究实验", [["Tip covered with foil or removed: the coleoptile does not bend towards light if the tip is covered or cut off; so the tip detects light and makes auxin.", "尖端遮光/切除：不向光弯曲"], ["Mica plate on the lit side has no effect; on the shaded side it blocks the movement of auxin, so no bending (Boysen-Jensen).", "云母片阻断生长素传递"], ["An agar block with auxin placed on one side of a cut stump makes it bend away from that side (Went).", "琼脂块放一侧：向对侧弯"], ["Variables: manipulated: tip covered/removed; responding: bending; fixed: light, temperature, age.", "变量"]], "", "Tip: the controls show the tip is essential."], ["Apical Dominance", "顶端优势", [["Apical dominance: the shoot tip produces auxin that moves down and inhibits the growth of lateral (axillary) buds.", "顶端优势：顶芽生长素抑制侧芽"], ["If the apical bud is removed (pruning), lateral buds grow and the plant becomes bushier.", "去顶芽→侧芽生长→更茂密"], ["Applying auxin to the cut stump again inhibits the lateral buds.", "在切口涂生长素又抑制侧芽"], ["Cytokinins counter auxin and promote lateral bud growth.", "细胞分裂素促进侧芽"]], "", "Tip: pruning hedges makes them thicker."], ["Gibberellins and Cytokinins", "赤霉素与细胞分裂素", [["Gibberellins: promote stem elongation (tall plants), break seed dormancy by stimulating amylase to break down starch in the seed, promote flowering and fruit growth.", "赤霉素：茎伸长、打破休眠、促淀粉酶"], ["Cytokinins: promote cell division, promote lateral bud growth and delay ageing (senescence) of leaves.", "细胞分裂素：促分裂、延缓衰老"], ["Auxin and cytokinin together control tissue culture: a high auxin/cytokinin ratio gives roots, a low ratio gives shoots.", "组织培养：比例决定生根或长芽"]], "", "Tip: gibberellin = growth; cytokinin = division."], ["Ethylene and Abscisic Acid", "乙烯与脱落酸", [["Ethylene (gas): speeds up fruit ripening (starch → sugar, softer cell walls, chlorophyll breakdown), leaf and fruit fall, flower fading.", "乙烯：催熟、脱落"], ["Ripening is a positive feedback: ripe fruit release ethylene which ripens nearby fruits; one rotten banana ripens the others.", "催熟是正反馈"], ["Abscisic acid (ABA): the stress hormone; closes stomata during drought, keeps seed and bud dormant, inhibits growth.", "脱落酸：干旱时关闭气孔；休眠"], ["Ethylene is a gas, so it spreads through the air.", "乙烯是气体"]], "", "Tip: ABA and gibberellins act oppositely on dormancy."], ["Summary Table of Phytohormones", "植物激素总结表", [["Auxin: elongation, tropism, apical dominance, rooting; made in apical meristems.", "生长素：伸长、向性、顶端优势、生根"], ["Gibberellins: stem elongation, germination, flowering; made in young leaves and seeds.", "赤霉素：伸长、萌发"], ["Cytokinins: cell division, delay senescence; made in roots.", "细胞分裂素：分裂、延缓衰老"], ["Ethylene: ripening, abscission; ABA: closes stomata, dormancy.", "乙烯：成熟；脱落酸：气孔、休眠"]], "", "Tip: learn one function for each hormone."], ["Applications of Phytohormones in Agriculture (1)", "植物激素在农业上的应用 (1)", [["Auxin rooting powder: cuttings dipped in auxin (e.g. IBA, NAA) develop roots faster.", "生根粉：扦插"], ["Selective weedkillers: synthetic auxin (2,4-D) kills broad-leaved (dicot) weeds in cereal and grass fields without harming monocots.", "选择性除草剂：2,4-D 杀双子叶杂草"], ["Seedless fruits (parthenocarpy): auxin or gibberellin sprayed on unpollinated flowers gives seedless tomatoes, watermelons and grapes.", "无籽果实"], ["Auxin sprays prevent premature fruit drop.", "防落果"]], "", "Tip: give the hormone, the use and the benefit."], ["Applications of Phytohormones in Agriculture (2)", "植物激素在农业上的应用 (2)", [["Gibberellins: larger seedless grapes, faster malting of barley for beer, longer sugarcane stems, uniform germination.", "赤霉素：葡萄、麦芽、甘蔗"], ["Cytokinins: tissue culture of orchids and oil palm; keep cut flowers and vegetables fresh.", "细胞分裂素：组织培养；保鲜"], ["Ethylene (ethephon): ripens bananas, pineapples and mangoes during transport; helps uniform harvest.", "乙烯：催熟香蕉、菠萝"], ["Concerns: overuse may harm the environment and health; growers must follow safe doses.", "须安全使用"]], "", "Tip: link each hormone to a Malaysian crop."], ["Worked Example: Explaining Plant Responses", "例题：解释植物反应", [["Q: Explain why a shoot bends towards light. A: Auxin moves to the shaded side → cells there elongate faster → bends toward the light.", "题：茎为何向光弯曲？答：生长素移向背光侧"], ["Q: Why does a horizontal root bend down? A: Auxin collects on the lower side and inhibits elongation, so the upper side grows faster.", "题：根为何向下弯？答：下侧生长受抑"], ["Q: Why does pruning make a plant bushier? A: Removing the apical bud lowers auxin, so lateral buds grow.", "题：为何修剪后更茂密？答：顶端优势消失"]], "", "Tip: use 'unequal growth' in every tropism answer."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Tropism (Tropisme); Phototropism (Fototropisme); Geotropism (Geotropisme); Nastic movement (Gerakan nasti)", "向性；向光性；向地性；感性运动"], ["Auxin (Auksin); Gibberellin (Giberelin); Cytokinin (Sitokinin); Ethylene (Etilena); Abscisic acid (Asid absisik)", "生长素；赤霉素；细胞分裂素；乙烯；脱落酸"], ["Apical dominance (Dominan apeks); Parthenocarpy (Partenokarpi)", "顶端优势；单性结实"]], "", "Tip: 'hormon tumbuhan' = plant hormone."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying auxin makes the shaded side grow slower; the shaded side grows faster.", "背光侧长得更快"], ["Writing that high auxin always promotes growth; in roots it inhibits elongation.", "根中高浓度抑制伸长"], ["Confusing tropism and nastic movements.", "混淆向性与感性"], ["Saying gibberellin is a gas; ethylene is the gas.", "乙烯才是气体"], ["Forgetting that the tip senses light and produces auxin.", "忘记尖端感光并产生生长素"]], "", "Tip: for 4 marks give mechanism + result."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: State two differences between tropism and nastic movement. J: Tropism is directional and involves growth; nastic is not directional and often involves turgor change.", "问：向性与感性两差异？答：向性定向、涉及生长；感性不定向、膨压变化"], ["S: Explain how auxin causes a shoot to bend towards light. J: Auxin accumulates on the shaded side, cells elongate more there, so the shoot bends towards the light.", "问：生长素如何使茎向光弯曲？答：背光侧积累、伸长更快"], ["S: Why can 2,4-D kill weeds in a paddy-like grass field? J: It is a synthetic auxin that kills dicot weeds but not monocot crops.", "问：2,4-D 为何能除杂草？答：杀双子叶不伤单子叶"], ["S: Why does one ripe banana ripen others? J: It releases ethylene, which speeds ripening.", "问：一只熟香蕉为何催熟其他？答：释放乙烯"], ["S: State one function of abscisic acid. J: Closes stomata during drought.", "问：脱落酸一功能？答：干旱时关气孔"]], "", ""]],"bio|T5-6":[["Structure of a Flower", "花的结构", [["A flower is the reproductive organ of a flowering plant; parts from outside inward: sepals (calyx), petals (corolla), stamens (male), carpels (female) on the receptacle.", "花：萼片、花瓣、雄蕊、心皮，着生于花托"], ["Sepals: protect the flower bud. Petals: often brightly coloured and scented to attract pollinators.", "萼片保护花蕾；花瓣吸引传粉者"], ["Stamen: anther (makes pollen grains) on a filament. Carpel (pistil): stigma (receives pollen), style (pollen tube grows through), ovary (contains ovules).", "雄蕊：花药+花丝；心皮：柱头、花柱、子房"], ["Bisexual (hermaphrodite) flowers have both stamens and carpels (hibiscus); unisexual flowers have only one (papaya, cucumber).", "两性花；单性花"]], "", "Tip: draw and label from the outside inward."], ["Functions of the Parts of a Flower", "花各部分的功能", [["Anther: contains pollen sacs where pollen forms; filament holds the anther in an exposed position.", "花药：产花粉；花丝托起"], ["Stigma: sticky or feathery to catch pollen; style: supports the stigma and the pollen tube grows through it.", "柱头捕花粉；花柱引导花粉管"], ["Ovary: protects the ovules and develops into the fruit; ovule: contains the embryo sac and develops into the seed.", "子房→果实；胚珠→种子"], ["Nectary: secretes nectar to attract insects.", "蜜腺：吸引昆虫"]], "", "Tip: ovary → fruit; ovule → seed."], ["Insect-Pollinated and Wind-Pollinated Flowers", "虫媒花与风媒花", [["Insect-pollinated: large, brightly coloured petals, scent, nectar; anthers and stigma inside the flower; small amount of sticky or spiky pollen.", "虫媒花：花瓣大、鲜艳、有香味和蜜；花粉少而粘"], ["Wind-pollinated: small, dull petals, no scent or nectar; anthers hang outside on long filaments; large feathery stigma outside; large amounts of light, smooth pollen.", "风媒花：花瓣小、无蜜；花药外露；柱头羽状；花粉多而轻"], ["Examples: hibiscus and orchid (insect); maize and grass (wind); durian (bat).", "例：木槿、兰花；玉米、禾草；榴莲（蝙蝠）"]], "", "Tip: link each feature to the pollinating agent."], ["Formation of Pollen Grains", "花粉的形成", [["The anther has four pollen sacs, each containing microspore mother cells (2n).", "花药有四个花粉囊：小孢子母细胞 (2n)"], ["Each microspore mother cell divides by meiosis → 4 haploid microspores (n).", "减数分裂→4 个小孢子 (n)"], ["Each microspore divides by mitosis → a pollen grain with a tube nucleus and a generative nucleus.", "有丝分裂→花粉粒：管核+生殖核"], ["The generative nucleus divides by mitosis to give 2 male gametes (n), before or after pollination; the pollen wall has an outer exine and inner intine.", "生殖核有丝分裂→2 个雄配子"]], "", "Tip: meiosis first, then mitosis."], ["Formation of the Embryo Sac", "胚囊的形成", [["The ovule has integuments with a small opening (micropyle) and a nucellus inside.", "胚珠：珠被、珠孔、珠心"], ["A megaspore mother cell (2n) divides by meiosis → 4 haploid megaspores; 3 degenerate and 1 survives.", "减数分裂→4 个大孢子，3 个退化"], ["The surviving megaspore divides by mitosis three times → 8 haploid nuclei in the embryo sac.", "三次有丝分裂→8 个核"], ["Arrangement: 1 egg cell and 2 synergids at the micropyle end, 3 antipodal cells at the opposite end, 2 polar nuclei in the centre (central cell).", "排列：卵细胞+2 助细胞在珠孔端；3 反足细胞；2 极核居中"]], "", "Tip: 8 nuclei = 1 egg + 2 synergids + 3 antipodals + 2 polar nuclei."], ["Pollination", "传粉", [["Pollination: the transfer of pollen from the anther to the stigma of a flower of the same species.", "传粉：花粉从花药到柱头"], ["Self-pollination: pollen goes to the stigma of the same flower or another flower on the same plant. Cross-pollination: to a flower on a different plant of the same species.", "自花传粉；异花传粉"], ["Agents: insects (bees), wind, water, birds and bats.", "媒介：昆虫、风、水、鸟、蝙蝠"], ["Cross-pollination gives more genetic variation and healthier offspring; self-pollination needs no agent but produces less variation.", "异花传粉变异多；自花传粉变异少"]], "", "Tip: always state 'same species'."], ["Fertilisation: Pollen Tube Growth", "受精：花粉管生长", [["On a compatible stigma the pollen grain absorbs sugary fluid and germinates → a pollen tube grows down the style, guided by chemicals (chemotropism).", "花粉萌发→花粉管沿花柱向下"], ["The tube nucleus leads and controls growth; the two male gametes follow inside the tube.", "管核引导；2 个雄配子随行"], ["The pollen tube enters the ovule through the micropyle and bursts into the embryo sac; the tube nucleus degenerates.", "经珠孔进入胚囊；管核退化"]], "", "Tip: pollen tube enters through the micropyle."], ["Double Fertilisation", "双受精", [["One male gamete (n) fuses with the egg cell (n) → zygote (2n) → develops into the embryo.", "一个雄配子+卵细胞→合子 (2n)→胚"], ["The other male gamete (n) fuses with the two polar nuclei (n + n) → a triploid endosperm nucleus (3n) → endosperm (food store).", "另一个雄配子+2 极核→三倍体胚乳核 (3n)"], ["It is called double fertilisation because two fusions occur; it is unique to flowering plants.", "两次融合：双受精，被子植物特有"], ["Synergids and antipodals degenerate.", "助细胞与反足细胞退化"]], "", "Tip: zygote = 2n; endosperm = 3n."], ["Development of Seed and Fruit", "种子与果实的发育", [["Zygote → embryo (plumule, radicle, cotyledon(s)); endosperm nucleus → endosperm; integuments → testa (seed coat); ovule → seed.", "合子→胚；珠被→种皮；胚珠→种子"], ["Ovary → fruit; ovary wall → pericarp; petals, stamens, style and stigma wither and fall off.", "子房→果实；子房壁→果皮"], ["Fruit protects the seeds and helps dispersal; examples: fleshy fruits (mango, tomato) and dry fruits (bean pod, rubber).", "果实保护种子并助传播"], ["Parthenocarpy: fruit develops without fertilisation, so it is seedless (banana, seedless watermelon).", "单性结实：无籽"]], "", "Tip: use 'develops into' arrows."], ["Structure of Seeds: Dicot and Monocot", "种子结构：双子叶与单子叶", [["Dicot (bean): two cotyledons store food; testa, micropyle, plumule and radicle; non-endospermic (food stored in the cotyledons).", "双子叶（豆）：子叶储存养分"], ["Monocot (maize): one cotyledon; endosperm stores food; coleoptile and coleorhiza protect the plumule and radicle.", "单子叶（玉米）：胚乳储存养分"], ["Seed germination needs water, oxygen and a suitable temperature (not light in most seeds).", "萌发：水、氧、适温"]], "", "Tip: bean = cotyledons store food; maize = endosperm."], ["Seed and Fruit Dispersal", "种子与果实的传播", [["Wind: light, winged or parachute fruits (dandelion, Tecoma, rubber seeds spin).", "风：蒲公英"], ["Water: fruits float with a fibrous husk (coconut, nipah).", "水：椰子"], ["Animals: hooked or sticky fruits cling to fur (Bidens); fleshy fruits are eaten and seeds pass through the gut (guava, rambutan).", "动物：钩刺；被食"], ["Explosive: the dry pod dries and splits, throwing seeds out (rubber, balsam, bean).", "弹射：橡胶树"]], "", "Tip: match each adaptation with its agent."], ["Importance of Seeds for Survival", "种子对生存的重要性", [["Seeds protect the embryo with a hard testa and can stay dormant until conditions are suitable.", "种子保护胚并可休眠"], ["Dispersal reduces competition and helps colonise new areas.", "传播减少竞争"], ["Food reserves (cotyledons or endosperm) feed the seedling until it can photosynthesise.", "养分供幼苗"], ["Sexual reproduction gives genetic variation, important for survival under changing conditions; seeds are our food (rice, beans, maize) and a source of oil.", "遗传变异；人类食物"]], "", "Tip: link each point to survival."], ["Worked Example: Chromosome Numbers", "例题：染色体数目", [["Q: A plant cell has 20 chromosomes (2n = 20). How many chromosomes are in a pollen grain nucleus? A: 10 (n), made by meiosis.", "题：2n=20，花粉核 → 10"], ["Q: How many chromosomes in the zygote and in the endosperm nucleus? A: Zygote 20 (2n); endosperm 30 (3n).", "题：合子 20；胚乳核 30"], ["Q: Why does the endosperm have three sets? A: One male gamete fuses with two polar nuclei (n + n + n).", "题：胚乳为何三倍？答：雄配子+2 极核"]], "", "Tip: show the working n + n + n."], ["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)", "重点术语（英文–马来文）", [["Stamen (Stamen); Carpel (Karpel); Ovule (Ovul); Stigma (Stigma); Pollen grain (Debunga)", "雄蕊；心皮；胚珠；柱头；花粉粒"], ["Pollination (Pendebungaan); Fertilisation (Persenyawaan); Embryo sac (Pundi embrio); Endosperm (Endosperma)", "传粉；受精；胚囊；胚乳"], ["Dispersal (Penyebaran); Germination (Percambahan); Parthenocarpy (Partenokarpi)", "传播；萌发；单性结实"]], "", "Tip: 'bunga' = flower."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Confusing pollination (transfer of pollen) with fertilisation (fusion of gametes).", "混淆传粉与受精"], ["Saying the ovary becomes the seed; the ovary becomes the fruit and the ovule becomes the seed.", "子房→果实；胚珠→种子"], ["Writing that endosperm is diploid; it is triploid (3n).", "胚乳是 3n"], ["Forgetting that the pollen tube enters through the micropyle.", "忘记珠孔"], ["Saying all flowers are insect-pollinated.", "并非都是虫媒"]], "", "Tip: for 'explain' questions give the sequence in order."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Name the parts of the male and female reproductive organs of a flower. J: Male: anther and filament; female: stigma, style and ovary.", "问：花的雄性与雌性器官？答：花药、花丝；柱头、花柱、子房"], ["S: State two features of a wind-pollinated flower. J: Feathery stigma outside the flower; anthers hanging outside producing light pollen.", "问：风媒花两特征？答：羽状柱头外露；花药外悬、花粉轻"], ["S: Describe double fertilisation. J: One male gamete fuses with the egg cell → zygote; the other fuses with two polar nuclei → triploid endosperm nucleus.", "问：双受精？答：雄配子+卵→合子；雄配子+2 极核→胚乳核"], ["S: What do the ovule and the ovary develop into? J: Seed; fruit.", "问：胚珠和子房发育成？答：种子；果实"], ["S: Give two ways seeds are dispersed. J: By wind (winged seeds) and by animals (fleshy fruit eaten).", "问：两种传播方式？答：风；动物"]], "", ""]]};
const PPTS_BIO2={"bio|T5-7":[["Habitats and Adaptations of Plants","植物的生境与适应",[["Habitat: the natural place where an organism lives. Adaptation: a structural, physiological or behavioural feature that helps an organism survive in its habitat.","生境：生物生活的自然环境；适应：帮助生存的结构、生理或行为特征"],["Plants are grouped by habitat: hydrophytes (water), xerophytes (dry), mesophytes (moderate water) and halophytes (saline).","按生境分类：水生、旱生、中生、盐生植物"],["Each group shows adaptations in leaves, stems, roots and stomata that control water uptake, water loss and gas exchange.","各组在叶、茎、根与气孔上有适应特征，调控吸水、失水与气体交换"],["Plants adapt to water availability, salinity, light and soil conditions.","植物适应水分、盐度、光照与土壤条件"]],"","Tip: write the feature + how it helps survival, e.g. 'sunken stomata trap moist air → less transpiration'."],["Hydrophytes: Aquatic Plants","水生植物",[["Floating hydrophytes (water lily, water hyacinth): stomata mostly on the upper surface exposed to air; broad flat leaves float and receive light; thin cuticle; long flexible petioles and stems that bend with the water.","漂浮植物：气孔多在上表皮；叶宽平漂浮；表皮薄；叶柄长而柔软"],["Large air spaces (aerenchyma) in leaves, petioles and stems: give buoyancy and store oxygen and CO₂. Water hyacinth has swollen petioles filled with air.","通气组织(气室)：提供浮力并储存气体；凤眼莲叶柄膨大充气"],["Submerged hydrophytes (Hydrilla): thin, narrow or finely divided leaves → large surface area to absorb CO₂, light and minerals directly from the water; no or very thin cuticle; few or no stomata.","沉水植物（黑藻）：叶薄细裂，表面积大，直接吸收CO₂、光、矿物质；无气孔"],["Poorly developed roots and xylem because water and minerals are absorbed over the whole surface; weak stems supported by water.","根与木质部不发达；茎柔弱靠水支持"]],"","Tip: aquatic plants need no cuticle and little xylem because water is everywhere."],["Xerophytes: Dry-Habitat Plants","旱生植物",[["Cactus: thick, fleshy stem stores water; leaves reduced to spines (small surface area, protection from herbivores); thick waxy cuticle; photosynthesis occurs in the green stem.","仙人掌：肉质茎储水；叶退化成刺；厚蜡质表皮；茎光合"],["Sunken stomata and fewer stomata: moist air is trapped near the stomata, reducing transpiration. Leaf hairs trap moisture and reflect light.","气孔下陷且少；毛茸茸困住湿气"],["Rolled leaves (marram grass): stomata inside the roll, humid air trapped, exposed surface reduced. Thick cuticle and leathery leaves (pineapple, oleander).","卷叶（沙草）：气孔在卷内；厚角质层与革质叶"],["Roots: widespread shallow roots absorb rain quickly, or very long tap roots reach deep water. Physiological: some xerophytes open stomata at night (CAM) to reduce water loss; some shed leaves in the dry season.","根：浅而广或深长直根；夜间开气孔(CAM)；旱季落叶"]],"","Tip: aim for 'reduce water loss' and 'store water' in every xerophyte answer."],["Mesophytes and Comparison of Plant Groups","中生植物与各类比较",[["Mesophytes (hibiscus, mango, bean) live where water supply is moderate: broad thin leaves; thin cuticle; stomata mostly on the lower epidermis; well-developed roots and vascular tissue.","中生植物：叶宽薄；表皮薄；气孔多在下表皮；根与维管发达"],["Hydrophyte: stomata on upper surface; large air spaces; poor roots. Xerophyte: thick cuticle; sunken stomata; reduced leaves; fleshy stem.","水生：上表皮气孔、气室大、根弱；旱生：厚角质、气孔下陷、叶小、肉质茎"],["Halophyte: salt glands; pneumatophores/prop roots; succulent leaves; viviparous seeds.","盐生：盐腺；呼吸根/支柱根；肉质叶；胎生种子"],["A comparison table should include: leaf size/shape, cuticle, stomata position, roots, special structures and example.","比较表要含：叶、角质层、气孔位置、根、特殊结构、例子"]],"","Tip: use the same headings for every plant group in a comparison table."],["Halophytes: Mangrove Plants","盐生植物：红树林",[["Mangrove habitat: salty, waterlogged, muddy, unstable soil with little oxygen, and daily tides.","红树林生境：盐、积水、泥泞不稳、缺氧、有潮汐"],["Prop (stilt) roots (Rhizophora) and buttress roots anchor the plant in soft mud; knee roots (Bruguiera).","支柱根固定于软泥；膝状根"],["Pneumatophores (breathing roots, Avicennia and Sonneratia) grow upward out of the mud and have lenticels/pores for gas exchange in oxygen-poor soil.","呼吸根（海榄雌、海桑）伸出泥面，有皮孔供气体交换"],["Salt control: salt glands on the leaves excrete salt; some salt is stored in old leaves that drop; thick waxy cuticle and succulent leaves store water; cell sap has a high solute concentration so water can enter roots.","盐控制：叶盐腺排盐；老叶积盐落叶；厚蜡质；肉质叶储水；细胞液浓度高"],["Viviparous germination: seeds germinate while still on the parent plant; the long propagules fall and stick in the mud, giving rapid anchorage (Rhizophora).","胎生萌发：种子在母树上发芽，长胚轴落下插入泥中"]],"","Tip: link each mangrove adaptation to one problem: salt, waterlogging or unstable mud."],["Investigation and Importance of Mangroves","探究与红树林的重要性",[["Investigation: compare leaf structures of hydrophyte, xerophyte and mesophyte by cutting transverse sections and observing under the microscope; count stomata using a nail-varnish peel.","探究：比较三类叶的横切面；用指甲油法数气孔"],["Expected results: hydrophyte has large air spaces; xerophyte has a thick cuticle and sunken stomata; mesophyte has palisade and spongy layers.","预期：水生叶多气室；旱生叶厚角质、气孔下陷；中生叶有栅栏与海绵组织"],["Importance of mangroves: protect the coast from erosion and waves; nursery for fish, prawns and crabs; absorb carbon dioxide; filter pollutants; source of wood and ecotourism.","红树林重要性：防海岸侵蚀；鱼虾蟹育幼场；吸CO₂；过滤污染；木材与生态旅游"],["Conservation: Matang Mangrove Forest Reserve in Perak is a well-managed mangrove forest.","保护：霹雳话望生红树林保护区为管理良好的例子"]],"","Tip: describe the observation under the microscope as 'large air spaces' etc., not just 'different'."],["Problems and Solutions: Plant Adaptations","问题与对策：植物适应",[["Too little water (desert): store water in stems/leaves, reduce leaf area, thick cuticle, sunken stomata, deep or widespread roots.","缺水：储水、减叶面积、厚角质、气孔下陷、深/广根"],["Too much water (aquatic): air spaces for buoyancy and gas storage, flexible stems, stomata on the upper surface of floating leaves, reduced roots.","水多：气室、柔韧茎、上表皮气孔、根退化"],["Salt and unstable mud (mangrove): salt glands, prop roots, pneumatophores, viviparous seeds.","盐与泥：盐腺、支柱根、呼吸根、胎生"],["Moderate water (mesophyte): broad thin leaves for photosynthesis, stomata mainly on the lower surface, well-developed vascular system.","水适中：宽薄叶、下表皮气孔、维管发达"],["Light competition: climbers (tendrils), epiphytes on tall trees, shade plants with large leaves.","光竞争：攀缘植物、附生植物、阴生植物"]],"","Tip: set out as 'problem → adaptation → how it helps'."],["Worked Example: Interpreting Leaf Sections","例题：解读叶切面",[["Q: A leaf section shows large air spaces and stomata only on the upper surface. Which plant is it? A: A floating hydrophyte (water lily) — the air spaces give buoyancy; the stomata on the upper surface contact the air.","题：大气室、气孔仅在上表皮→漂浮水生植物（睡莲）"],["Q: A plant has sunken stomata in a pit lined with hairs and rolled leaves. A: A xerophyte — humid air is trapped, reducing transpiration.","题：气孔在毛坑内、卷叶→旱生植物"],["Q: Why do mangrove roots grow upward out of the mud? A: To obtain oxygen for gas exchange in waterlogged, oxygen-poor soil.","题：红树根为何向上伸出泥面？答：泥中缺氧，需交换气体"],["Q: Why do desert plants have shallow wide roots? A: To absorb rain water quickly before it evaporates or drains away.","题：沙漠植物为何浅而广的根？答：快速吸收少量雨水"]],"","Tip: first identify the plant group, then link each feature to its function."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Habitat (Habitat); Adaptation (Penyesuaian); Hydrophyte (Hidrofit); Xerophyte (Xerofit)","生境；适应；水生植物；旱生植物"],["Mesophyte (Mesofit); Halophyte (Halofit); Mangrove (Bakau); Pneumatophore (Akar pernafasan)","中生植物；盐生植物；红树；呼吸根"],["Stomata (Stoma); Cuticle (Kutikel); Succulent (Sukulen); Air space (Ruang udara)","气孔；角质层；多汁植物；气室"]],"","Tip: 'akar topang' = prop roots."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Writing 'the plant has a thick cuticle' without saying why (reduces water loss).","只写特征不写作用"],["Saying hydrophytes have thick cuticle or many stomata on the lower surface (floating leaves have stomata on the upper surface).","水生植物不是厚角质层；漂浮叶气孔在上表皮"],["Confusing pneumatophores (breathing roots) with prop roots (anchorage).","混淆呼吸根与支柱根"],["Forgetting examples of plants in comparison questions.","比较题忘记举例"]],"","Tip: remember one example per plant group."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Why do water lily leaves have stomata on the upper surface? J: The upper surface is exposed to air for gas exchange.","问：睡莲叶气孔为何在上表皮？答：上表皮接触空气，便于气体交换"],["S: State two ways a cactus reduces water loss. J: Leaves reduced to spines; thick waxy cuticle; sunken stomata.","问：仙人掌减少失水的两种方式？答：叶变刺；厚蜡质；气孔下陷"],["S: What is the function of pneumatophores? J: Gas exchange for roots in waterlogged, oxygen-poor mud.","问：呼吸根作用？答：缺氧泥地中根的气体交换"],["S: What is viviparous germination? J: Seeds germinate while still attached to the parent plant.","问：胎生萌发？答：种子仍在母树上就发芽"],["S: How do mangroves cope with salty water? J: Salt glands excrete salt; salt stored in old leaves; high cell sap concentration.","问：红树如何应对盐？答：盐腺排盐；老叶储盐；细胞液浓度高"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-8":[["Levels of Biodiversity","生物多样性层次",[["Biodiversity: the variety of living organisms in an area, including genetic diversity, species diversity and ecosystem diversity.","生物多样性：遗传、物种、生态系统多样性"],["Genetic diversity: variation in genes within a species (e.g. different varieties of rice or dog breeds).","遗传多样性：同种内基因差异"],["Species diversity: the number of different species and how evenly they are distributed in an area.","物种多样性：物种数目与分布均匀度"],["Ecosystem diversity: variety of habitats, communities and ecological processes (rainforest, mangrove, coral reef, peat swamp).","生态系统多样性：雨林、红树林、珊瑚礁、泥炭沼泽"],["Malaysia is one of the world's megadiverse countries, with tropical rainforests rich in species.","马来西亚是全球megadiverse（超多样性）国家之一"]],"","Tip: give one example for each level of biodiversity."],["Taxonomy and Binomial Nomenclature","分类学与双名法",[["Classification groups organisms based on similarities and differences. Reasons: easier to study and identify organisms, shows evolutionary relationships, helps communication and conservation.","分类：按异同分组，便于研究、反映亲缘关系、利于沟通与保护"],["Taxonomic hierarchy: Domain → Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order → Family → Genus → Species.","分类阶元：域→界→门→纲→目→科→属→种"],["Species: a group of organisms that can interbreed to produce fertile offspring.","物种：能交配并产生可育后代的群体"],["Binomial nomenclature (Carolus Linnaeus): scientific name = Genus (capital letter) + species (small letter), written in italics or underlined, e.g. Homo sapiens, Hibiscus rosa-sinensis.","双名法：属名(大写)+种加词(小写)；斜体或下划线"]],"","Tip: underline the two names separately when writing by hand."],["Domains and Kingdoms","域与界",[["Three domains: Archaea (extremophile prokaryotes), Bacteria (true bacteria, prokaryotes) and Eukarya (organisms with a nucleus).","三域：古菌域、细菌域、真核生物域"],["Kingdoms of Eukarya: Protista (mostly unicellular; Amoeba, Euglena, algae), Fungi (heterotrophic, chitin cell walls, absorb food; mushroom, yeast, mould), Plantae (multicellular autotrophs with cellulose walls), Animalia (multicellular heterotrophs, no cell walls).","真核界：原生生物界、真菌界、植物界、动物界"],["Prokaryotes have no nucleus and no membrane-bound organelles; DNA is circular and free in the cytoplasm.","原核生物无核膜、无膜细胞器"],["Viruses are not classified in a kingdom — they are non-cellular and can reproduce only inside a host cell.","病毒不属于任何界：非细胞，只能在宿主细胞内繁殖"]],"","Tip: fungi absorb food after digesting externally — they do not photosynthesise."],["Classification of Plants","植物的分类",[["Bryophyta (mosses, liverworts): no true roots, stems or leaves; no vascular tissue; reproduce by spores; live in damp places.","苔藓植物：无真根茎叶、无维管；孢子繁殖；生于潮湿处"],["Pteridophyta (ferns): true roots, stems and leaves; vascular tissue present; reproduce by spores formed in sporangia.","蕨类：有真根茎叶、有维管；孢子囊产孢子"],["Gymnosperms (pine, cycad): produce seeds in cones; seeds not enclosed in fruit; vascular tissue.","裸子植物：球果产种子；无果实包被"],["Angiosperms (flowering plants): flowers; seeds enclosed in fruit; monocotyledons (one cotyledon, parallel veins) and dicotyledons (two cotyledons, net veins).","被子植物：有花；种子在果实内；单子叶、双子叶"]],"","Tip: classification of plants is by vascular tissue, seeds, flowers and fruits."],["Classification of Invertebrates","无脊椎动物的分类",[["Porifera (sponges): pores; no true tissues. Cnidaria (jellyfish, sea anemone): radial symmetry, stinging cells.","多孔动物；刺胞动物"],["Platyhelminthes (flatworms, tapeworm): flat unsegmented body. Nematoda (roundworms): round unsegmented body, tapered ends. Annelida (earthworm, leech): segmented body.","扁形动物；线形动物；环节动物"],["Arthropoda (insects, crustaceans, arachnids, centipedes): jointed legs, chitin exoskeleton. Mollusca (snails, squids): soft body, often with shell. Echinodermata (starfish, sea urchin): spiny skin, tube feet.","节肢动物；软体动物；棘皮动物"]],"","Tip: use body symmetry, segmentation, skeleton and appendages as classification features."],["Classification of Vertebrates","脊椎动物的分类",[["Fish: gills, scales, fins, cold-blooded, lay eggs in water. Amphibians: moist skin, gills (larva) then lungs, lay eggs in water.","鱼类：鳃、鳞、鳍；两栖类：湿润皮肤、幼体鳃成体肺"],["Reptiles: dry scaly skin, lungs, lay shelled eggs on land, cold-blooded. Birds: feathers, wings, beak, lay hard-shelled eggs, warm-blooded.","爬行类：干燥鳞皮、陆上产硬壳卵；鸟类：羽毛、翅、喙"],["Mammals: hair/fur, mammary glands, give birth to live young (except monotremes), warm-blooded, diaphragm.","哺乳类：毛发、乳腺、胎生、恒温、膈肌"],["Cold-blooded (ectotherms) vs warm-blooded (endotherms): body temperature changes with environment vs stays constant.","变温 vs 恒温"]],"","Tip: put the vertebrate classes in a table with skin, breathing organs, reproduction, body temperature."],["Dichotomous Keys","二歧检索表",[["A dichotomous key identifies organisms using paired contrasting statements; each step has two choices that lead to another step or to the name of the organism.","二歧检索表：用成对对立描述逐步鉴别"],["Rules: use observable features (not size or colour alone); each pair must be contrasting; number the steps; end with the organism's name.","规则：用可观察特征；成对对立；编号；最后给出名称"],["Example: 1a Has wings → 2; 1b No wings → 3. 2a One pair of wings → fly; 2b Two pairs of wings → butterfly.","例：1a有翅→2；1b无翅→3；2a一对翅→蝇；2b两对翅→蝴蝶"],["Cladograms show evolutionary relationships (extension).","分支图显示进化关系（拓展）"]],"","Tip: do not use words like 'big' or 'small' in a key — use clear characteristics."],["Importance of Biodiversity","生物多样性的重要性",[["Food and agriculture: crop varieties and wild relatives provide genes for disease resistance and yield.","食物与农业：品种与野生近缘提供抗病高产基因"],["Medicine: quinine (from Cinchona) for malaria; Taxol from yew for cancer; many traditional medicines (e.g. tongkat ali); potential new drugs.","医药：奎宁、紫杉醇、传统药材；潜在新药"],["Economy: timber, rubber, tourism (ecotourism), fisheries, raw materials.","经济：木材、橡胶、旅游、渔业"],["Ecological balance: pollination, seed dispersal, decomposition, nutrient recycling, climate regulation, soil protection and water cycle.","生态平衡：授粉、传播种子、分解、养分循环、气候调节"],["Scientific research, education, cultural and aesthetic values.","科研、教育、文化与美学价值"]],"","Tip: classify the importance into economic, ecological, medical and aesthetic."],["Threats to Biodiversity","生物多样性的威胁",[["Habitat loss and fragmentation (deforestation, urbanisation, agriculture), overexploitation (hunting, illegal wildlife trade), pollution, invasive species and climate change.","栖息地丧失与破碎、过度开发、污染、入侵物种、气候变化"],["Malaysian examples of endangered species: Malayan tiger, orang utan, Malayan sun bear, hawksbill turtle, Rafflesia; the Sumatran rhinoceros is regarded as extinct in Malaysia.","濒危物种：马来虎、红毛猩猩、马来熊、玳瑁、大王花；苏门答腊犀牛在马来西亚被视为灭绝"],["Extinction: when the last individual of a species dies. Loss of one species affects other species in the food web.","灭绝：最后一个个体死亡；影响食物网"],["IUCN Red List categories: Extinct, Extinct in the Wild, Critically Endangered, Endangered, Vulnerable, Near Threatened, Least Concern.","IUCN红色名录等级"]],"","Tip: give a threat + its effect + one example."],["Preservation and Conservation","保存与保护",[["Preservation: protecting species and habitats in their natural state without human use. Conservation: sustainable use and management of natural resources.","保存：保持原状不使用；保育：可持续使用与管理"],["In situ conservation (in the natural habitat): national parks (Taman Negara, Kinabalu Park), wildlife reserves, forest reserves, marine parks (Pulau Payar), sanctuaries.","就地保护：国家公园、野生动物保护区、森林保护区、海洋公园"],["Ex situ conservation (outside the habitat): zoos, botanical gardens, captive breeding, seed banks, gene banks, tissue culture, aquariums.","迁地保护：动物园、植物园、圈养繁殖、种子库、基因库、组织培养"],["Advantages of in situ: natural environment, whole ecosystem protected. Advantages of ex situ: protects species near extinction, allows research and breeding.","就地：保护整个生态系统；迁地：保护濒临灭绝物种、可研究繁殖"]],"","Tip: always state whether the example is in situ or ex situ."],["Laws, Cooperation and Public Awareness","法律、合作与公众意识",[["Malaysian laws: National Parks Act 1980, Wildlife Conservation Act 2010, International Trade in Endangered Species Act 2008, Fisheries Act, Environmental Quality Act 1974.","马来西亚法律：国家公园法令、野生动物保护法令、濒危物种国际贸易法令、环境质量法令"],["International agreements: CITES (controls trade in endangered species), Convention on Biological Diversity (1992), Ramsar Convention (wetlands).","国际协定：CITES、生物多样性公约、拉姆萨尔湿地公约"],["Public awareness and education: campaigns, eco-tourism, school programmes, NGO work (WWF Malaysia, Malaysian Nature Society).","公众教育：宣传、生态旅游、学校活动、非政府组织"],["Sustainable use: sustainable logging, fishing quotas, replanting, and research and monitoring.","可持续利用：可持续伐木、捕鱼配额、重新种植、研究监测"]],"","Tip: link every law or agreement to what it protects."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Biodiversity (Biodiversiti); Species (Spesies); Genus (Genus); Kingdom (Kingdom); Domain (Domain)","生物多样性；物种；属；界；域"],["Binomial nomenclature (Tatanama binomial); Dichotomous key (Kekunci dikotomi)","双名法；二歧检索表"],["Conservation (Pemuliharaan); Preservation (Pemeliharaan); In situ (In situ); Ex situ (Ex situ)","保育；保存；就地；迁地"],["Endangered (Terancam); Extinct (Pupus); Invertebrate (Invertebrat); Vertebrate (Vertebrat)","濒危；灭绝；无脊椎；脊椎"]],"","Tip: 'pemuliharaan' = conservation; 'pemeliharaan' = preservation."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Mixing up conservation (sustainable use) and preservation (no use).","混淆保育与保存"],["Writing scientific names without capital for the genus or without italics/underlining.","学名写法错误"],["Classifying viruses into a kingdom, or fungi as plants.","把病毒列入界；真菌当植物"],["Writing dichotomous keys with vague features such as 'big' and 'small'.","检索表用含糊特征"],["Giving only a definition of biodiversity without examples at each level.","只写定义不举例"]],"","Tip: use Malaysian examples to earn the extra mark."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Name the three levels of biodiversity. J: Genetic, species and ecosystem diversity.","问：生物多样性三个层次？答：遗传、物种、生态系统多样性"],["S: Write the scientific name of humans correctly. J: Homo sapiens (genus with a capital letter, species with a small letter, italics/underlined).","问：人类学名怎么写？答：Homo sapiens，属名大写，种加词小写，斜体或下划线"],["S: Give two features of insects. J: Jointed legs and chitin exoskeleton; three pairs of legs.","问：昆虫两特征？答：分节附肢、几丁质外骨骼；三对足"],["S: State one example of ex situ conservation. J: Zoo, botanical garden, seed bank or gene bank.","问：迁地保护例子？答：动物园、植物园、种子库、基因库"],["S: What does CITES control? J: International trade in endangered species.","问：CITES管制什么？答：濒危物种的国际贸易"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-9":[["Components of an Ecosystem","生态系统的组成",[["Ecosystem: a community of living organisms interacting with each other and with their physical environment.","生态系统：生物群落与非生物环境相互作用"],["Abiotic factors: light, temperature, water, humidity, pH, soil, wind, salinity. Biotic factors: producers, consumers, decomposers.","非生物因素：光、温度、水、湿度、pH、土壤、风；生物因素：生产者、消费者、分解者"],["Terms: habitat (where an organism lives), population (same species in an area), community (all populations in an area), ecosystem (community + abiotic factors), biosphere (all ecosystems), niche (role of an organism in the ecosystem).","术语：生境、种群、群落、生态系统、生物圈、生态位"],["Levels: individual → population → community → ecosystem → biosphere.","层次：个体→种群→群落→生态系统→生物圈"]],"","Tip: define each ecological term with an example from the same ecosystem."],["Trophic Levels and Food Chains","营养级与食物链",[["Producers (autotrophs) make food by photosynthesis. Primary consumers (herbivores) eat producers; secondary consumers (carnivores/omnivores) eat herbivores; tertiary consumers eat secondary consumers.","生产者；初级、次级、三级消费者"],["Decomposers (bacteria, fungi) break down dead organisms and release nutrients back to the soil. Detritivores (earthworms) eat dead organic matter.","分解者；碎屑食者"],["Food chain: a sequence showing who eats whom; arrows show the direction of energy flow, e.g. grass → grasshopper → frog → snake → eagle.","食物链：箭头表示能量流向"],["Food web: interconnected food chains; more stable than a single food chain because organisms have alternative food sources.","食物网：多条链相连；更稳定"]],"","Tip: arrows point to the organism that gets the energy (from prey to predator)."],["Energy Flow and Ecological Pyramids","能量流动与生态金字塔",[["Energy flows one way: Sun → producers → consumers; at each trophic level only about 10% of the energy is passed to the next level.","能量单向流动；每级约10%传至下一级"],["Energy is lost as heat through respiration, in faeces and urine, and in parts not eaten (bones, roots). Therefore food chains have only 4–5 trophic levels.","能量以呼吸热、排泄物、未食部分损失；食物链通常4–5级"],["Pyramid of numbers (can be inverted, e.g. one tree supports many insects), pyramid of biomass (usually upright) and pyramid of energy (always upright).","数量金字塔可能倒置；生物量；能量金字塔总是正立"],["Example: producers 10 000 kJ → primary consumers 1 000 kJ → secondary consumers 100 kJ → tertiary consumers 10 kJ.","例：10000→1000→100→10 kJ"]],"","Tip: the pyramid of energy cannot be inverted because energy is lost at each level."],["Carbon Cycle","碳循环",[["Carbon enters the biotic community as CO₂ through photosynthesis and moves along food chains as organic compounds.","CO₂经光合作用进入生物，沿食物链传递"],["Carbon returns to the air as CO₂ through respiration (plants, animals, microorganisms), decomposition of dead organisms, and combustion of wood and fossil fuels.","经呼吸、分解、燃烧回到大气"],["Fossil fuels form from dead organisms buried over millions of years; burning them releases stored carbon.","化石燃料由埋藏生物形成，燃烧释放碳"],["Human activities (deforestation, burning fossil fuels) increase CO₂ in the atmosphere, causing global warming.","人类活动使CO₂增加，导致全球变暖"]],"","Tip: draw the cycle with arrows labelled photosynthesis, respiration, decomposition and combustion."],["Nitrogen Cycle","氮循环",[["Nitrogen fixation: Rhizobium in legume root nodules, Azotobacter (free-living) and lightning convert N₂ into ammonium compounds/nitrates.","固氮：根瘤菌、固氮菌、闪电"],["Nitrification: Nitrosomonas converts ammonium to nitrite; Nitrobacter converts nitrite to nitrate. Plants absorb nitrate and use it for amino acids and proteins (assimilation).","硝化：亚硝化菌→亚硝酸盐；硝化菌→硝酸盐；植物吸收"],["Ammonification: decomposers break down proteins in dead organisms and urea into ammonium compounds.","氨化：分解者把蛋白质、尿素变成铵"],["Denitrification: denitrifying bacteria convert nitrate back to nitrogen gas in waterlogged soil, returning it to the air.","反硝化：细菌把硝酸盐还原成N₂"],["Fertilisers and crop rotation with legumes maintain soil nitrogen.","施肥与豆科轮作维持土壤氮"]],"","Tip: name the bacteria and the product of each stage in the cycle."],["Interactions Between Organisms","生物间的相互作用",[["Mutualism (both benefit): lichen (alga + fungus), Rhizobium and legumes, mycorrhiza, cleaner fish and large fish.","互利共生：地衣、根瘤菌、菌根"],["Commensalism (one benefits, other unaffected): orchids on trees, remora on shark, barnacles on whales.","偏利共生：附生兰、鮣鱼、藤壶"],["Parasitism (one benefits, host harmed): tapeworm, flea, mistletoe, Plasmodium, Rafflesia.","寄生：绦虫、跳蚤、寄生藤、疟原虫"],["Predation: predator kills and eats prey. Competition: organisms compete for resources — intraspecific (same species) and interspecific (different species).","捕食；竞争：种内竞争与种间竞争"]],"","Tip: say who benefits and who is harmed in each symbiosis."],["Population Dynamics","种群动态",[["Population size changes through natality (births), mortality (deaths), immigration and emigration.","种群大小受出生、死亡、迁入、迁出影响"],["Population growth curve: S-shaped — lag phase, exponential phase, stationary phase when the carrying capacity is reached.","种群生长曲线S形：延滞期、指数期、稳定期（环境容纳量）"],["Limiting factors: food, space, predators, disease, water, temperature. Predator–prey populations rise and fall in cycles.","限制因素：食物、空间、天敌、疾病；捕食者—猎物周期变化"],["Interspecific competition may lead to competitive exclusion of the weaker species.","种间竞争可能导致较弱者被排除"]],"","Tip: explain a plateau using 'limiting factors' and 'carrying capacity'."],["Sampling Techniques","取样技术",[["Quadrat: used for plants and slow-moving animals; place at random; count species and calculate density, frequency and percentage cover.","样方：用于植物与行动慢的动物；随机放置"],["Line transect and belt transect: study changes across a gradient (e.g. from shore to land).","样线与样带：研究梯度变化"],["Mark–release–recapture (mobile animals): population = (number marked first × total second catch) ÷ number marked in the second catch.","标记重捕：N＝(M×n)÷m"],["Example: 50 marked; second catch 40 with 10 marked → N = (50 × 40) ÷ 10 = 200.","例：N＝50×40÷10＝200"],["Other methods: pitfall trap (ground insects), sweep net, light trap, Berlese funnel (soil organisms).","其他：陷阱、扫网、灯诱、柏利斯漏斗"]],"","Tip: state assumptions of mark–recapture: marks do not fade, no migration, random mixing."],["Quadrat Calculations and Abiotic Measurements","样方计算与非生物因素测量",[["Population density = total number of individuals ÷ total area sampled.","种群密度＝个体总数÷取样总面积"],["Example: mean 8 plants per 0.25 m² quadrat; area 100 m² → 8 × (100 ÷ 0.25) = 3 200 plants.","例：8×(100÷0.25)＝3200"],["Measuring abiotic factors: light meter (light intensity), thermometer (temperature), soil pH meter, hygrometer (humidity), anemometer (wind), soil moisture meter.","非生物测量：光度计、温度计、pH计、湿度计、风速计"],["Take readings repeatedly and calculate the mean; choose random sampling to avoid bias.","重复取读数求平均；随机取样"]],"","Tip: show formula, substitution and units in every calculation."],["Ecological Succession","生态演替",[["Primary succession: starts on bare rock or new land; pioneer species (lichens, mosses) → grasses → shrubs → trees → climax community.","初级演替：裸岩上先锋(地衣、苔藓)→草→灌木→树→顶极群落"],["Secondary succession: occurs after a disturbance (fire, logging, landslide) where soil is present; faster.","次级演替：干扰后土壤仍在，较快"],["Changes during succession: soil depth and fertility increase; species diversity, biomass and shade increase; the environment becomes stable.","变化：土壤增厚肥沃；多样性、生物量增加"],["Climax community: a stable community in balance with climate (e.g. tropical rainforest).","顶极群落：稳定，与气候平衡"]],"","Tip: succession involves pioneer species changing the environment for others."],["Balance and Disturbance of Ecosystems","生态系统的平衡与干扰",[["Ecosystem balance (dynamic equilibrium): populations fluctuate around a stable level thanks to feedback, food webs and nutrient cycling.","生态平衡：动态平衡"],["Disturbances: deforestation, pollution, introduction of invasive species, overhunting, natural disasters.","干扰：砍伐、污染、入侵物种、过度捕猎"],["Biological control: use of natural predators or parasites (e.g. barn owls to control rats in oil palm estates) reduces chemical use.","生物防治：如用仓鸮防治油棕园老鼠"],["Biomagnification: non-biodegradable toxins (DDT, mercury) become more concentrated along the food chain, so top consumers are most affected.","生物放大：不可降解毒素沿食物链浓缩"]],"","Tip: biological control must be tested to avoid it becoming an invasive species."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Ecosystem (Ekosistem); Habitat (Habitat); Population (Populasi); Community (Komuniti); Niche (Relung)","生态系统；生境；种群；群落；生态位"],["Producer (Pengeluar); Consumer (Pengguna); Decomposer (Pengurai); Food chain (Rantai makanan)","生产者；消费者；分解者；食物链"],["Mutualism (Mutualisme); Commensalism (Komensalisme); Parasitism (Parasitisme); Predation (Pemangsaan)","互利；偏利；寄生；捕食"],["Succession (Sesaran); Quadrat (Kuadrat); Transect (Transek); Biomagnification (Pembesaran biologi)","演替；样方；样线；生物放大"]],"","Tip: 'sesaran' = succession."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Drawing food chain arrows from predator to prey — arrows show energy flow from prey to predator.","箭头方向画反"],["Saying 100% of energy passes to the next trophic level — only about 10%.","能量只传约10%"],["Mixing up nitrification and denitrification.","混淆硝化与反硝化"],["Confusing commensalism and mutualism: in commensalism the other organism is not affected.","混淆偏利与互利"],["Forgetting to state assumptions of mark–recapture.","忘记标记重捕的假设"]],"","Tip: practise drawing the carbon and nitrogen cycles."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Why are food chains short? J: Only about 10% of energy is passed to the next trophic level, so little energy remains for higher levels.","问：食物链为何短？答：每级仅传约10%，高营养级能量太少"],["S: Name the bacteria that fix nitrogen in legume root nodules. J: Rhizobium.","问：根瘤中固氮菌？答：根瘤菌"],["S: 60 beetles marked; second sample 50 with 15 marked. Estimate the population. J: (60 × 50) ÷ 15 = 200.","问：标记60，二次50只含15标记，估算？答：60×50÷15＝200"],["S: Give one example each of mutualism and parasitism. J: Lichen (mutualism); tapeworm (parasitism).","问：互利、寄生各一例？答：地衣；绦虫"],["S: What is biomagnification? J: Increase in concentration of non-biodegradable toxins along the food chain.","问：生物放大？答：不可降解毒素沿食物链浓度升高"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-10":[["Environmental Issues: Overview","环境问题概览",[["Main issues: air pollution, water pollution, soil pollution, noise pollution, deforestation, global warming, ozone depletion and loss of biodiversity.","主要问题：空气、水、土壤、噪音污染；砍伐；全球变暖；臭氧层破坏；生物多样性丧失"],["Causes are mostly human activities: industry, transport, agriculture, open burning, urbanisation, overuse of resources and improper waste disposal.","原因主要是人类活动"],["Environmental problems cross borders (e.g. haze, climate change) and need cooperation.","环境问题跨国界，需要合作"],["Sustainability: use resources so that future generations can meet their needs too.","可持续：不损害后代满足需求的能力"]],"","Tip: for each issue give cause → effect → solution."],["Air Pollution and Acid Rain","空气污染与酸雨",[["Pollutants: carbon monoxide (incomplete combustion), carbon dioxide, sulphur dioxide (burning coal), nitrogen oxides (vehicles), CFCs, particulates (PM2.5, PM10, soot) and ground-level ozone.","污染物：CO、CO₂、SO₂、氮氧化物、CFC、悬浮微粒、地面臭氧"],["Haze: caused by open burning (peat, forest, agricultural waste) and industrial emissions; harms respiratory health and reduces visibility.","烟霾：露天焚烧与工业排放；伤害呼吸、降低能见度"],["Acid rain: sulphur dioxide and nitrogen oxides dissolve in rainwater to form sulphuric and nitric acids; pH below 5.6.","酸雨：SO₂、氮氧化物溶于雨水形成硫酸硝酸；pH＜5.6"],["Effects of acid rain: kills fish and aquatic life, damages forests, leaches nutrients from the soil, corrodes buildings and statues.","影响：杀死水生生物、损害森林、土壤养分流失、腐蚀建筑"]],"","Tip: acid rain pH is lower than 5.6 — normal rain is slightly acidic."],["Global Warming and Climate Change","全球变暖与气候变化",[["Greenhouse effect: gases (CO₂, CH₄, N₂O, CFCs, water vapour) trap heat in the atmosphere; a natural process that keeps Earth warm.","温室效应：气体吸收并保留热量，自然过程"],["Enhanced greenhouse effect: burning fossil fuels, deforestation, livestock and rice fields increase greenhouse gases → global warming.","增强的温室效应：化石燃料、砍伐、畜牧、稻田使温室气体增加"],["Effects: melting polar ice and rising sea level; extreme weather (floods, droughts, storms); coral bleaching; loss of habitats and species; changes in crop yield; spread of tropical diseases.","影响：冰融海平面上升；极端天气；珊瑚白化；生物栖息地丧失；作物改变；疾病扩散"],["Solutions: reduce fossil fuel use, renewable energy, plant trees, energy efficiency, reduce methane from waste and farming, international agreements.","对策：减少化石燃料、再生能源、植树、节能、减排、国际协定"]],"","Tip: do not mix greenhouse effect (natural) with enhanced greenhouse effect/global warming."],["Ozone Depletion","臭氧层破坏",[["The ozone layer in the stratosphere absorbs most harmful ultraviolet (UV-B) radiation.","平流层臭氧层吸收有害紫外线"],["Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs, from refrigerators, air conditioners, aerosols) release chlorine atoms under UV; one chlorine atom destroys many ozone molecules.","CFC在紫外线下释放氯原子，破坏大量臭氧"],["Effects of more UV: skin cancer, cataracts, weakened immunity, damage to phytoplankton and crops.","影响：皮肤癌、白内障、免疫力下降、浮游植物与作物受损"],["Solution: Montreal Protocol (1987) phases out CFCs; use CFC-free refrigerants and aerosols.","对策：蒙特利尔议定书逐步淘汰CFC"]],"","Tip: CFC → chlorine → breaks ozone → more UV → skin cancer."],["Water Pollution and Eutrophication","水污染与富营养化",[["Sources: untreated sewage, industrial effluents (heavy metals), agricultural run-off (fertilisers, pesticides), oil spills, detergents, rubbish.","来源：污水、工业废水、农业径流、漏油、洗涤剂、垃圾"],["Eutrophication: excess nitrates and phosphates → algal bloom → light blocked, submerged plants die → bacteria decompose dead matter and use up oxygen (high BOD) → fish and aquatic animals die.","富营养化：营养过多→藻华→遮光→植物死亡→细菌分解耗氧(BOD高)→鱼死亡"],["BOD (biochemical oxygen demand): the amount of oxygen needed by microorganisms to decompose organic matter; high BOD = polluted water.","BOD：微生物分解有机物所需氧量；越高越污染"],["Indicators of clean water: high dissolved oxygen, low BOD, neutral pH, mayfly nymphs; polluted: bloodworms, rat-tailed maggots.","清洁水指标：溶氧高、BOD低；污染：红虫、鼠尾蛆"]],"","Tip: draw the eutrophication sequence as numbered steps."],["Soil Pollution, Waste and Deforestation","土壤污染、废物与森林砍伐",[["Soil pollution: pesticides, heavy metals, plastics, landfill leachate and e-waste contaminate the soil and may enter food chains.","土壤污染：农药、重金属、塑料、垃圾渗滤液、电子废物"],["Plastic waste is non-biodegradable; it harms marine life and takes hundreds of years to break down.","塑料不可降解，伤害海洋生物"],["Deforestation (logging, agriculture, plantations, urbanisation): causes soil erosion, floods, loss of habitat and biodiversity, less CO₂ absorbed and a change in local climate.","砍伐：水土流失、洪水、栖息地与多样性丧失、少吸收CO₂"],["Solutions: reduce, reuse, recycle (3R); proper landfill and incineration; biodegradable materials; reforestation.","对策：3R、妥善处理、可降解材料、重新造林"]],"","Tip: link deforestation to both biodiversity loss and global warming."],["Conservation and Green Technology","保育与绿色科技",[["Renewable energy: solar, hydroelectric, wind, biogas and biofuel reduce the use of fossil fuels.","再生能源：太阳能、水力、风能、沼气、生物燃料"],["3R: Reduce, Reuse, Recycle; also Refuse and Repair. Energy saving: efficient appliances, LED lamps, public transport.","3R：减少、重复使用、回收；节能"],["Sustainable forest management: selective logging, reforestation, afforestation and forest reserves.","可持续森林管理：选择性伐木、重新造林、植树"],["Waste treatment: wastewater treatment plants, composting, biological treatment; sustainable farming and organic fertilisers; green technology for products with low carbon footprints.","废物处理：污水处理、堆肥；永续农业；绿色科技"]],"","Tip: give one action, the problem it solves and its benefit."],["Laws and International Agreements","法律与国际协定",[["Malaysia: Environmental Quality Act 1974, Wildlife Conservation Act 2010, National Policy on Biological Diversity, National Green Technology Policy.","马来西亚：环境质量法令、野生动物保护法令等"],["International: Montreal Protocol (1987, ozone), Kyoto Protocol (1997, reduce greenhouse gases), Paris Agreement (2015, limit global temperature rise), Convention on Biological Diversity (1992).","国际：蒙特利尔(1987)、京都(1997)、巴黎协定(2015)、生物多样性公约(1992)"],["Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) is required for major development projects.","大型发展需做环境影响评估(EIA)"],["Law enforcement, penalties and public education are needed together.","执法、罚款与教育并行"]],"","Tip: give the year and the purpose of each agreement."],["Roles of Individuals and Communities","个人与社区的角色",[["Individuals: practise 3R, save water and electricity, use public transport or cycle, plant trees, avoid open burning, choose eco-friendly products, do not litter.","个人：3R、节水节电、用公共交通、植树、不露天焚烧、环保产品、不乱丢垃圾"],["Communities: gotong-royong, river clean-up, recycling centres, community gardens, awareness campaigns, school eco-clubs and green labels.","社区：集体清洁、河流清理、回收中心、社区花园、宣传活动"],["NGOs (WWF Malaysia, Malaysian Nature Society) and the government cooperate with the public.","非政府组织与政府合作"],["Sustainable development balances the environment, the economy and society.","可持续发展：环境、经济与社会平衡"]],"","Tip: 'think globally, act locally' — give practical local actions."],["Sustainable Development and Case Study","可持续发展与案例",[["Sustainable development: development that meets present needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet theirs.","可持续发展：满足当代而不损害后代"],["Example: managed mangrove forest (Matang) provides timber and fish while protecting the coast.","例：话望生红树林兼顾木材、渔业与海岸保护"],["Ecological footprint: the area of land and water needed to support a person's consumption and absorb waste.","生态足迹：支持个人消耗与吸收废物所需的土地与水域"],["Evaluate a project by environmental, economic and social effects, and consider alternatives.","从环境、经济、社会评估，并考虑替代方案"]],"","Tip: in 'opinion' questions state your stand and give two reasons."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Pollution (Pencemaran); Global warming (Pemanasan global); Greenhouse effect (Kesan rumah hijau)","污染；全球变暖；温室效应"],["Eutrophication (Eutrofikasi); Acid rain (Hujan asid); Ozone depletion (Penipisan ozon)","富营养化；酸雨；臭氧层破坏"],["Sustainable development (Pembangunan lestari); Renewable energy (Tenaga boleh baharu); Recycle (Kitar semula)","可持续发展；再生能源；回收"],["Deforestation (Penebangan hutan); Biodegradable (Terbiodegradasi)","砍伐森林；可生物降解"]],"","Tip: 'lestari' = sustainable."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Confusing the ozone layer problem (UV, CFCs) with global warming (greenhouse gases).","混淆臭氧层与全球变暖"],["Saying acid rain is caused by CO₂ — mainly SO₂ and NOₓ.","酸雨主要由SO₂与NOₓ引起"],["Describing eutrophication without mentioning decomposers using oxygen.","富营养化漏写分解者耗氧"],["Giving vague solutions such as 'protect the environment' — give specific actions.","解决办法太笼统"]],"","Tip: use cause–effect chains with arrows."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Name two greenhouse gases. J: Carbon dioxide and methane.","问：两种温室气体？答：二氧化碳、甲烷"],["S: What causes eutrophication? J: Excess fertilisers (nitrates and phosphates) entering water.","问：富营养化原因？答：过量肥料(硝酸盐、磷酸盐)进入水体"],["S: What does a high BOD value indicate? J: Water heavily polluted by organic matter with low dissolved oxygen.","问：高BOD表示？答：有机污染严重、溶氧低"],["S: Which gas destroys the ozone layer? J: CFC (chlorine from CFCs).","问：哪种气体破坏臭氧层？答：CFC"],["S: State two actions individuals can take to reduce pollution. J: Practise 3R; use public transport; avoid open burning.","问：个人减污染两做法？答：3R、公共交通、不露天焚烧"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-11":[["Basic Terms in Genetics","遗传学基本术语",[["Gene: a segment of DNA that codes for a protein/trait. Allele: an alternative form of a gene (e.g. T for tall, t for short). Locus: position of a gene on a chromosome.","基因；等位基因；基因座"],["Genotype: the combination of alleles (TT, Tt, tt). Phenotype: the observable trait (tall or short).","基因型；表型"],["Dominant allele: expressed in heterozygous condition (capital letter). Recessive allele: expressed only when homozygous (small letter).","显性；隐性"],["Homozygous: two identical alleles (TT or tt). Heterozygous: two different alleles (Tt). P generation: parents; F₁: first generation offspring; F₂: second.","纯合；杂合；亲代、子一代、子二代"]],"","Tip: write the genotype with letters and the phenotype in words."],["Mendel's Experiments","孟德尔的实验",[["Gregor Mendel used garden pea plants (Pisum sativum): easy to grow, short life cycle, many seeds, clear contrasting traits (tall/short, round/wrinkled seeds, yellow/green).","孟德尔用豌豆：易种、周期短、种子多、性状分明"],["He cross-pollinated pure-breeding plants: Tall × Short → all F₁ tall; F₁ self-pollinated → F₂ tall : short in a 3 : 1 ratio.","纯种高×矮→F₁全高；F₁自交→F₂高:矮＝3:1"],["Conclusions: traits are controlled by factors (now called genes) that exist in pairs; one dominates the other.","结论：性状由成对因子控制；一个显性"],["He counted large numbers of offspring and applied mathematics to the results.","统计大量后代并用数学分析"]],"","Tip: remember the reasons peas are suitable for Mendel's experiments."],["Monohybrid Cross and the Law of Segregation","单因子杂交与分离定律",[["Law of segregation: the two alleles of a gene separate during gamete formation so each gamete carries only one allele.","分离定律：配子形成时一对等位基因分离"],["Cross: Tt × Tt → gametes T, t and T, t → offspring TT : Tt : Tt : tt. Genotype ratio 1 TT : 2 Tt : 1 tt; phenotype ratio 3 tall : 1 short.","Tt×Tt→TT:Tt:tt＝1:2:1；表型3:1"],["Probability: a Tt × Tt cross gives 25% chance of a short (tt) offspring and 75% tall.","概率：tt 25%，高75%"],["Test cross: cross an individual of unknown genotype (dominant phenotype) with a homozygous recessive (tt). If any offspring are recessive, the unknown is heterozygous (1 : 1); if all dominant, it is homozygous.","测交：与纯隐性杂交；有隐性后代＝杂合(1:1)；全显性＝纯合"]],"","Tip: write parental genotypes, gametes, Punnett square, offspring genotypes, phenotypes and ratio."],["Worked Example: Monohybrid Cross","例题：单因子杂交",[["Q: In peas, round (R) is dominant over wrinkled (r). A heterozygous round plant is crossed with a wrinkled plant. A: Rr × rr → gametes R, r and r → offspring Rr, Rr, rr, rr = 1 round : 1 wrinkled (50%:50%).","题：Rr×rr→Rr:rr＝1:1"],["Q: Two black guinea pigs (Bb) produce a white offspring. Explain. A: Both parents are heterozygous carriers of the recessive allele (b); 25% chance of bb (white).","题：两黑豚鼠生出白色：双亲都是杂合子"],["Q: A tall plant is crossed with a short plant; all offspring are tall. Genotype of the tall parent? A: TT (homozygous dominant).","题：高×矮→全高：高亲为TT"],["Answer pattern: key → parents → gametes → Punnett square → results.","答题：图例→亲代→配子→棋盘→结果"]],"","Tip: define the allele symbols at the start (e.g. T = tall, t = short)."],["Dihybrid Cross and Independent Assortment","双因子杂交与自由组合",[["Law of independent assortment: alleles of different genes are inherited independently of each other because homologous pairs line up at random in meiosis I.","自由组合定律：不同基因的等位基因独立遗传"],["Mendel crossed round yellow (RRYY) with wrinkled green (rryy): F₁ all RrYy (round yellow).","圆黄×皱绿→F₁全为RrYy"],["F₁ self-cross RrYy × RrYy → gametes RY, Ry, rY, ry; 16 combinations → F₂ phenotype ratio 9 round yellow : 3 round green : 3 wrinkled yellow : 1 wrinkled green.","F₂表型比 9:3:3:1"],["This ratio applies when the two genes are on different chromosomes.","基因位于不同染色体时成立"]],"","Tip: a dihybrid Punnett square has 16 boxes; list the four gametes first."],["Incomplete Dominance and Codominance","不完全显性与共显性",[["Incomplete dominance: neither allele is completely dominant; heterozygote has an intermediate phenotype (red × white snapdragon → pink; F₂ 1 red : 2 pink : 1 white).","不完全显性：杂合子表现中间型（红×白→粉）"],["Codominance: both alleles are fully expressed in the heterozygote (e.g. AB blood group; roan cattle).","共显性：两等位基因都表达（AB血型）"],["Multiple alleles: a gene with more than two alleles in the population (ABO blood groups: Iᴬ, Iᴮ, i).","复等位基因：ABO血型"],["These are extensions beyond simple dominant–recessive inheritance.","超越简单显隐性的遗传"]],"","Tip: in incomplete dominance the phenotype ratio equals the genotype ratio (1:2:1)."],["Sex Determination","性别决定",[["Humans have 23 pairs of chromosomes: 22 pairs of autosomes and 1 pair of sex chromosomes (XX female, XY male).","人有23对染色体：22对常染色体+1对性染色体"],["Eggs always carry X; sperm carry either X or Y; the sex of the child is decided by the sperm.","卵子都含X；精子含X或Y；性别由精子决定"],["XX × XY → 50% XX (girl) and 50% XY (boy): probability of each sex is 1/2 at every pregnancy.","每次怀孕男女概率各1/2"],["The Y chromosome carries SRY gene that triggers male development.","Y染色体上的SRY基因诱导男性发育"]],"","Tip: draw the genetic diagram showing gametes X, Y and X, X."],["Sex-Linked Inheritance","性连锁遗传",[["Sex-linked genes are carried on the sex chromosomes (usually the X chromosome). X-linked recessive disorders: colour blindness, haemophilia.","性连锁基因位于X染色体：色盲、血友病"],["Males (XY) have only one X so a single recessive allele is expressed; females (XX) need two recessive alleles; heterozygous females are carriers.","男性只有一个X，隐性即表现；女性杂合为携带者"],["Carrier mother (XᴴXʰ) × normal father (XᴴY): daughters 50% normal and 50% carriers; sons 50% normal and 50% affected.","携带者母×正常父：女儿1/2携带；儿子1/2患病"],["Colour blindness: cannot distinguish red and green; haemophilia: blood clots slowly. Affected men pass the allele to all daughters (carriers), not to sons.","色盲、血友病：患病父亲把基因传给女儿，不传儿子"]],"","Tip: use symbols such as XᴴXʰ to show the allele on the X chromosome."],["Inheritance of Blood Groups","血型遗传",[["ABO blood group is controlled by three alleles: Iᴬ and Iᴮ (codominant) and i (recessive).","ABO血型由3个等位基因控制"],["Group A: IᴬIᴬ or Iᴬi; group B: IᴮIᴮ or Iᴮi; group AB: IᴬIᴮ; group O: ii.","A型、B型、AB型、O型基因型"],["Example: Iᴬi × Iᴮi → AB, A, B and O in a 1 : 1 : 1 : 1 ratio. AB × O → A or B only.","例：Iᴬi×Iᴮi→AB:A:B:O＝1:1:1:1"],["Rhesus factor: Rh⁺ (dominant, D) and Rh⁻ (recessive, d). Blood groups are used in paternity disputes (can exclude, not prove).","Rh：Rh⁺显性；血型可排除不能证明亲子"]],"","Tip: remember group O is ii (recessive), so two group A or B parents can have a group O child."],["Pedigree Analysis","系谱分析",[["Pedigree symbols: square = male; circle = female; shaded = affected; horizontal line = marriage; vertical line = offspring.","系谱符号：方形男，圆形女，涂黑患者"],["If two unaffected parents have an affected child, the trait is recessive and both parents are carriers.","双亲正常有患病子女→隐性，双亲为携带者"],["If affected parents have only affected children, or the trait appears in every generation, it may be dominant.","每代出现→可能是显性"],["If affected individuals are mostly male and pass it through carrier mothers, it is likely X-linked recessive.","男性多、经携带母亲传递→X连锁隐性"]],"","Tip: first decide dominant or recessive from a family with two normal parents and an affected child."],["Genetic Diseases in Humans","人类遗传病",[["Thalassaemia (autosomal recessive): defective haemoglobin → anaemia; carriers (thalassaemia trait) can be detected by screening. Sickle cell anaemia (recessive): abnormal haemoglobin makes red cells sickle-shaped; carriers resist malaria.","地中海贫血（隐性）；镰刀型细胞贫血（隐性）；携带者抗疟疾"],["Albinism (recessive): lack of melanin. Haemophilia and colour blindness: X-linked recessive. Huntington's disease: autosomal dominant.","白化病（隐性）；血友病、色盲（X连锁隐性）；亨廷顿舞蹈症（显性）"],["Chromosomal disorders: Down syndrome (trisomy 21; 47 chromosomes), Turner syndrome (XO), Klinefelter syndrome (XXY).","染色体病：唐氏综合征、特纳综合征、克氏综合征"],["Genetic counselling and screening help families assess risks; prenatal tests (amniocentesis) detect some disorders.","遗传咨询与产前检查(羊水穿刺)"]],"","Tip: gene mutation disorders vs chromosomal disorders — know the difference."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Gene (Gen); Allele (Alel); Genotype (Genotip); Phenotype (Fenotip)","基因；等位基因；基因型；表型"],["Dominant (Dominan); Recessive (Resesif); Homozygous (Homozigot); Heterozygous (Heterozigot)","显性；隐性；纯合；杂合"],["Monohybrid cross (Kacukan monohibrid); Dihybrid cross (Kacukan dihibrid); Test cross (Kacukan uji)","单因子杂交；双因子杂交；测交"],["Sex-linked (Pertalian seks); Carrier (Pembawa); Pedigree (Salasilah)","性连锁；携带者；系谱"]],"","Tip: 'fenotip' = phenotype."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Writing capital and small letters carelessly — use clear, consistent symbols and a key.","字母大小写混乱"],["Forgetting to write gametes in circles or listing them as full genotypes.","配子写法不规范"],["Confusing genotype ratio (1:2:1) with phenotype ratio (3:1).","混淆基因型比与表型比"],["In sex-linked crosses, forgetting to write the allele on the X chromosome.","性连锁题忘记把基因写在X上"],["Saying 'males are carriers' of X-linked recessive disorders — males are affected or normal.","男性不是携带者"]],"","Tip: practise Punnett squares until the layout is automatic."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Heterozygous tall (Tt) × heterozygous tall (Tt). What fraction are short? J: 1/4 (25%).","问：Tt×Tt，矮的比例？答：1/4"],["S: Give the dihybrid phenotype ratio of F₂. J: 9 : 3 : 3 : 1.","问：双因子F₂表型比？答：9:3:3:1"],["S: A man with colour blindness marries a normal woman (not a carrier). What are the genotypes of their children? J: Daughters are carriers (XᴴXʰ); sons are normal (XᴴY).","问：色盲男性×非携带正常女性，子女？答：女儿携带者，儿子正常"],["S: Parents with blood groups A and B have a child with group O. Their genotypes? J: Iᴬi and Iᴮi.","问：A型与B型父母生O型孩子，基因型？答：Iᴬi和Iᴮi"],["S: Which parent determines the sex of a child? J: The father (sperm carry X or Y).","问：谁决定孩子性别？答：父亲"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-12":[["Variation: Meaning and Types","变异：含义与类型",[["Variation: differences between individuals of the same species. It can be caused by genes (inherited) and the environment.","变异：同种个体间差异，由基因与环境造成"],["Two types: continuous variation and discontinuous variation.","两类：连续变异与不连续变异"],["Variation is important for the survival of a species when the environment changes.","变异有利物种适应环境变化"]],"","Tip: give examples when classifying variation."],["Continuous Variation","连续变异",[["Characteristic shows a range of values with intermediate forms (height, body mass, skin colour, hand span, leaf size).","性状有一系列中间值：身高、体重、肤色、叶大小"],["Controlled by many genes (polygenic) and strongly influenced by the environment (diet, sunlight, exercise).","由多基因控制，受环境影响大"],["Data are presented as a histogram or a line graph; frequency distribution is bell-shaped (normal distribution) — most individuals are near the mean.","用直方图/折线图；呈钟形正态分布"],["Example: a graph of heights of Form 5 students shows a normal curve.","例：学生身高分布呈正态曲线"]],"","Tip: continuous variation → bell-shaped curve."],["Discontinuous Variation","不连续变异",[["Characteristic falls into distinct categories with no intermediates (ABO blood group, tongue rolling, attached/free earlobes, sex, presence of dimples, fingerprint types).","性状分明无中间型：血型、卷舌、耳垂、性别、酒窝"],["Controlled by one or a few genes; little or no effect of the environment.","由一个或少数基因控制，受环境影响少"],["Data are presented as a bar chart.","用柱状图表示"],["Example: blood group A, B, AB or O — you cannot be 'between' A and B.","例：血型只能是A、B、AB、O"]],"","Tip: discontinuous variation → clear groups, bar chart."],["Continuous vs Discontinuous Variation","连续与不连续变异比较",[["Range: continuous — a range of values; discontinuous — distinct categories.","范围：连续有一系列值；不连续有明确类别"],["Genes: continuous — many genes (polygenic); discontinuous — one or few genes.","基因：多基因/单或少基因"],["Environment: continuous — strongly influenced; discontinuous — little influence.","环境：影响大/影响小"],["Graph: continuous — histogram/normal curve; discontinuous — bar chart. Examples: height, mass / blood group, tongue rolling.","图：直方图正态曲线/柱状图；例：身高体重/血型卷舌"]],"","Tip: set out a comparison table with these four headings."],["Genetic Sources of Variation","变异的遗传来源",[["Meiosis: crossing over and independent assortment of homologous chromosomes produce new combinations of alleles in gametes.","减数分裂：交叉互换与自由组合产生新基因组合"],["Random fertilisation: any sperm can fuse with any egg, giving a very large number of possible genotypes.","随机受精：任一精子可与任一卵子结合"],["Mutation: a sudden change in the DNA sequence or chromosome structure/number; the only source of new alleles.","突变：DNA序列或染色体结构/数目的突然变化；新等位基因的唯一来源"],["Sexual reproduction produces more variation than asexual reproduction.","有性生殖比无性生殖产生更多变异"]],"","Tip: only mutation creates NEW alleles; meiosis shuffles existing ones."],["Environmental Factors and Twin Studies","环境因素与双胞胎研究",[["Diet and nutrition affect height and body mass; sunlight changes skin colour (tanning) and plant growth; exercise affects muscle size; temperature influences animal coat thickness.","饮食、阳光、运动、温度影响性状"],["Environment acts only on the phenotype; acquired characteristics (e.g. big muscles from exercise) are not inherited.","环境只影响表型；获得性状不遗传"],["Identical twins have the same genotype; differences between them are caused by the environment. Studying twins raised apart shows the effects of genes and environment.","同卵双胞胎基因相同，差异来自环境"],["Hydrangea flower colour depends on soil pH; Himalayan rabbit fur colour depends on temperature.","绣球花颜色受土壤pH影响"]],"","Tip: say 'acquired characteristics cannot be inherited'."],["Mutation: Types and Causes","突变：类型与成因",[["Gene (point) mutation: a change in one or a few nucleotides — substitution, insertion or deletion; insertion/deletion can cause a frameshift. Example: sickle cell anaemia (one base substitution).","基因突变：碱基替换、插入、缺失；例镰刀型贫血"],["Chromosome mutation: change in the structure or number of chromosomes — non-disjunction (Down syndrome), deletion, duplication, translocation; polyploidy in plants.","染色体突变：不分离、缺失、重复、易位；多倍体"],["Mutagens: ionising radiation (X-rays, gamma rays), ultraviolet light, chemicals (tar in tobacco smoke, mustard gas, benzopyrene), some viruses.","诱变剂：电离辐射、紫外线、化学物质、某些病毒"],["Effects: most mutations are harmful or neutral; a few are beneficial. Only mutations in gametes (germline) can be inherited.","影响：多数有害或中性；生殖细胞突变才可遗传"]],"","Tip: mutations in body cells (somatic) are not passed to offspring."],["Natural Selection","自然选择",[["Darwin and Wallace: (1) individuals in a population show variation; (2) more offspring are produced than can survive; (3) competition for limited resources ('struggle for existence'); (4) individuals with advantageous characteristics survive and reproduce (survival of the fittest); (5) the advantageous alleles are passed on to the next generation; (6) over many generations the population changes — evolution.","达尔文与华莱士：变异→过度繁殖→竞争→适者生存→遗传→进化"],["Natural selection acts on phenotype; the environment is the selecting agent.","自然选择作用于表型；环境是选择因素"],["Adaptation and evolution lead to new species (speciation) when populations are isolated.","隔离导致新物种形成"]],"","Tip: use the sequence variation → competition → survival → inheritance → change."],["Examples of Natural Selection","自然选择的例子",[["Peppered moth (Biston betularia): before industry, light moths were camouflaged on lichen-covered bark; in polluted areas, soot-darkened bark favoured dark (melanic) moths because birds ate light moths more easily; the dark allele increased.","桦尺蛾：污染区深色型因保护色而存活，深色等位基因增加"],["Antibiotic-resistant bacteria: a resistant mutant survives the antibiotic and reproduces; resistance spreads (MRSA).","抗药细菌：抗药突变体存活并繁殖"],["Insecticide resistance in mosquitoes and pests; herbicide resistance in weeds.","昆虫抗药性；杂草抗除草剂"],["Sickle cell allele is common in malaria areas because heterozygous carriers resist malaria (selective advantage).","镰刀型细胞等位基因在疟疾区常见：杂合子抗疟"]],"","Tip: explain each example with 'variation (mutation) → selection pressure → survival → more of the allele'."],["Natural vs Artificial Selection","自然选择与人工选择",[["Natural selection: the environment selects individuals with advantageous characteristics; slow; no human involvement.","自然选择：环境选择，缓慢"],["Artificial selection (selective breeding): humans choose parents with desirable traits (high-yield rice, milk cows, dog breeds, disease-resistant crops); faster.","人工选择：人选择优良性状，较快"],["Disadvantages of selective breeding: reduced genetic diversity, inbreeding depression, higher risk from disease.","缺点：遗传多样性降低、近交衰退"],["Both rely on variation and inheritance.","两者都依赖变异与遗传"]],"","Tip: compare using 'selecting agent', 'speed', 'purpose'."],["Importance of Variation","变异的重要性",[["Variation allows some individuals to survive when the environment changes (disease, climate, new predators).","变异使部分个体能在环境变化时存活"],["Provides the raw material for natural selection and evolution; maintains biodiversity.","为自然选择与进化提供原料；维持生物多样性"],["Populations with very low variation (e.g. cheetahs, inbred crops) are vulnerable to extinction.","变异少的群体（如猎豹）易灭绝"],["Variation is useful in breeding programmes and medicine (e.g. identifying disease-resistant varieties).","变异用于育种与医学"]],"","Tip: link importance of variation to survival of the species."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Variation (Variasi); Continuous variation (Variasi selanjar); Discontinuous variation (Variasi tak selanjar)","变异；连续变异；不连续变异"],["Mutation (Mutasi); Mutagen (Mutagen); Natural selection (Pemilihan semula jadi)","突变；诱变剂；自然选择"],["Adaptation (Penyesuaian); Evolution (Evolusi); Selective breeding (Pembiakan terpilih)","适应；进化；选择性育种"]],"","Tip: 'pemilihan semula jadi' = natural selection."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying individuals 'change' to adapt — selection acts on existing variation; individuals do not change.","个体不会为适应而改变"],["Writing 'acquired characteristics are inherited'.","获得性状不遗传"],["Mixing up continuous and discontinuous variation or using the wrong graph.","混淆两类变异或图表"],["Writing that mutations are always harmful.","突变并非都有害"],["Forgetting that mutations are random and not caused by need.","突变随机，不因需要而发生"]],"","Tip: use 'survive, reproduce, pass on the allele'."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Give two examples of discontinuous variation. J: ABO blood group; tongue rolling.","问：两个不连续变异例子？答：血型；卷舌"],["S: Why does continuous variation form a bell-shaped curve? J: Many genes and environmental factors act together, so most individuals have intermediate values.","问：为何呈钟形？答：多基因与环境作用，多数为中间值"],["S: State the source of new alleles. J: Mutation.","问：新等位基因来源？答：突变"],["S: Explain how bacteria become resistant to antibiotics. J: A resistant mutant survives the antibiotic, reproduces and passes on the resistance allele.","问：细菌如何抗药？答：抗药突变体存活繁殖并传递"],["S: Differentiate natural and artificial selection. J: Natural: the environment selects; artificial: humans select desired traits.","问：自然与人工选择？答：环境选择；人为选择"]],"",""]],"bio|T5-13":[["Genetic Technology: Overview","基因科技概览",[["Genetic engineering (recombinant DNA technology): transferring a gene from one organism into another to produce a desired trait or product.","基因工程：把基因转入另一生物以获得性状或产物"],["The organism that receives the foreign gene is a transgenic organism or genetically modified organism (GMO).","转基因生物(GMO)"],["Genetic technology includes DNA profiling, gene cloning, PCR, gene therapy and organism cloning.","包括DNA指纹、基因克隆、PCR、基因疗法、克隆"],["The genetic code is universal, so a human gene can be expressed in bacteria.","遗传密码通用，人类基因可在细菌表达"]],"","Tip: the universal genetic code is the reason genes can be transferred between species."],["Tools of Genetic Engineering","基因工程工具",[["Restriction enzymes cut DNA at specific recognition sequences (e.g. EcoRI cuts GAATTC), leaving short single-stranded 'sticky ends'.","限制酶在特定序列切割DNA，留下黏性末端"],["DNA ligase joins DNA fragments with complementary sticky ends together (forming sugar–phosphate bonds).","DNA连接酶连接互补黏性末端"],["Vector: carries the gene into the host cell — usually a bacterial plasmid or a virus.","载体：质粒或病毒"],["Host cell: bacterium (E. coli), yeast, plant or animal cell. Marker genes (e.g. antibiotic resistance) identify successfully transformed cells.","宿主细胞；标记基因用于筛选"]],"","Tip: same restriction enzyme for plasmid and gene so that the sticky ends match."],["Producing Human Insulin by Bacteria","细菌生产人胰岛素",[["1. Isolate the human insulin gene from human DNA using a restriction enzyme.","1. 用限制酶取出胰岛素基因"],["2. Cut a bacterial plasmid with the same restriction enzyme.","2. 用同一限制酶切质粒"],["3. Join the insulin gene into the plasmid with DNA ligase → recombinant plasmid.","3. 连接酶连接→重组质粒"],["4. Introduce the recombinant plasmid into bacteria (transformation); select transformed bacteria using an antibiotic marker.","4. 导入细菌并筛选"],["5. Culture the bacteria in a fermenter; they express the gene and produce insulin, which is extracted and purified.","5. 发酵培养表达并提纯胰岛素"]],"","Tip: benefits: large amounts, cheaper, pure, fewer allergic reactions than animal insulin."],["PCR and Gel Electrophoresis","PCR与凝胶电泳",[["PCR (polymerase chain reaction) amplifies a small sample of DNA: denaturation (about 95 °C, strands separate) → annealing (about 55 °C, primers bind) → extension (about 72 °C, Taq polymerase builds new strands). Each cycle doubles the DNA (2ⁿ copies after n cycles).","PCR：变性→退火→延伸；每循环翻倍"],["Gel electrophoresis: DNA fragments (negatively charged) move through a gel towards the positive electrode; smaller fragments travel farther, forming bands.","凝胶电泳：DNA带负电，向正极移动；小片段走得更远"],["Combined, they allow DNA profiling from tiny samples of blood, hair or saliva.","结合可用微量样本做DNA分析"]],"","Tip: remember the three temperatures of PCR and the role of Taq polymerase."],["DNA Profiling and Its Applications","DNA指纹及应用",[["DNA profiling (genetic fingerprinting): compares repeated DNA sequences (STRs) that vary between individuals; each person except identical twins has a unique pattern.","DNA指纹：比较个体差异的重复序列"],["Forensic science: match DNA from a crime scene with a suspect's bands. Paternity testing: half of a child's bands match the mother and half match the father.","法医：比对犯罪现场DNA；亲子鉴定：一半来自母，一半来自父"],["Identifying victims of disasters, diagnosing genetic diseases, studying evolution and conservation (illegal wildlife trade).","灾难身份识别、遗传病诊断、保护生物学"],["Interpreting a profile: bands at the same level = same DNA fragments.","同一水平的条带＝相同片段"]],"","Tip: describe how the results are compared (matching bands)."],["Genetically Modified Crops and Animals","转基因作物与动物",[["Bt crops (corn, cotton): contain a gene from Bacillus thuringiensis that makes a toxin killing certain insect pests → less pesticide.","Bt作物：含苏云金杆菌毒素基因，抗虫"],["Golden Rice: contains genes to make β-carotene (vitamin A precursor) to prevent vitamin A deficiency. Herbicide-resistant soya; virus-resistant papaya; longer shelf-life tomatoes.","黄金大米；抗除草剂大豆；抗病毒木瓜"],["Transgenic animals: fast-growing fish, goats producing medicines in their milk, GM mosquitoes to reduce dengue.","转基因动物：快长鱼、产药羊奶、转基因蚊子"],["Aims: higher yield, resistance to pests and diseases, improved nutrition, longer storage.","目的：高产、抗病虫、营养、耐储"]],"","Tip: give a gene, its source and its benefit for each GM example."],["Gene Therapy","基因疗法",[["Gene therapy: replacing or adding a functional gene into the cells of a patient to treat a genetic disorder.","基因疗法：把正常基因导入患者细胞"],["A healthy gene is placed into a virus vector (modified to be harmless) which infects the patient's cells and delivers the gene. Examples: severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID), some blood and eye disorders; research on thalassaemia.","病毒载体导入基因；SCID等"],["Somatic gene therapy affects only body cells and is not inherited; germline therapy would be inherited (banned or restricted in many countries).","体细胞疗法不遗传；生殖细胞疗法受限"],["Challenges: risk of immune reaction, vector causing cancer, high cost, ethical concerns.","挑战：免疫反应、致癌风险、成本、伦理"]],"","Tip: do not confuse gene therapy with drug treatment — it repairs the gene."],["Cloning","克隆",[["Plant cloning by tissue culture (micropropagation): cells from a plant are grown on nutrient agar with hormones → identical plantlets (orchids, banana, oil palm).","植物组织培养：快速繁殖相同幼苗"],["Animal cloning (Dolly the sheep, 1996): nucleus taken from an udder (body) cell of a donor sheep → inserted into an egg whose nucleus was removed → electric shock fuses and activates → embryo implanted in a surrogate mother.","动物克隆（多利羊）：体细胞核移植"],["The clone is genetically identical to the donor. Therapeutic cloning produces stem cells; reproductive cloning produces an organism.","克隆体与供体基因相同；治疗性与生殖性克隆"],["Advantages: preserve endangered species, produce animals with useful traits. Disadvantages: low success rate, health problems, ethical concerns, reduced genetic variation.","优缺点：保护濒危物种；成功率低、伦理、变异减少"]],"","Tip: somatic cell nuclear transfer — nucleus from a body cell + enucleated egg."],["Applications in Medicine, Agriculture and Industry","在医药、农业与工业的应用",[["Medicine: insulin, growth hormone, interferon, vaccines (hepatitis B vaccine), diagnostic tests, gene therapy.","医药：胰岛素、生长激素、疫苗、诊断"],["Agriculture: GM crops, tissue culture, disease-resistant and drought-resistant varieties.","农业：转基因作物、组织培养"],["Industry and environment: enzymes for detergents and food, bacteria that clean up oil spills (bioremediation), biofuels.","工业环境：酶制剂、清洁溢油细菌、生物燃料"],["Forensics and conservation: DNA profiling, gene banks.","法医与保育：DNA指纹、基因库"]],"","Tip: give one application for each sector."],["Ethical, Social and Safety Issues","伦理、社会与安全问题",[["Safety of GM food: possible allergies and long-term effects; gene flow to wild relatives ('superweeds'); effects on non-target organisms and biodiversity.","GM食品安全：过敏；基因漂流；非目标生物"],["Economic and social issues: patents and control by large companies, cost to poor farmers, labelling of GM food.","经济社会：专利垄断、成本、标示"],["Ethical concerns: animal welfare, human cloning, 'designer babies', genetic discrimination, privacy of genetic information, religious and cultural beliefs.","伦理：动物福利、克隆人、定制婴儿、基因歧视、隐私、宗教文化"],["In Malaysia the Biosafety Act 2007 regulates living modified organisms (LMOs) through the National Biosafety Board.","马来西亚：2007年生物安全法令规管活体改性生物"]],"","Tip: for 'discuss' questions give advantages AND disadvantages, then a conclusion."],["Benefits and Risks: Summary","利弊总结",[["Benefits: higher yields, less pesticide use, new medicines, early diagnosis, solving crimes, saving endangered species.","益处：高产、少农药、新药、早期诊断、破案、保育"],["Risks: unknown long-term health effects, loss of biodiversity, ethical misuse, social inequality, ecological imbalance.","风险：长期健康未知、多样性丧失、伦理滥用、不平等、生态失衡"],["Balanced approach: strict regulation, risk assessment, labelling, public discussion and responsible research.","平衡做法：严格监管、风险评估、标示、公众讨论"]],"","Tip: express your own opinion with reasons, using evidence."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Genetic engineering (Kejuruteraan genetik); Recombinant DNA (DNA rekombinan); Plasmid (Plasmid)","基因工程；重组DNA；质粒"],["Restriction enzyme (Enzim penyekatan); DNA ligase (Ligase DNA); Vector (Vektor)","限制酶；连接酶；载体"],["DNA profiling (Pemprofilan DNA); Gene therapy (Terapi gen); Cloning (Pengklonan); GMO (Organisma ubah suai genetik)","DNA指纹；基因疗法；克隆；转基因生物"]],"","Tip: 'ubah suai genetik' = genetically modified."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Using different restriction enzymes for the gene and the plasmid (sticky ends would not match).","基因与质粒用不同限制酶"],["Confusing restriction enzyme (cuts) and DNA ligase (joins).","混淆限制酶与连接酶"],["Writing that a clone is 'identical in everything' — it is genetically identical but the environment can cause differences.","克隆体基因相同，表型可有差异"],["Listing only benefits in discussion questions.","讨论题只写好处"]],"","Tip: sequence the steps and name each enzyme/tool."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: What is the function of DNA ligase? J: Joins DNA fragments (e.g. the gene into the plasmid) by forming bonds between sticky ends.","问：DNA连接酶作用？答：连接DNA片段（如基因与质粒）"],["S: Why is the same restriction enzyme used to cut the plasmid and the gene? J: To produce complementary sticky ends that can join.","问：为何同一限制酶？答：产生互补黏性末端"],["S: State one use of PCR. J: Amplify a small DNA sample for DNA profiling.","问：PCR一个用途？答：扩增微量DNA用于鉴定"],["S: Give one benefit and one concern of GM crops. J: Benefit: higher yield/pest resistance; concern: gene flow to wild relatives or health effects.","问：转基因作物一利一弊？答：高产抗虫；基因漂流或健康担忧"],["S: How was Dolly the sheep produced? J: By transferring the nucleus of a body cell into an egg without a nucleus and implanting the embryo into a surrogate.","问：多利羊如何诞生？答：体细胞核移入去核卵，胚胎植入代孕母羊"]],"",""]]};
const PPTS_REPL={"bio|T4-10":[["10.1 Types of Circulatory Systems","10.1 循环系统的类型",[["Why a transport system is needed: large organisms have a small surface-area-to-volume ratio, so diffusion alone is too slow to supply cells with oxygen and nutrients and to remove wastes.","需要运输系统：大型生物表面积/体积比小，仅靠扩散太慢"],["Open circulatory system (insects, e.g. grasshopper): the heart pumps haemolymph into the body cavity (haemocoel) where it bathes the tissues directly; the blood is not confined to vessels; low pressure; flow is slow.","开放式：血淋巴由心脏泵入体腔直接浸润组织；不限于血管；压力低、流动慢"],["In insects the haemolymph does not carry oxygen — oxygen is delivered directly to the cells by the tracheal system.","昆虫血淋巴不运氧，由气管系统直接供氧"],["Closed circulatory system (earthworm, fish, mammals): blood flows only inside blood vessels; higher pressure; faster, more efficient and the flow can be directed to the organs that need it.","封闭式：血液只在血管内流动；压力高、速度快、可定向输送"]],"","Tip: say where the blood flows (inside vessels / into the haemocoel)."],["10.1 Single and Double Circulation","10.1 单循环与双循环",[["Single circulation (fish): heart with 2 chambers (1 atrium, 1 ventricle); the blood passes through the heart ONCE in one complete circuit: heart → gills → body → heart.","单循环(鱼)：心脏2室；每一圈血液只经心脏一次"],["After passing through the gill capillaries the blood pressure drops, so blood reaches the body tissues slowly with low pressure.","经鳃毛细血管后压力下降，供给身体较慢"],["Double circulation (mammals, birds): heart with 4 chambers; blood passes through the heart TWICE in one complete circuit — pulmonary circulation (heart → lungs → heart) and systemic circulation (heart → body → heart).","双循环：心脏4室；每圈经心脏两次：肺循环+体循环"],["Oxygenated and deoxygenated blood do not mix because of the septum; blood returns to the heart to be pumped again at high pressure after the lungs.","隔膜使含氧与缺氧血不混；肺后再回心脏加压"],["Advantage: faster and more efficient delivery of oxygen to tissues, which supports the high metabolic rate of warm-blooded animals.","优点：供氧快且有效，支持恒温动物高代谢率"]],"","Tip: the key idea is 'blood returns to the heart to regain pressure'."],["10.1 SPM Mark Points: Types of Circulatory Systems","10.1 SPM得分点：循环系统的类型",[["Q: Compare open and closed circulatory systems. [6 marks, any 6 points]","题：比较开放式与封闭式循环系统 [6分]"],["P1 Open: blood flows into the haemocoel / Closed: blood flows inside blood vessels. P2 Open: blood (haemolymph) bathes the tissues directly / Closed: exchange occurs across capillary walls.","P1 流向体腔 vs 在血管内；P2 直接浸润 vs 经毛细血管交换"],["P3 Open: low pressure / Closed: high pressure. P4 Open: slow flow / Closed: fast flow. P5 Open: example insects / Closed: example earthworm, fish, humans. P6 Open: cannot be directed to specific organs / Closed: can be directed.","P3 压力低/高；P4 速度慢/快；P5 例子；P6 能否定向输送"],["Q: Explain why double circulation is more efficient than single circulation. [3 marks]","题：解释双循环为何比单循环有效 [3分]"],["P1 Blood passes through the heart twice per circuit. P2 Blood is pumped again after the lungs so it flows at high pressure to the body. P3 Oxygenated and deoxygenated blood do not mix, so more oxygen is delivered to the tissues.","P1 每圈经心脏两次；P2 肺后再加压；P3 含氧缺氧不混合，供氧更多"]],"","Tip: one similarity/difference pair = 1 mark. Always mention both sides."],["10.2 The Human Heart: Structure","10.2 人类心脏的结构",[["The heart is a muscular organ (cardiac muscle) of 4 chambers: right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium and left ventricle. The septum separates the right (deoxygenated) side and the left (oxygenated) side.","心脏4室；隔膜分开左右两侧"],["Atria receive blood and have thin walls; ventricles pump blood out and have thick walls. The left ventricle has the thickest wall because it pumps blood at high pressure around the whole body.","心房收血壁薄；心室泵血壁厚；左心室最厚"],["Valves: tricuspid valve (between right atrium and ventricle) and bicuspid (mitral) valve (left) are atrioventricular valves; semilunar valves are at the bases of the pulmonary artery and aorta. They prevent backflow of blood.","瓣膜：三尖瓣、二尖瓣、半月瓣；防止血液倒流"],["Tendons (chordae tendineae) attach the AV valves to the ventricle wall to prevent the valves from turning inside out. Coronary arteries supply oxygen and nutrients to the cardiac muscle.","腱索防止瓣膜翻转；冠状动脉供应心肌"]],"","Tip: label the vena cava, pulmonary artery, pulmonary vein, aorta and the four chambers in a diagram."],["10.2 Pathway of Blood: Pulmonary and Systemic Circulation","10.2 血液路径：肺循环与体循环",[["Systemic circulation: left ventricle → aorta → arteries → arterioles → body capillaries (exchange of O₂, nutrients, CO₂, wastes) → venules → veins → vena cava → right atrium.","体循环：左心室→主动脉→…→毛细血管→…→腔静脉→右心房"],["Pulmonary circulation: right atrium → (tricuspid valve) → right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs (alveolar capillaries) → pulmonary veins → left atrium → (bicuspid valve) → left ventricle.","肺循环：右心房→右心室→肺动脉→肺→肺静脉→左心房→左心室"],["Pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood and pulmonary vein carries oxygenated blood — exceptions to 'arteries = oxygenated'.","肺动脉含缺氧血，肺静脉含氧血：例外"],["Other vessels: hepatic portal vein (intestine → liver), renal artery and renal vein (kidney), coronary arteries (heart).","其他血管：肝门静脉、肾动脉与静脉、冠状动脉"]],"","Tip: write the pathway as a numbered sequence including the valves."],["10.2 Blood Vessels: Structure and Adaptation","10.2 血管：结构与适应",[["Artery: thick, muscular and elastic wall; narrow lumen; no valves; carries blood away from the heart at high pressure; pulse can be felt. Elastic wall withstands high pressure and recoils to maintain blood flow.","动脉：壁厚有弹性、管腔窄、无瓣；高压；可感脉搏"],["Vein: thin wall with less muscle; wide lumen; valves present; carries blood to the heart at low pressure. Valves prevent backflow; skeletal muscle contraction helps push the blood.","静脉：壁薄、管腔宽、有瓣；低压；瓣膜防倒流"],["Capillary: wall one cell thick; very narrow lumen (one red blood cell at a time); extremely large total surface area; permeable. Allows rapid exchange of materials between blood and tissue fluid.","毛细血管：壁一层细胞；极窄；总面积大；利于物质交换"],["Arterioles regulate blood flow to tissues by constricting or dilating.","小动脉收缩/扩张调节血流"]],"","Tip: link each structural feature to a function (e.g. valves → prevent backflow)."],["10.2 Components of Blood and Their Functions","10.2 血液成分与功能",[["Plasma (about 55%): water, dissolved nutrients (glucose, amino acids), mineral ions, hormones, plasma proteins (albumin, fibrinogen, antibodies), urea and CO₂ (as hydrogen carbonate). Transports substances and heat.","血浆(约55%)：水、营养物、离子、激素、蛋白质、废物"],["Red blood cells: biconcave disc → large surface area-to-volume ratio for oxygen absorption; no nucleus → more space for haemoglobin; haemoglobin + O₂ → oxyhaemoglobin.","红细胞：双凹增面积；无核容纳更多血红蛋白；运氧"],["White blood cells: phagocytes engulf pathogens (phagocytosis); lymphocytes produce antibodies. Platelets: cell fragments that start blood clotting.","白细胞：吞噬细胞吞噬、淋巴细胞产抗体；血小板：启动凝血"],["Blood also helps regulate body temperature and pH, and defends the body.","血液也调节体温与pH并防御"]],"","Tip: name the structure, then its function (e.g. no nucleus → space for haemoglobin)."],["10.2 SPM Mark Points: Heart, Vessels and Blood","10.2 SPM得分点：心脏、血管与血液",[["Q: Describe the pathway of blood from the right atrium to the aorta. [6 marks]","题：描述血液从右心房到主动脉的路径 [6分]"],["P1 Right atrium → through tricuspid valve → right ventricle. P2 Right ventricle → pulmonary artery. P3 Lungs: blood gains oxygen and loses CO₂. P4 Pulmonary vein → left atrium. P5 Through bicuspid valve → left ventricle. P6 Left ventricle contracts → aorta.","P1–P6：右心房→三尖瓣→右心室→肺动脉→肺(换气)→肺静脉→左心房→二尖瓣→左心室→主动脉"],["Q: Explain the adaptations of an artery and a vein. [6 marks]","题：解释动脉与静脉的适应 [6分]"],["Artery — P1 thick muscular wall withstands high pressure; P2 elastic wall recoils to push blood; P3 narrow lumen maintains high pressure. Vein — P4 thin wall; P5 wide lumen lets blood flow with little resistance; P6 valves prevent backflow.","动脉：壁厚耐压、弹性回缩、管腔窄；静脉：壁薄、管腔宽、瓣膜防倒流"],["Q: Explain how a red blood cell is adapted to carry oxygen. [3 marks] P1 biconcave shape → large surface area; P2 no nucleus → more haemoglobin; P3 contains haemoglobin which binds oxygen.","题：红细胞如何适应运氧？[3分] 双凹面积大；无核多血红蛋白；血红蛋白结合氧"]],"","Tip: for 'explain', write the feature AND the reason for each mark."],["10.3 Mechanism of the Heartbeat: The Cardiac Cycle","10.3 心跳机制：心动周期",[["Cardiac muscle is myogenic: it can contract rhythmically without nervous stimulation. One cardiac cycle lasts about 0.8 s at 72 beats per minute.","心肌具自发性；每周期约0.8秒"],["Atrial systole (about 0.1 s): both atria contract; the atrioventricular (AV) valves are open; blood is pushed into the ventricles.","心房收缩：AV瓣开，血入心室"],["Ventricular systole (about 0.3 s): ventricles contract; pressure rises; AV valves close (first heart sound 'lub'); semilunar valves open; blood is forced into the aorta and pulmonary artery.","心室收缩：压力升；AV瓣关；半月瓣开；血入动脉"],["Diastole (about 0.4 s): the whole heart relaxes; semilunar valves close (second heart sound 'dub'); blood flows from the veins into the atria and ventricles.","舒张期：半月瓣关；血从静脉流入心房心室"]],"","Tip: valves open/close because of pressure differences, not because they are controlled by nerves."],["10.3 Mechanism of the Heartbeat: Conduction System","10.3 心跳机制：传导系统",[["1. The sinoatrial (SA) node (pacemaker) in the wall of the right atrium generates electrical impulses.","1. 窦房结(起搏点)产生电冲动"],["2. The impulse spreads over both atria → the atria contract (atrial systole).","2. 冲动扩散至心房→心房收缩"],["3. The impulse reaches the atrioventricular (AV) node; the AV node delays it by about 0.1 s so the atria finish emptying before the ventricles contract.","3. 房室结延迟约0.1秒，使心房排空"],["4. The impulse passes down the bundle of His and the Purkinje fibres to the apex.","4. 经希氏束、浦肯野纤维到心尖"],["5. The ventricles contract from the apex upward, pushing blood out through the arteries.","5. 心室从心尖向上收缩，血被挤出"]],"","Tip: SA node → atria → AV node (delay) → bundle of His → Purkinje fibres → ventricles."],["10.3 Regulation of Heart Rate","10.3 心率的调节",[["The cardiac centre in the medulla oblongata controls heart rate through the autonomic nervous system: the sympathetic nerve (cardiac accelerator) increases the rate; the vagus nerve (parasympathetic) decreases it.","延髓心脏中枢：交感神经加快；迷走神经减慢"],["Adrenaline (from the adrenal glands) increases heart rate and the force of contraction in stress or danger.","肾上腺素使心率与收缩力增加"],["During exercise: muscles respire faster → more CO₂ in the blood → blood pH falls → chemoreceptors detect it → the medulla sends impulses along sympathetic nerves → SA node fires faster → heart rate increases → more blood supplies oxygen and removes CO₂.","运动时：CO₂增多→pH降→化学感受器→延髓→交感神经→窦房结加快→心率增加"],["Blood pressure: about 120/80 mmHg (systolic/diastolic); pulse = the stretching of the artery wall with each ventricular contraction.","血压约120/80 mmHg；脉搏＝心室收缩时动脉壁搏动"]],"","Tip: use the full pathway: stimulus → receptor → centre → effector → response."],["10.3 SPM Mark Points: Heartbeat","10.3 SPM得分点：心跳",[["Q: Explain the mechanism of the heartbeat. [8 marks]","题：解释心跳机制 [8分]"],["P1 Cardiac muscle is myogenic. P2 SA node (pacemaker) in the right atrium sends impulses. P3 Both atria contract. P4 AV node receives the impulse and delays it. P5 Impulse travels along the bundle of His. P6 Then through the Purkinje fibres. P7 Ventricles contract from the apex upward. P8 Blood is pumped into the aorta and pulmonary artery.","P1–P8：自发性→窦房结→心房收缩→房室结延迟→希氏束→浦肯野纤维→心室自心尖收缩→泵血"],["Q: Explain why the heart rate increases during exercise. [5 marks]","题：解释运动时心率为何增加 [5分]"],["P1 Muscles respire faster and produce more CO₂. P2 Blood pH falls. P3 Chemoreceptors/medulla detect the change. P4 Impulses along the sympathetic nerve to the SA node. P5 Heart rate increases to supply more oxygen and remove CO₂ faster.","P1 CO₂增多；P2 pH降；P3 延髓检测；P4 交感神经；P5 心率增加供氧排CO₂"]],"","Tip: put the eight points in the same order as the electrical pathway."],["10.4 Mechanism of Blood Clotting","10.4 凝血机制",[["When a blood vessel is damaged, platelets stick to the wound and release thromboplastin (thrombokinase); damaged tissue also releases it.","血管受损，血小板释放凝血活酶"],["Thromboplastin + calcium ions (Ca²⁺) catalyse the conversion of prothrombin (inactive plasma protein made in the liver with the help of vitamin K) to thrombin (active enzyme).","凝血活酶+Ca²⁺：凝血酶原→凝血酶"],["Thrombin catalyses the conversion of soluble fibrinogen to insoluble fibrin threads.","凝血酶：纤维蛋白原→纤维蛋白"],["Fibrin threads form a mesh that traps blood cells (red cells, platelets) → a blood clot; the clot dries to form a scab and seals the wound.","纤维蛋白网住血细胞形成凝块，干燥成痂"]],"","Tip: remember it as a chain: thromboplastin → thrombin → fibrin."],["10.4 Importance and Disorders of Blood Clotting","10.4 凝血的重要性与相关疾病",[["Importance: prevents excessive blood loss, prevents entry of pathogens, and starts wound healing.","重要性：防失血、防病原体侵入、促进愈合"],["Haemophilia: an inherited X-linked recessive disorder — a clotting factor is missing so blood clots very slowly; patients may bleed severely even from small wounds.","血友病：X连锁隐性遗传，缺凝血因子，凝血很慢"],["Vitamin K deficiency or liver disease reduces prothrombin, so clotting is slow.","缺维生素K或肝病凝血慢"],["Thrombosis: a clot (thrombus) forms inside an unbroken blood vessel (e.g. coronary or brain arteries); it can cause heart attack or stroke. Anticoagulants (heparin, warfarin) reduce clotting.","血栓：血管内形成凝块；抗凝血剂减少凝血"]],"","Tip: do not mix haemophilia (cannot clot) and thrombosis (clots when it should not)."],["10.4 SPM Mark Points: Blood Clotting","10.4 SPM得分点：凝血",[["Q: Explain the mechanism of blood clotting. [6 marks]","题：解释凝血机制 [6分]"],["P1 Damaged tissue/platelets release thromboplastin. P2 Thromboplastin and calcium ions convert prothrombin to thrombin. P3 Thrombin converts soluble fibrinogen to insoluble fibrin. P4 Fibrin threads form a mesh. P5 The mesh traps blood cells. P6 A clot forms and seals the wound.","P1–P6：凝血活酶→凝血酶→纤维蛋白→网→困住血细胞→凝块"],["Q: State the importance of blood clotting. [2 marks] P1 Prevents excessive loss of blood. P2 Prevents entry of pathogens.","题：凝血的重要性 [2分]"],["Q: Why does a haemophiliac bleed for a long time? [2 marks] P1 Lacks a clotting factor. P2 Blood cannot clot quickly.","题：血友病患者为何流血不止？[2分]"]],"","Tip: write the enzymes and substrates (prothrombin/thrombin, fibrinogen/fibrin) exactly."],["10.5 ABO Blood Groups","10.5 ABO血型",[["ABO blood group depends on antigens on the surface of red blood cells and antibodies in the plasma.","血型取决于红细胞表面抗原与血浆抗体"],["Group A: antigen A; antibody anti-B. Group B: antigen B; antibody anti-A. Group AB: antigens A and B; no antibodies. Group O: no antigens; antibodies anti-A and anti-B.","A型：抗原A、抗体anti-B；B型：抗原B、抗体anti-A；AB型：两种抗原无抗体；O型：无抗原、两种抗体"],["Agglutination: if antibodies meet the corresponding antigens, the red blood cells clump together, which can block small blood vessels and be fatal.","凝集：抗体遇相应抗原使红细胞聚集，可阻塞小血管致命"],["Group O is the universal donor (no antigens on the red cells); group AB is the universal recipient (no antibodies in the plasma).","O型万能供血者；AB型万能受血者"]],"","Tip: draw a table of antigens and antibodies for A, B, AB and O."],["10.5 Blood Transfusion and the Rhesus Factor","10.5 输血与Rh因子",[["Compatible transfusions: A receives A or O; B receives B or O; AB receives A, B, AB or O; O receives only O.","可输血：A收A、O；B收B、O；AB收全部；O只收O"],["Blood must be matched (cross-matched) before transfusion to avoid agglutination.","输血前须配血"],["Rhesus (Rh) factor: Rh-positive people have antigen D; Rh-negative people do not. An Rh-negative person must not receive Rh-positive blood repeatedly.","Rh因子：Rh⁺有抗原D；Rh⁻没有"],["Haemolytic disease of the newborn: an Rh-negative mother with an Rh-positive baby makes anti-D antibodies; in the next pregnancy the antibodies cross the placenta and destroy the red cells of an Rh-positive baby. Prevented by an anti-D injection after the first birth.","新生儿溶血病：Rh⁻母亲怀Rh⁺胎儿，二胎抗D抗体破坏红细胞；产后注射抗D预防"]],"","Tip: antibodies are in the recipient's plasma; antigens are on the donor's red cells."],["10.5 SPM Mark Points: Blood Groups","10.5 SPM得分点：血型",[["Q: Explain why a person with blood group A cannot receive blood from group B. [3 marks]","题：为何A型不能接受B型血？[3分]"],["P1 Group A plasma contains anti-B antibodies. P2 Donor group B red cells have antigen B. P3 Anti-B binds antigen B → agglutination (red cells clump and block blood vessels).","P1 A型血浆含anti-B；P2 B型红细胞有抗原B；P3 抗体与抗原结合→凝集"],["Q: Why is group O called the universal donor? [2 marks] P1 Red cells have no antigens A or B. P2 No agglutination occurs when given to any recipient.","题：O型为何是万能供血者？[2分]"],["Q: Explain haemolytic disease of the newborn. [4 marks] P1 Rh-negative mother, Rh-positive baby. P2 Mother's blood forms anti-D antibodies (first pregnancy/birth). P3 In the next pregnancy anti-D crosses the placenta. P4 Destroys the red blood cells of the baby.","题：解释新生儿溶血病 [4分]"]],"","Tip: antigen–antibody pairs are worth marks — always name both."],["10.6 Health Issues: Atherosclerosis and Coronary Heart Disease","10.6 健康问题：动脉粥样硬化与冠心病",[["Atherosclerosis: fatty deposits (cholesterol, plaque) build up on the inner wall of arteries; the wall thickens and loses elasticity; the lumen narrows.","动脉粥样硬化：胆固醇斑块使管壁增厚变硬、管腔变窄"],["Causes: high LDL cholesterol, saturated fat diet, smoking, high blood pressure, obesity, diabetes, lack of exercise, stress, ageing, genetics.","原因：高LDL、饱和脂肪、吸烟、高血压、肥胖、糖尿病、缺乏运动、压力、遗传"],["Coronary heart disease: narrowed or blocked coronary arteries → heart muscle receives too little oxygen → angina (chest pain) or myocardial infarction (heart attack). Stroke: a brain artery is blocked or ruptures.","冠心病：冠状动脉变窄/堵塞→心肌缺氧→心绞痛/心肌梗死；中风：脑动脉堵塞或破裂"],["Hypertension (high blood pressure, above about 140/90 mmHg) damages arteries and strains the heart.","高血压损害动脉并增加心脏负担"]],"","Tip: write the chain: plaque → narrow lumen → less blood → heart muscle lacks oxygen → attack."],["10.6 Health Issues: Anaemia, Leukaemia and Prevention","10.6 健康问题：贫血、白血病与预防",[["Anaemia: too few red blood cells or too little haemoglobin → tiredness, pale skin, breathlessness. Causes: iron deficiency, blood loss, thalassaemia, vitamin B₁₂ deficiency.","贫血：红细胞/血红蛋白不足；缺铁、失血、地中海贫血"],["Leukaemia: cancer of the white blood cells; abnormal white cells are produced in large numbers in the bone marrow. Treatment: chemotherapy, bone marrow/stem cell transplant.","白血病：白细胞癌变；化疗、骨髓/干细胞移植"],["Prevention of circulatory diseases: balanced diet low in saturated fat, cholesterol and salt; regular exercise; avoid smoking and excessive alcohol; manage stress; maintain healthy body mass; regular check-ups.","预防：低脂低盐、运动、戒烟限酒、减压、控制体重、定期检查"],["Blood donation helps patients and keeps the donor's blood cells regenerating.","献血帮助病人"]],"","Tip: for 'suggest measures', give 4 or more specific actions."],["10.6 SPM Mark Points: Circulatory Health Issues","10.6 SPM得分点：循环系统健康问题",[["Q: Explain how atherosclerosis can cause a heart attack. [5 marks]","题：解释动脉粥样硬化如何引起心脏病发作 [5分]"],["P1 Cholesterol/fat deposits form plaque on the artery wall. P2 The lumen of the coronary artery narrows. P3 Less blood/oxygen reaches the heart muscle. P4 A blood clot may block the narrowed artery. P5 Heart muscle cells die from lack of oxygen → heart attack.","P1 斑块；P2 管腔变窄；P3 心肌缺氧；P4 血栓堵塞；P5 心肌细胞死亡"],["Q: Suggest four ways to reduce the risk of coronary heart disease. [4 marks] P1 Reduce saturated fat/cholesterol intake. P2 Exercise regularly. P3 Do not smoke. P4 Control blood pressure/stress/body mass.","题：降低冠心病风险的四种方法 [4分]"]],"","Tip: do not repeat the same idea in different words — each mark needs a new point."],["10.7 Tissue Fluid and Lymph Formation","10.7 组织液与淋巴的形成",[["At the arterial end of a capillary, the hydrostatic pressure of blood is higher than the osmotic pressure of the plasma proteins → plasma (without red cells and large proteins) is forced out into the tissue spaces → tissue fluid.","动脉端：静水压高于血浆蛋白渗透压→血浆被压出形成组织液"],["Tissue fluid bathes the cells: it supplies oxygen and nutrients and collects CO₂ and wastes by diffusion.","组织液供给氧与养料，收集CO₂与废物"],["At the venous end, the hydrostatic pressure is lower and the osmotic pressure of plasma proteins draws most of the fluid back into the capillary by osmosis.","静脉端：静水压低，蛋白渗透压使大部分液体回血管"],["The remaining tissue fluid (about 10%) enters the blind-ended lymph capillaries → lymph. Lymph flows through lymph vessels (with valves) and lymph nodes and returns to the blood near the heart (subclavian veins).","其余约10%进入淋巴管成为淋巴，经淋巴结，最后汇入锁骨下静脉"]],"","Tip: describe both ends of the capillary — arterial and venous."],["10.7 Lymphatic System: Structure and Functions","10.7 淋巴系统：结构与功能",[["Lymph vessels have thin walls and valves; lymph is moved by contraction of skeletal muscles and breathing movements, not by the heart.","淋巴管壁薄有瓣；靠骨骼肌与呼吸运动推动"],["Lymph nodes contain lymphocytes and phagocytes (macrophages) that destroy pathogens and filter lymph.","淋巴结含淋巴细胞和吞噬细胞，滤过并消灭病原体"],["Functions: (1) returns excess tissue fluid to the blood and prevents oedema (swelling); (2) defence against infection; (3) absorbs and transports fats from the lacteals of the small intestine.","功能：回收组织液防水肿；防御感染；运输脂肪"],["Compared with blood plasma, lymph has less protein and no red blood cells, but contains many lymphocytes.","与血浆比，淋巴蛋白少、无红细胞、淋巴细胞多"]],"","Tip: oedema = accumulation of tissue fluid; the lymphatic system prevents it."],["10.7 SPM Mark Points: Tissue Fluid and Lymphatic System","10.7 SPM得分点：组织液与淋巴系统",[["Q: Explain how tissue fluid is formed and how it returns to the blood. [6 marks]","题：解释组织液如何形成并回流 [6分]"],["P1 At the arterial end hydrostatic pressure is high. P2 Plasma (without large proteins and cells) is forced out of the capillary. P3 This forms tissue fluid. P4 At the venous end the osmotic pressure of plasma proteins is higher than the hydrostatic pressure. P5 Water returns to the capillary by osmosis. P6 Excess tissue fluid enters lymph capillaries and flows back to the blood.","P1–P6：动脉端高压→血浆压出→组织液→静脉端渗透压高→渗透回血管→多余入淋巴管回血"],["Q: State three functions of the lymphatic system. [3 marks] P1 Returns tissue fluid to blood. P2 Lymph nodes destroy pathogens. P3 Transports fats absorbed from the intestine.","题：淋巴系统三功能 [3分]"]],"","Tip: use the words hydrostatic pressure and osmotic pressure."],["10.8 Health Issues of the Lymphatic System","10.8 淋巴系统的健康问题",[["Lymphoedema: swelling (usually of a limb) when lymph vessels are blocked or removed (surgery, radiotherapy) so tissue fluid accumulates.","淋巴水肿：淋巴管阻塞，组织液积聚"],["Filariasis (elephantiasis): caused by the parasitic worm Wuchereria bancrofti transmitted by mosquito bites; adult worms block lymph vessels → severe swelling of legs, arms and genitals.","丝虫病：丝虫经蚊传播阻塞淋巴管，肢体严重肿胀"],["Lymphoma: cancer of lymphocytes in the lymph nodes; swollen painless lymph nodes. Swollen lymph nodes in infections are a sign that lymphocytes are fighting pathogens.","淋巴瘤：淋巴细胞癌；淋巴结肿大"],["Prevention of filariasis: control mosquitoes (remove stagnant water), use repellent and bed nets, mass drug treatment of infected people.","预防丝虫病：灭蚊、驱蚊、蚊帐、药物治疗"]],"","Tip: give the cause, how it affects the lymph vessels and one preventive step."],["10.8 SPM Mark Points: Lymphatic Health Issues","10.8 SPM得分点：淋巴系统健康问题",[["Q: Explain how filariasis causes swelling of the legs. [3 marks]","题：解释丝虫病如何使腿肿胀 [3分]"],["P1 Filarial worms live in the lymph vessels. P2 They block the flow of lymph. P3 Tissue fluid accumulates in the tissues and causes swelling.","P1 丝虫寄居淋巴管；P2 阻塞淋巴流动；P3 组织液积聚肿胀"],["Q: Suggest two ways to prevent filariasis. [2 marks] P1 Destroy mosquito breeding places. P2 Use mosquito nets/repellents.","题：预防丝虫病两法 [2分]"]],"","Tip: link the vessel blockage to the accumulation of tissue fluid."],["10 SPM-Style Structured Question with Mark Scheme","第10章 SPM结构题与评分",[["Q1 (a) Name the blood vessel that carries blood from the lungs to the heart. [1] → Pulmonary vein (1).","Q1(a) 肺到心的血管：肺静脉"],["Q1 (b) State two differences between the walls of an artery and a vein. [2] → Artery wall is thicker and more elastic (1); vein wall is thinner (1).","Q1(b) 动脉壁更厚更有弹性；静脉壁薄"],["Q1 (c) Explain why the left ventricle has a thicker wall than the right ventricle. [3] → The left ventricle pumps blood to the whole body (1) which is far (1); it needs a higher pressure (1) while the right ventricle pumps only to the lungs.","Q1(c) 左心室泵至全身，需高压"],["Q1 (d) Explain how the SA node is involved in controlling heartbeat. [3] → SA node is the pacemaker (1) sends impulses (1) causing atria to contract (1).","Q1(d) 窦房结起搏、发冲动、使心房收缩"]],"","Tip: marks in square brackets show how many points to write."],["10 SPM-Style Essay with Mark Scheme (20 marks)","第10章 SPM论述题与评分(20分)",[["Q: (a) Explain the mechanism of blood clotting. [6] (b) Explain the importance of the double circulation in humans. [4] (c) A person has high blood pressure and a high cholesterol level. Explain how this person can develop coronary heart disease, and suggest ways to reduce the risk. [10]","题：(a)凝血机制[6]；(b)双循环重要性[4]；(c)高血压高胆固醇与冠心病及预防[10]"],["(a) Use the six clotting points from 10.4 (thromboplastin, calcium, prothrombin→thrombin, fibrinogen→fibrin, mesh, clot).","(a) 用10.4的六个得分点"],["(b) P1 Blood passes through the heart twice. P2 Blood regains pressure after the lungs. P3 Delivers oxygen faster. P4 Keeps oxygenated and deoxygenated blood separate. P5 Supports high metabolic rate.","(b) 5点任写4"],["(c) Explanation (up to 6): high cholesterol/LDL → plaque → narrowed lumen → higher blood pressure → less blood to heart muscle → clot blocks artery → heart attack. Suggestions (up to 4): low-fat/low-salt diet, exercise, no smoking, control stress/weight, medication and check-ups.","(c) 解释最多6分；建议最多4分"]],"","Tip: label each part (a)(b)(c) and count your points against the marks."],["Key Terms (English – Bahasa Melayu)","重点术语（英文–马来文）",[["Circulatory system (Sistem peredaran); Artery (Arteri); Vein (Vena); Capillary (Kapilari)","循环系统；动脉；静脉；毛细血管"],["Atrium (Atrium); Ventricle (Ventrikel); Valve (Injap); Pacemaker (Perentak jantung)","心房；心室；瓣膜；起搏点"],["Blood clotting (Pembekuan darah); Platelet (Platelet); Fibrinogen (Fibrinogen); Antibody (Antibodi)","凝血；血小板；纤维蛋白原；抗体"],["Lymph (Limfa); Tissue fluid (Bendalir tisu); Blood group (Kumpulan darah); Agglutination (Aglutinasi)","淋巴；组织液；血型；凝集"]],"","Tip: 'vena' = vein."],["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips","常见错误与考试提示",[["Saying arteries always carry oxygenated blood — the pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood.","动脉不一定含氧：肺动脉含缺氧血"],["Mixing up prothrombin/thrombin and fibrinogen/fibrin in the clotting sequence.","混淆凝血各物质"],["Group O has no antigens but both antibodies; AB has both antigens and no antibodies.","O型无抗原有两抗体；AB型相反"],["Forgetting the AV node delay in the heartbeat mechanism.","漏写房室结延迟"],["Writing 'high pressure' for tissue fluid formation without saying 'hydrostatic' and where (arterial end).","写“高压”却没说静水压与动脉端"]],"","Tip: for sequences (heartbeat, clotting, blood flow) use numbered points."],["Uji Diri","自测",[["S: Which chamber has the thickest wall? Why? J: Left ventricle; it pumps blood at high pressure to the whole body.","问：哪个腔壁最厚？为何？答：左心室，把血以高压送往全身"],["S: Name the pacemaker of the heart. J: The sinoatrial (SA) node.","问：心脏起搏点？答：窦房结"],["S: What is the role of fibrin in blood clotting? J: Forms a mesh of insoluble threads that traps blood cells to form a clot.","问：纤维蛋白作用？答：形成网状不溶丝，网住血细胞形成凝块"],["S: Why can group O donate to others? J: Red blood cells have no antigens A or B, so no agglutination occurs.","问：O型为何可供血给他人？答：红细胞无A、B抗原，不凝集"],["S: Give two functions of the lymphatic system. J: Returns tissue fluid to the blood; destroys pathogens in the lymph nodes; transports fats.","问：淋巴系统两功能？答：回收组织液；淋巴结防御；运输脂肪"],["S: How does the AV node help the heart? J: It delays the impulse so the atria finish contracting before the ventricles contract.","问：房室结作用？答：延迟冲动，使心房先排空再收缩心室"]],"",""]]};
const PPTS_INS={"bio|T4-1":[9,[["SPM Biology (4551): Paper Format","SPM生物(4551)：试卷格式",[["Paper 1 (4551/1): 40 objective questions = 40 marks; answer all.","试卷1：40道选择题＝40分"],["Paper 2 (4551/2) = 100 marks: Section A — 8 structured questions, 60 marks, answer all (about 7.5 marks each on average); Section B — 2 essay questions, 20 marks, answer ONE; Section C — 1 question, 20 marks (compulsory).","试卷2共100分：A部分8题结构题60分(全答)；B部分2题20分(选1)；C部分1题20分"],["Paper 3 (4551/3): 15 marks (practical / experimental skills).","试卷3：15分（实验技能）"],["Content: the KSSM DSKP content and learning standards of Form 4 and Form 5, so every sub-chapter can be examined.","内容范围：KSSM DSKP的中四中五全部标准，每个小章节都可能考"],["A 20-mark question can come from any chapter, so each sub-chapter must be studied deeply enough to give 10–20 correct points.","20分的题可能来自任何章节，每个小章节都要准备到能写出10–20个得分点"]],"","Tip: format from the Pandai KSSM SPM-preparation page; check the latest official format document from Lembaga Peperiksaan."],["How Marks Are Awarded: 1 Point = 1 Mark","评分方式：一点＝一分",[["SPM marks are given for correct key points (keywords) and their explanations; usually a keyword/point gets 1 mark and an explanation gets 1 mark.","评分按得分点：关键词1分，解释1分"],["Example: for a 6-mark question, write about 3 keywords and 3 explanations (or 6 separate points).","例：6分题写约3个关键词+3个解释（或6个独立点）"],["Use the correct scientific terms: marks are lost for vague words (e.g. 'pressure' instead of 'hydrostatic pressure').","用准确术语：含糊用词会丢分"],["Write one idea per point; repeating the same idea in different words earns only one mark.","一点一个意思；重复说法只得一分"],["Numerical answers need the formula/working and the correct unit.","计算要有公式、步骤和单位"]],"","Tip: marks in brackets [ ] = the number of different points you must write."],["Command Words and Answer Techniques","指示词与答题技巧",[["State / Name / Label (Nyatakan / Namakan / Labelkan): short fact; 1 point = 1 mark.","列出/命名/标示：简短事实，1点1分"],["Explain (Terangkan / Jelaskan): give the point AND the reason ('because…', 'so that…'). Describe (Huraikan): give the details in sequence of what happens.","解释：写要点+原因；描述：按顺序写出经过"],["Compare (Bandingkan): similarity and difference in pairs, with both sides stated (use a table). Suggest (Cadangkan): apply knowledge to a new situation.","比较：成对写相同点/不同点，两边都要写；建议：应用知识"],["Justify (Justifikasi): give a statement and a reason. Calculate (Hitung): formula, substitution, answer with unit.","辩解：陈述+理由；计算：公式、代入、答案带单位"],["Plan: (1) read the question and the marks, (2) underline the command word, (3) list the points, (4) write in a logical order.","步骤：看分数→圈指示词→列要点→按顺序写"]],"","Tip: these are common teaching conventions, not an official definition list."],["Study Standard: Points Needed per Sub-Chapter","学习标准：每个小章节需要多少得分点",[["Define / state: 1–2 points. Explain a short process: 3–4 points.","定义/列举1–2点；短过程3–4点"],["Describe a mechanism or pathway (e.g. heartbeat, clotting, urine formation): 6–8 points.","机制/路径(心跳、凝血、尿的形成)：6–8点"],["Compare two items: 3–4 pairs (6–8 points). Experiments: variables, apparatus, steps, results, conclusion.","比较：3–4对；实验：变量、仪器、步骤、结果、结论"],["A 10-mark essay part needs at least 10–12 points; keep a few spare points in case some are not accepted.","10分论述要备10–12点，多备几点以防不被接受"],["Self-check for every sub-chapter: Can I write 10 correct points? If not, revise that sub-chapter.","自测：每个小章节能否写出10个正确得分点？不能就重温"]],"","Tip: this is a study guideline based on the 1-point-1-mark rule and the paper format, not an official quota."]]]};
